{
    "bug_id": 1021,
    "summary": "[html.css] Widgets should use CSS2 system colors (and fonts)",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "The default background colors for most widgets except buttons are very dark. It\nwould be nice if the widget library could set them to reasonable defaults and\npossibly even get the settings from the operating system.\n\nThis can be tested by uncommenting the code in\nforms\\nsFormControlFrame::SetColors and switching to Standard mode in the\nviewer upon viewing test8.",
            "creator": "karnaze@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1998-10-08T01:37:24Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Last I heard, peterl was hooking up CSS2 System Colors, which would let you set\nthe colors for these correctly in ua.css in a way that's consistent with the OS.",
            "creator": "angus@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1998-11-08T08:02:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Setting all current Open/Normal to M4.",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-02-03T16:09:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "per leger, assigning QA contacts to all open bugs without QA contacts according\nto list at http://bugzilla.mozilla.org/describecomponents.cgi?product=Browser",
            "creator": "paulmac@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-03-06T07:42:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Peter I'm assigning this bug to you. You can assign it back to me when the CSS2\nSystem color property values are available.",
            "creator": "kmcclusk@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-05-05T21:53:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Moving all Widget Set bugs, past and present, to new HTML Form Controls\ncomponent per request from karnaze.  Widget Set component will be retired\nshortly.",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-22T00:46:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "CSS system colors in place, now needs nsILookAndFeel support.",
            "creator": "peterl-retired@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-10T06:14:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Peter, This is what I sent you mail on a few days ago. This now works on Windows\nand needs to be implemented on Mac and GTK.",
            "creator": "rods@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-14T20:51:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "reassigning to pavlov to do on linux, cc'ing pink to implement on Mac. Please\nleave this bug open until it is done on both",
            "creator": "trudelle@acm.org",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-14T23:40:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "done on linux, reassigning to pink for mac work",
            "creator": "pavlov@pavlov.net",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-17T08:11:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "accepting",
            "creator": "mikepinkerton@mac.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-12T20:32:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "first stab checked in. i will open a new bug to get the colors correct via\nappearance manager.",
            "creator": "mikepinkerton@mac.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-13T00:08:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Just happened to look at this bug. Just wanted to note that the status probably\nshould be \"resolved\" instead of \"new\"? At least the combination of \"new\" and\n\"fixed\" is strange.",
            "creator": "benjamin-bugzilla@pflugmann.de",
            "timestamp": "1999-11-29T05:44:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "changed to M14",
            "creator": "rods@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-11-30T16:51:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "this is a test\n",
            "creator": "rods@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-28T18:32:53Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "changing to M15",
            "creator": "rods@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-28T22:03:09Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This bug is similar to bug 16729.\nReassigned to ben.\nCCd Sherry Wang <xiaotong@us.ibm.com> who volunteered to do the work.\n",
            "creator": "pierre@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-03-27T19:54:18Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Really reassigning to ben.\n",
            "creator": "pierre@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-03-27T19:54:49Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 22620 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "bugs@bengoodger.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-03T11:22:24Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Move to M16 for now ...\n",
            "creator": "don@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-05T20:37:14Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "non-essential skin work. shifting off. ",
            "creator": "bugs@bengoodger.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-30T02:31:27Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Remark: one of the things on our plate is a 4.x classic theme, that will attempt \n\nto take advantage of system colors and fonts like 4.x did. There is a variety of \n\nbugs on all three system properties that can be used in CSS2 (colors, fonts and \n\nthe third one escapes me...) so its coming. Varying or user set often do not work \n\nwell with design skins with the author will create and rely on certain color \n\ncombination, thus the advice is (see also\" Cascading Style Sheets\" by Bos/Li, \n\nAdison-Wesley) to either do a fully systm compliant design or to do a fully \n\ncustom designed one, but to not mix from either.\n\n",
            "creator": "german@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-05-01T04:32:02Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Basics appear to be in place on Linux and Windows; changing platform, OS to Mac.",
            "creator": "braden@endoframe.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-06-28T05:19:30Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Based on comments, the CSS system colours code is in, and now we just need to\nchange html.css. Luckily enough, that is exactly what I am doing now.\n\nTaking bug. This will not fully work on the mac until bug 1004 is fixed.",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-23T00:13:21Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "almost done",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-30T00:59:52Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "PDT believes that enough of this feature is implemented to make classic skin\nwork, and we're therefore marking this bug nsbeta3-. ",
            "creator": "phil@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-09-07T00:54:15Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This has nothing to do with classic skin. This is an html.css fix which I have\nalmost completed (I am merely waiting for the CSS pseudos renaming to finish).\nReinstating [nsbeta3+] per Eric Krock's request that I plus all bugs that I \nwould have time to do by the nsbeta3 deadline.",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "2000-09-07T01:08:51Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "per PDT team.  At this time, PDT marking priority to P5.  If you believe this to\nbe a P1 priority, please let us know how this fits into the P1 criteria.\n\nBug was marked nsbeta3- by PDT team earlier.  We are sorry to see that it be\nsuggested by ekrock for this to be a nsbeta3 merely due to having time to fix.\nNormally, if a person doesn't have any more nsbeta3+ bugs to fix, s/he should\nhelp out the team with other nsbeta3+ bugs. Thanks.\n",
            "creator": "lchiang@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-09-13T21:01:13Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Since I'm getting lectured by the PDT team in print here ;-> ... for the record, \nto clarify, I have never given anyone a blanket instruction to \"nsbeta3+ all \nbugs they have time to fix, irrespective of severity.\" Rather, during the \nnsbeta3 timeframe, authority to + or - bugs was passed down to the first-line \nengineers and their managers. During triage, I noticed that dbaron and ianh had \nopen nsbeta3 nominees whose status had not been assigned, so, per PDT team \ninstructions to resolve the status of outstanding nsbeta3 nominees that had not \nbeen nominated, I asked them (just like the other first-line engineers) to \nindicate which bugs currently assigned to them they were going to fix by the \nnsbeta3 deadline, and to minus or reassign the others, so their status would be \nresolved. This is what Ian was referring to. Let's not convict the innocent on \nterse hearsay please ... ;->",
            "creator": "ekrock@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-09-14T17:03:54Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "While we're at it, I should possibly point out that since I'm a QA person doing\nthis in addition to all the other QA work, and that I don't know C++, there is\nno way I could have \"helped out the team with other nsbeta3+ bugs\".\n\nThis is effectively a free fix, guys! Quit complaining! :-)",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "2000-09-16T08:20:01Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Ian, there isn't free work late in a product cycle.  Perceived risk becomes a \ndominant factor.  That's what's going on here with pdt intervention.  Not \nresetting priority, for once, PDT weighed in earlier on its assessment.",
            "creator": "clayton@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-09-20T00:07:26Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 53483 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "pierre@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-09-21T03:33:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "marking fixed because i think ian's *.css changes fixed this...please do reopen \nif I'm mistaken.",
            "creator": "bugzilla@blakeross.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-09-22T03:18:20Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "blake: You should never set the resolution to FIXED unless _you fixed it_.\n\nFIXED. Please verify by checking on at least five platforms as this is a very\nplatform-sensitive change.",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "2000-09-22T05:22:12Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "cc: gerardok.  ckritzer is on sabbatical and can't verify this bug.  We should \nget this verified soon, if possible.",
            "creator": "lchiang@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-09-26T06:29:54Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Updating QA contact.",
            "creator": "bsharma@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-09-27T01:03:25Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Build: 2000092711 MN6\nPlatform: WinNT\n\nVerified by loading the test8 file under sample directory.",
            "creator": "bsharma@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-09-28T21:45:09Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "reopening and remarking fixed (and spamming people who will hate me forever in \nthe process).\n\nPlease read Ian's comment:\n\"Please verify by checking on at least five platforms as this is a very\nplatform-sensitive change.\"",
            "creator": "bugzilla@blakeross.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-09-28T21:55:44Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "..and remarking fixed!\n\n(please direct spam complaints to nobody@mozilla.org, my secretary)",
            "creator": "bugzilla@blakeross.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-09-28T21:57:16Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "[Thanks Blake.]\n\nTo check this you need to:\n  1. Change your system font\n  2. Change your system colours\n  3. Check that widgets in Mozilla are using these new settings \n  4. Repeat this for edge cases\nThis needs to be done, as I said, on at least five platforms since this issue\nis known to have so many hidden dependencies and is very OS sensitive.\n\nThings to look out for: Are the inset/outset borders on radio buttons correct?\nIs the page background correct? Are text fields getting the correct background\ncolour? Are fonts the right size, not too big and not smaller than the OS?",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "2000-09-28T22:42:16Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "asa - can we get some folks on mozilla.org to help verify this also?  It sounds \nlike the changes are fairly sensitive and there may be hidden problems waiting \nto be uncovered.",
            "creator": "lchiang@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-10-01T06:59:11Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Verifying Win 98 build 2001-02-06-04-Mtest\nLinux RedHat build 2001-02-06-08-Mtest\nand MacOS 8.x build 2001-02-06-08-Mtest",
            "creator": "vladimire@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2001-02-12T01:45:23Z"
        }
    ]
}

{
    "bug_id": 4722,
    "summary": "[FEATURE] Cut, copy, paste, & select all in URL entry",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "Apprunner, Mac. URL bar issues:\n1. Type a URL. You have to hit return twice before it loads\n2. Cannot copy & paste in URL bar\n3. URL bar does not update to show URL of current page.",
            "creator": "sfraser_bugs@smfr.org",
            "timestamp": "1999-04-07T23:20:23Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Re-assinged to radha@netscape.com, set target milestone to M5, changed component\nto XPApps, priority to P2, platform and OS to All, and changed summary line.\n\nRadha, copy and paste actually work on Windows via the keyboard equivalents\nonly, i.e. the menu commands are not hooked up.\n\n----------\n\nSimon,\n\n1. Type a URL. You have to hit return twice before it loads -- this is a\nduplicate of bug #4544 that Radha is working on now.\n\n3. URL bar does not update to show URL of current page. -- this is a duplicate\nof bugs #4054 and #4071.",
            "creator": "don@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-04-07T23:57:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 4857 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "don@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-04-09T17:26:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 4859 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "don@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-04-09T18:45:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "[QA Assigning to self.]",
            "creator": "elig@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-04-20T22:50:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "updating title to show part 3.   that the only thing not working now, right?",
            "creator": "chofmann@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-04-26T22:38:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Changed title again. It is the second part that is not working . Rest have been\nfixed.",
            "creator": "radha@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-04-26T23:26:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 6516 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "don@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-05-17T23:59:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 7663 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-07T16:44:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 7691 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-07T19:20:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Move this out to M8 when Radha will be working on the URL bar.",
            "creator": "don@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-08T22:02:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "BTW, copy and paste actually work on Windows and Linux after a fashion.  The\nmenu commands don't work, but the keyboard equivalents work on Windows and the\nmiddle button mouse shortcut works on Linux.",
            "creator": "don@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-08T22:06:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Marking as FEATURE. To be newly implemented..",
            "creator": "radha@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-28T19:21:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "There is more work to this than hooking up menu items. First, the cut & paste\nfeatures are not there. There is some code for copy. To cut,copy & paste in the\nright way,  we need to figure  who has the focus and the last drag, the content\narea or url bar or a text field inside content area etc... Based on who had the\nlast mouse drag, the appropriate hooking up to either nsIPresShell or the text\nwidget needs to be done. Once all this is done, the menu options should be\nhooked.  I don't see all this happening in the near future. Moving to M10.\ncc'ing mcafee for more input.",
            "creator": "radha@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-07T19:33:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "There is more work to this than hooking up menu items. First, the cut & paste\nfeatures are not there. There is some code for copy. To cut,copy & paste in the\nright way,  we need to figure  who has the focus and the last drag, the content\narea or url bar or a text field inside content area etc... Based on who had the\nlast mouse drag, the appropriate hooking up to either nsIPresShell or the text\nwidget needs to be done. Once all this is done, the menu options should be\nhooked.  I don't see all this happening in the near future. Moving to M10.\ncc'ing mcafee for more input.",
            "creator": "radha@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-07T19:34:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Radha, are there some known \"feature\" bugs by toolkit folks that this should be\ndependent upon?",
            "creator": "don@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-13T19:35:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "depends on 12022.",
            "creator": "radha@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-18T06:52:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "The deal is, For the content area only the copy operation is permitted. For the\nurlbar and any text form element, cut, copy and paste are allowed. Which\nexplains why presentation shell has only copy operation. For the urlbar I\nbelieve we will go thro' ender once the gfx switch is flipped. What about the\nform elements. Can some one answer?\n\nBrowser needs to know when something is selected. So that it can decide whether\nto  enable only the copy menuitem (if selection is in the content area) or cut\ncopy and paste menu items if the selection is in a text field. How can I get\nthat info?",
            "creator": "radha@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-18T18:27:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 4663 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "radha@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-18T18:28:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "How much XPToolkit support do we need to implement this?",
            "creator": "don@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-28T00:18:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This depends on the gfx text widget's clipboard APIs it is not sure at this time\nif those are in place.",
            "creator": "radha@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-30T22:32:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "you can find out if something is selected in the URL bar (or any gfx text\ncontrol) by  adding a listener on the onSelect notification from the gfx text\ncontrol.",
            "creator": "buster@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-09T23:47:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I get notifications on select event. But I need a way to get to the text widget\nfrom DOMNode. I think there is already  a bug against buster for that.",
            "creator": "radha@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-17T20:01:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "12022 is going to get fixed in M12. So will this be.",
            "creator": "radha@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-17T22:10:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "we're unblocked here now, radha's on vacation, back ? 2nd week of december?",
            "creator": "mcafee@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-03T16:33:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Chris, can you own this for beta?",
            "creator": "don@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-20T22:52:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Hmmm ... why is this bug re-assinging? ...",
            "creator": "don@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-20T23:24:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I have some changes for this in my tree and having some problems. I'll keep\nposted. Let it stay in my palte for now, so that I can keep track...",
            "creator": "radha@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-20T23:51:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Re-summarized.",
            "creator": "don@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-23T05:13:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 22776 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "alan-lists@ajsquared.us",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-05T01:07:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 23294 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "sidr@albedo.net",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-09T03:08:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "[note to self: be sure to verify dupes of this bug while verifying it.]",
            "creator": "elig@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-10T22:47:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Chris, this is waiting for some M13 work from Hyatt.",
            "creator": "don@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-14T01:04:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Moving to M14 ...",
            "creator": "don@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-19T02:02:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "buster: why is this dependent on 20471?  I don't see that bug mentioned here.\nMarking dependant on saari's focus bug, 14026.",
            "creator": "mcafee@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-19T02:30:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This bug is not strictly dependent on 20471, in the sense that no progress can\nbe made on this bug until 20471 is fixed.  However, the fix for this bug won't\nwork right from the user's perspective until 20471 is also fixed.  They can be\nfixed in parallel.\n\nAs you fix this bug, you'll want to test it.  So you'll make edits to the URL\nbar, but the commands won't be updated automatically as they should.  Instead,\nyou'll have to point focus elsewhere (like the tree control in the sidebar, for\nexample), then back to the URL bar to get the URL bar to update it's commands.\n\nQA would have a hard time marking this bug verified until 20471 is fixed,\nbecause commands won't be enabled/disabled at the expected times.",
            "creator": "buster@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-19T02:53:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 25529 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "asa@piercedotzler.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-29T00:29:26Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "don will track this.\n",
            "creator": "mcafee@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-02-03T00:04:46Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Nominating as \"beta1\" blocker.\n",
            "creator": "don@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-02-03T04:36:36Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "OK, this is fixed.\n",
            "creator": "don@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-02-16T07:50:17Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This definitely works using the 2.17.00 build. \n\nAfter checking this bug (and nearly all bugs marked as duplicate of this bug) on \nall 3 primary platforms, I'm Verifying.\n\nThere are several side-issues:\n\t* You can copy via keyboard shortcut when the menu item is disabled\n\t* If you paste text on Windows into a text field until you exceed the right \n(or bottom) edge of the text field, the text field won't scroll to display the \ntext you're entering. Of course, if you exceed the edge through typing, it will.\n\nWill see if bugs exist for both of these, and if not, will submit them.\n",
            "creator": "elig@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-02-18T00:40:38Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Verified fixed.\n\n\t- first side-issue noted by trudelle to be an existing bug; bug number \nunknown.\n\t- second side-issue now contained in bug #28317.\n",
            "creator": "elig@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-02-18T01:15:31Z"
        }
    ]
}

{
    "bug_id": 6117,
    "summary": "[FEATURE] Append CCK's custom string to browser's user agent string",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "We want to be able to append the \"Company Identifier\" string that the CCK user\nenters in the CCK Wizard to the browser's user agent string. Not sure what\nComponent category this bug belongs to, so I just took a guess.",
            "creator": "robinf@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-05-07T22:32:20Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** This bug has been marked as a duplicate of 806 ***",
            "creator": "selmer@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-05-17T18:23:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Verified Dup...see Bug 806 comments",
            "creator": "jaymoz@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-08T17:44:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I don't believe this was appropriate to dup to 806 since the fix for 806 didn't\ninclude this feature.\n\nIn 4.x (according to the old winfe/nsapp.cpp) we keyed off the existence of a\nconfiguration pref called \"user_agent\" and when it existed we would add\nC-<user_agent_prev_value> to the user agent string.  See the routine\nResolveAppVersion for the exact code.\n\nThere appear to be other places where this logic existed since winfe/custom.cpp\ndid something almost but not quite identical.",
            "creator": "selmer@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-08T23:45:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Don, I'm sending this back to you with the info on how we did this in 4.x.",
            "creator": "selmer@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-08T23:46:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Clearing Duplicate resolution due to ReOpen of this bug.",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-19T17:21:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Move to M10 until I can figure out when we can do this ...",
            "creator": "don@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-19T18:25:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Move to M15.  Not a beta 1 requirement.",
            "creator": "don@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-22T01:53:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "The mighty user agent service will slay this foul beast!\n\n\n\nThe pref in question is just \"user_agent\"?\n\n\n\n",
            "creator": "mike.shaver@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-20T22:52:41Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Do we have to fix this for M14?\n",
            "creator": "don@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-02-03T04:37:45Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "CC:'ing Bijal so he can answer Don's question. Is this a Beta 1 feature for CCK?",
            "creator": "robinf@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-02-03T17:55:04Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This is a beta 2 feature, especially since netscape.cfg is a beta 2 feature for \nSeamonkey.",
            "creator": "bijals@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-02-03T18:21:21Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Adding to CCK tracking bug.",
            "creator": "selmer@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-03-01T21:28:31Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 20941 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "selmer@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-03-01T21:33:38Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Don, it may be that this should be assigned to shaver.  I just marked 20941 as a \ndup of this because this one is older.  20941 was assigned to shaver and we had \nworked out how this was to be implemented.  Adding shaver to the cc list.",
            "creator": "selmer@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-03-01T21:36:29Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Move to M16 ...\n",
            "creator": "don@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-06T21:11:11Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "M17 for mcafee ...\n",
            "creator": "don@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-05-12T06:10:38Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Putting on [nsbeta2+][5/16] radar.  This is a feature MUST complete work by \n05/16 or we may pull this feature for PR2.",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-05-12T19:04:18Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I have no idea what this bug is about.  Can someone shed some light here?\n",
            "creator": "mcafee@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-05-16T07:01:00Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This bug will give a better understanding of the problem. A pref is\n needed so that the user agent string gets the \"C-\" tag inserted and\n then the value of the pref gets added as well -> in the form of\n Netscape 5.0 [en] C- <foo>.We can choose to have a different tag for\n mozilla say \"M-\". The length of this value can be limited to say 10\n extra characters or so.\nAdding myself to CC.",
            "creator": "vparthas@netscape.net",
            "timestamp": "2000-05-16T19:28:16Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Move to M19 target milestone.\n",
            "creator": "don@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-05-26T00:37:40Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Don, this bug is a requirement for CCK's PR2 features.  PDT marked the bug \nnsbeta2+ so we are expecting this to be fixed.  Is there a change in the plans?",
            "creator": "bijals@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-05-30T16:25:04Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Putting on [nsbeta2-] radar. Removing [5/16]. Will do for nsbeta3",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-05-31T01:26:26Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "user-agent, gagan\n",
            "creator": "mcafee@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-06-21T22:58:06Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I think valeski added the code for customizing the user-agent. So it might just \nbe him explaining how to do it. ",
            "creator": "gagan@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-06-21T23:01:52Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "use this attribte, \nhttp://lxr.mozilla.org/seamonkey/source/netwerk/protocol/http/public/nsIHTTPProt\nocolHandler.idl#152. First *get* the attribute, append your string to it, then \nset the whole string back in using that attribute.",
            "creator": "jud@me.dium.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-06-21T23:13:26Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Re-opening bug.\nWe need a pref to do this change.",
            "creator": "vparthas@netscape.net",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-24T22:30:20Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Reassigning to XPapps to implement a preference that will customize the user \nagent string.",
            "creator": "vparthas@netscape.net",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-24T22:31:26Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This is an extremely critical bug/feature for N6 Client Customization Kit.  The \nmost basic customization is appending to the user agent string already in the \nbrowser.  CCK tool tags anyone who uses CCK to customize the browser with \n\"-CCK\".  Distributors can also add their own tag to the user agent string.  This \ntagged user agent string is used to measure indirect revenue from distributors.\n\nBill Law and I talked about this and we could easily append the CCK string to \nthe vendor portion. \n\nIn Communicator 4.x and CCK 4.x, the following javascript is in the netscape.cfg \nfor the user agent string append command:\n\nwith (PrefConfig) {\nconfig(\"user_agent\", \"CCK-MCD bij's browser\");\n}\n",
            "creator": "bijals@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-24T23:13:13Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Putting on [nsbeta2-] since PR2 is outta here.",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-24T23:34:14Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Does:\nwith (PrefConfig) {\nconfig(\"user_agent\", \"CCK-MCD bij's browser\");\n}\nput an entry in prefs.js or somewhere else (e.g., netscape.cfg or equivalent)?\n\nI guess what I need to know is how to get this value *out* (from wherever it \ngoes).",
            "creator": "law@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-25T01:28:57Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Not sure it puts a value at all.  Basically, the code I supplied is in the\nnetscape.cfg which is a hashed preference file in Communicator.  Everytime you\nlaunch Communicator, this file is read and it appends to the user agent string\ndynamically.  Therefore, this javascript does not change the actual user agent\nstring in Communicator code.",
            "creator": "bijals@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-25T01:47:34Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "OK, I think I've found what I need.  The 4.x code calls PREF_CopyConfigString\nto get this customized user agent string.  I'll use the same API (it's in the \n6.0 version of prefapi).\n\nYo, Varada; does that sound right? ",
            "creator": "law@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-25T02:22:28Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "with (PrefConfig) {\nconfig(\"user_agent\", \"CCK-MCD bij's browser\");\n}\nis present in the prefs.js which is the input to create the netscape.cfg.\nThis will change the value of the pref IFF the pref exists and not otherwise and \nso in reply to your question.\nYes you are right :-)",
            "creator": "vparthas@netscape.net",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-25T03:58:55Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Use of the non-XPCOM pref API makes me wince.  Is it really necessary?\n",
            "creator": "mike.shaver@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-25T14:37:34Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I guess that's what I'm asking.  I don't understand this netscapt.cfg magic.  If \nI just read the \"user_agent\" pref using the conventional means would I get what \nI need?  Varada, does that question make sense?  If so, what's the answer?",
            "creator": "law@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-25T21:59:36Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "over to paw for qa triage.",
            "creator": "bugzilla@iwaruna.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-26T00:29:25Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I believe so.  The preferenes are read during launch of Seamonkey.  When an end \nuser changes his/her preferences through the edit dialog, they are changed in \nmemory, but not on disk.  When the browser is closed (quit), the preferences are \nsaved.  \n\nThis user agent preference is read on launch and there is no way to change it \nfrom the client. ",
            "creator": "bijals@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-28T19:27:36Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Marking [nsbeta3+] per discussion with Bijal.  Note that this bug depends on \n5132.",
            "creator": "law@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-28T20:18:16Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "yes, don't worry about libpref's unique way of defining prefs, just use \nCopyCharPref where appropriate",
            "creator": "alecf@flett.org",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-28T21:23:25Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Please make it so that we can put this special \"user agent\" string in any prefs \nfile such as foo.js.  Therefore, you do not need to have netscape.cfg to have \nthis preference working.",
            "creator": "bijals@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-28T21:36:56Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I found out that our http protocol handler is already using the content of \nvarious pref settings to determine the user agent string.  See \nhttp://lxr.mozilla.org/seamonkey/source/netwerk/protocol/http/src/nsHTTPHandler.\ncpp#615.\n\nThis means that if CCK arranged to set, say, \"general.useragent.vendorComment\" \nthen that would automatically appear in the user agent string.  I think that \nmight be better than adding additional code on top of what's there already.\n\nFor example, you could put this in your prefs.js right now:\n   user_pref(\"general.useragent.vendorComment\", \"CCK-MCD bij's browser\");\n\nThe only drawback would be if CCK is only capable of setting the \"user_agent\" \npref, rather than \"general.useragent.vendorComment\" (or some other \ngeneral.useragent pref).\n\nCan CCK use the existing pref?  Or, do I need to add the code that extracts the \n\"user_agent\" pref and inserts it into the vendor comment field?",
            "creator": "law@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-29T18:07:05Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "We think CCK can manage this by simply setting the \ngeneral.useragent.vendorComment pref (rather than the user_agent pref).\n\nSo, I'm reassigning to Varada to prompt him (or somebody) to tweak CCK to do \nthat.  Leaving [nsebeta3+]; hope that's OK.",
            "creator": "law@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-29T19:17:31Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "PDT agrees P1",
            "creator": "phil@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-31T01:07:55Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "accepting ",
            "creator": "vparthas@netscape.net",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-31T17:12:04Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Adding [pdtp1] in status summary.",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-09-07T10:15:27Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "The user agent which is an aggregate of 8 different pref values including the\nvendor comment. The vendor comment is given the value of the customized string\nthru CCK. This then gets inserted in the pref file and is read by the browser\nand is used while creating the overall value for the navigator.userAgent.\n",
            "creator": "vparthas@netscape.net",
            "timestamp": "2000-09-22T16:50:38Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Varada, please add to this bug examples of the following:\n\n*user agent string customized by CCK user (for example, MyISP)\n*user agent string default (not customized by CCK user)\n\nThanks.",
            "creator": "robinf@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-09-22T17:26:21Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Updating QA Contact\n",
            "creator": "pawyskoczka@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-09-25T16:24:48Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "updating QA Contact to blee@netscape.com",
            "creator": "bmartin@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2001-06-18T21:24:45Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "qa to me since blee is on sabatical.  Verified on CCK build 2001-09-24-07",
            "creator": "BarrettLndstrm@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "2001-09-24T21:51:44Z"
        }
    ]
}

{
    "bug_id": 6141,
    "summary": "FTP download crashes",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "Using the CVS source of Mozilla here, freshly compiled with EGCS 1.1.2 on a Red\nHat 6.0 i386 system, with glibc 2.1 and GTK+ 1.2.1, (Linux kernel 2.2.7, and on\na Pentium 200 MMX with 32 megs of RAM), with a build ID of 1999050422, it seems\nwhen I try to do an FTP download from the above URL,\n\n1) The statistics are a bit strange; I notice about 9 or 10 decimal places in\nthe statistics, and sometimes it even goes into scientific notation.\n2) When I finally got the file, it was completely corrupted...  It did not even\nbegin to resemble what I was expecting, and it was about 5 times larger than\nwhat it was supposed to be.  VERY odd indeed.",
            "creator": "zuperdee@yahoo.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-05-08T07:40:03Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "BTW, I still have the corrupted file available, in case it gives you any\nadditional clues.  I would attach it here, but Bugzilla doesn't seem to like\nit.  I guess maybe it's too big?",
            "creator": "zuperdee@yahoo.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-05-08T07:47:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Update: I forgot that Mozilla would automatically un-gzip it.  So I tried just\nun-tarring it, but found that even as a plain tar file, it is corrupted...  The\ntar program returned this error message:\ntar: Skipping to next file header\ntar: Only read 7848 bytes from archive flyingwindows-0.2.tar.gz\ntar: Error is not recoverable: exiting now\n\nThis is really getting wierder and wierder...",
            "creator": "zuperdee@yahoo.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-05-08T08:56:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Bill, is FTP download on Linux really this torqued?",
            "creator": "don@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-05-10T16:32:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I'll have to beg some help from an x-head for this one.  Will look at next week.",
            "creator": "law@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-05-15T01:15:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Move this to M7 ...",
            "creator": "don@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-05-20T23:46:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "paulmac, is this similar to http://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=5854",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-01T22:45:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "no this bug appears to have something to do with the integrity of the file being\ndownloaded, as opposed to a simple crash",
            "creator": "paulmac@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-01T23:01:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "All the same, I wonder if this isn't related to bug 5854...  In any case, I am\nwilling to wait until Necko lands to look at this further.\n\nBTW, Bugzilla will form links automatically if you type \"bug ####.\"  Do you\nsuppose you can do this in the future instead of just the bug number alone, so I\ndon't have to open up a new browser window and enter the bug number manually\neverytime?",
            "creator": "zuperdee@yahoo.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-01T23:28:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Bill, should we move this out a milestone or two until Nekko lands?",
            "creator": "don@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-09T22:05:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Moving this to M9 until after Nekko lands.",
            "creator": "don@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-10T01:04:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 8897 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-28T21:54:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Okay, now that Necko has landed, I thought I'd give a further update: When I\nvisit the given URL again, I now get a popup \"Unknown File Type\" box.  This\nshouldn't be, since the URL is for an FTP directory, not a file.",
            "creator": "zuperdee@yahoo.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-16T01:09:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "ftp doesn't seem to be working at all so I can't do anything with this one.\nWill try again when ftp comes back online (see bug #12834).",
            "creator": "law@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-13T21:37:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "There must be something funky about that particular ftp server.  I can\nsuccessfully browser other ftp: directories (e.g., ftp://hobbes.nmsu.edu/).\n\nI'm reassigning this to valeski who hacks the ftp protocol handler.  If he\ndetermines that the protocol handler is doing the right thing, then I'll look at\nit again from my end.",
            "creator": "law@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-20T20:07:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I can access the site just fine (a little slow though)",
            "creator": "jud@me.dium.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-22T18:29:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Hot damn, it works for me, too (at least today).  I'll hurry up and marke it\nresolved.",
            "creator": "law@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-22T21:14:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I'm using Build ID 1999112108 on Linux, and I'm experiencing more FTP problems.\nThe test link shown above (ftp://hobbes.nmsu.edu/) opens up an \"Unknown File\nType\" box.\n  Also, when trying to download the latest nightly build for Mozilla\n(ftp://www.mozilla.org/pub/mozilla/nightly/latest/mozilla-i686-pc-linux-gnu.tar.gz\nin my case), it goes to the download window, waits a few seconds, and then pops\nopen a box that says \"Unknown topic:\ncomponent://netscape/appshell/component/xfer;onError    Data: 2 8052E891\".\nAfter closing the box, a new one appears, and I am eventually forced to kill the\ndownload and Mozilla with it.",
            "creator": "gstoll@rice.edu",
            "timestamp": "1999-11-23T04:37:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Should we re-open this bug then?",
            "creator": "zuperdee@yahoo.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-11-23T16:27:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Sigh.\n\nftp://ftp.sonic.net/pub/users/nbs/unix/x/flyingwindows/ produces a ftp directory\nlisting.  Clicking on the tar.gz file in that directory produces a crash in nspr\nevent queue code.  At least that's what it does on WinNT.  My Linux build\ndownloads it fine.  That's bug #1.\n\nftp://hobbes.nmsu.edu/ produces a ftp directory listing.  I can't descend any\nsubfolders. though.  I can add the subdirectory name to the URL in the urlbar,\nthough.  That's bug #2.\n\nftp://www.mozilla.org/pub/mozilla/nightly/latest/mozilla-i686-pc-linux-gnu.tar.g\nz generates an error because that file doesn't exist at the server.  This error\nisn't handled by Mozilla, however.  It generates an unknown-content dialog.  If\nyou choose \"Save file...\" it \"successfully\" downloads 0 bytes (ignoring the fact\nthat there is no file at that URL).  That's bug #3.\n\nI'd like to use this bug report to track bug #1 (since current behavior\nresembles the original bug report).  The other two bugs are either covered by\nother bugs or I will open some.\n\nI'll dig deeper into why it's failing to download files from that one location\nin today's Windows build.",
            "creator": "law@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-11-24T01:05:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Clearing WorkForMe and reopening.",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-11-24T02:14:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Setting to M12, since M11 is outta here!",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-11-24T02:15:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Jeez, let's move this to M14 if warren is gonna fix bug #12834 until then.",
            "creator": "don@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-02T01:10:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Worry about this later ...",
            "creator": "don@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-23T06:32:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Going to <URL:ftp://ftp.sonic.net/pub/users/nbs/unix/x/flyingwindows/> and\nclicking on \"flyingwindows-0.2.tar.gz\" works just fine for me as well under\nLinux, using build 2000030316.\n\nI'm changing OS to Windows NT per law's comments, and changing the summary to be\na little more descriptive.",
            "creator": "braden@endoframe.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-03-06T07:37:22Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Bill, is this still a bug?  If not, close it ASAP, please.\n",
            "creator": "don@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-07T02:42:51Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This is working (for the moment).  If download breaks again, do we really have \nto go and re-open every single \"download didn't work\" but that was ever written?  \nPlease, let's not.",
            "creator": "law@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-07T18:26:22Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "sorry fot the spam, changing QA contact.",
            "creator": "shrir@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-24T23:19:52Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "verif.",
            "creator": "bugzilla@iwaruna.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-24T23:23:57Z"
        }
    ]
}

{
    "bug_id": 6873,
    "summary": "Mailnews folder loading performance tracker.",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "Using IMAP, I get a bunch of messages about how mailnews is going to the server\nand the timing between gets progressively slower and slower. Looks like there's\nsome sort of slow linear process here that it does for each message. After a while\nit REALLY starts to crawl. I'm not sure if this has to do with the fact that my\nmailbox has lots of messages, or that there are lots of mailboxes in my IMAP\nmailspace, but it sure is annyoing.",
            "creator": "cyrus@neomorphic.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-05-21T00:26:48Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Unfortunately, this is expected behavior with the current code. We need to have\nsome table layout improvements from hyatt before we expect this to get better.\nReassigning to hyatt for now.",
            "creator": "phil@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-05-21T01:16:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Adding myself and waterson to the cc list since we are both involved in this.\nChanged Platform and OS to All since the Mac shouldn't get all the fun, and\nchanged priority to P1 since we aren't a product without this fix.\n\nThis will happen on Pop3, and news, as well as Imap.  Although we may have\nperformance problems with regard to getting the messages from the Imap Server,\nthat's most likely not the case(or at least the bottleneck) since we've seen the\nsame slowing down affect on both Pop and News.\n\nChris and I have been able to improve performance a bunch with some other\nchanges we've made but at the moment it looks like the number of times we\nrelayout the table is what is causing our problem.\n\nSee following threads in the netscape.public.mozilla.mail-news for discussions\nof this:\n\n\"Profiling results for displaying headers in the thread pane.\" 5/22/99\n\"More profiling results for displaying headers in the Messenger thread pane\"\n5/26/99\n\"Messenger Performance update\" 6/2/99 which I will use to track our progress\n\nChris and David, we should talk about how this is going to work at some point.\nOne of my concerns is that David's code will only ask for 10 messages but that\nthe RDF code will still build up the content model for 10,000 messages.  In that\ncase GetTarget will be a huge bottleneck since it looks like we can process\nabout 100 messages in .5 sec currently(i.e. 10,000 messages would take 50\nseconds by default).  Even if I can speed up GetTarget, we still have another 5\nor so columns that haven't been added, so at best those cancel each other out.",
            "creator": "scottputterman@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-07T18:50:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "What we'll probably need to do is change RDF-generated content to be fully lazy,\ni.e., make it so that it has a finer level of granularity regarding the building\nof children.  Right now whenever we need to find out information about the\nchildren of a node, RDF goes off and builds all of the children.\n\nRDF should only build children as they are asked for, and we should annotate\nnodes with visible child counts, so that we don't have to make all the children\nwhen we ask for the child count of a node.",
            "creator": "hyatt@mozilla.org",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-07T19:00:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 8472 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "phil@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-18T15:53:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Added dogfood distinction to summary.",
            "creator": "michaell@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-18T22:17:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "We will have some numbers for loading POP folders soon.  The machine we're\nusing is a 166mhz with 48mb RAM.  Recently, it took about 64 seconds to load\n1000 messages (.msf file already created) on Win32.",
            "creator": "lchiang@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-29T16:17:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I'm still (6/28) seeing unacceptable performance when deleting messages via\nIMAP. The particular scenario is:\n1. Open mozilla. Load mailbox with 650 messages. Quit.\n2. An another machine, delete some messages, get some new messages, etc...\n3. Open mozilla. Watch mozilla crawl as it attempts to sync up the mailbox.",
            "creator": "cyrus@neomorphic.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-29T16:25:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I have numbers for loading Pop folders on the mail-news newsgroup in various\nthreads called \"Messenger Performance update\".  The machine may be fast, but you\ncan still see progress made with the numbers.  A machine with less memory is\nuseful also since it will help us measure the performance hit we take because of\nit.\n\nGetting new messages is always going to be worse than just loading a folder\nwith our current architecture.  That's one of the reasons why this bug exists\nand is not marked fixed yet. You can view the various threads on the newsgroup\nto see why the asynchronous case is worse.  Therefore I'd also expect things\nlike deleting and marking read to be slow as well.  Admittedly I haven't used\nimap very much with 5.0, but until we get folder performance fixed, I'm not sure\nwe can attribute anything to the IMAP code yet (unless of course you are running\nIMAP tests outside of Apprunner or you are synching with a folder that is not\nthe currently loaded folder in which case we could attribute this to the IMAP\ncode).",
            "creator": "scottputterman@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-29T16:41:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Moving to M9 and handing off to waterson. My task here is done. :)",
            "creator": "hyatt@mozilla.org",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-01T07:26:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Boy oh boy!",
            "creator": "waterson@maubi.net",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-01T14:37:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Checked in some improvements for the template builder (lazily build template\ncontent as frame system asks for it). This should give a 2-3x speedup for\nfolders that have already been indexed.",
            "creator": "waterson@maubi.net",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-19T19:46:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I'm going to change the meaning of this bug.  We're getting a big push right now\non the async case, I guess people higher up suddenly started seeing our numbers.\nSo, since a large portion of the work on this bug has gone to .msf case, I'd\nlike to leave this to represent that.  I will open up another bug we can track\nfor the async case.  I will cc all of the people on this bug.",
            "creator": "scottputterman@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-28T21:51:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "scottip is owner of this \"meta bug\" now.",
            "creator": "waterson@maubi.net",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-06T21:55:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This bug goes on as long as the product does.  Marking M15.  Changing summary.",
            "creator": "scottputterman@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-06T22:19:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Obviously, we need to get faster performance by Beta 1.\n\nScott: If the target milestone is M15, will this bug stay on your radar as we go\nfrom one pre-Beta 1 milestone to the next?",
            "creator": "sol@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-12T16:46:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This bug will never leave my radar.  I made it M15 because I'm sure it will be\nongoing until we ship.  Plus, the bugs it depends upon are the more important\nones since those are where the real work is being done.",
            "creator": "scottputterman@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-12T17:06:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I'm going to change the dependency bug from 12176 (dogfood) to 10791\n(feature) tracking bugs since we're already at dogfood, I believe, since folks\nare using the product internally.  Since this bug is always \"on-going,\" I\nthink having it on the feature tracking bug is better.  If anyone disagrees, pls\nchange back.  Thanks.",
            "creator": "lchiang@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-18T19:49:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Remove [dogfood] from bug summary",
            "creator": "phil@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-07T01:46:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 21419 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "lchiang@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-21T23:51:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Bulk add of \"perf\" to new keyword field.  This will replace the [PERF] we were\nusing in the Status Summary field.",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-07T16:21:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Removing [PR1] since we're using keywords now. Nominating for beta1 since we are\ncurrently more than 2x slower than 4.x (according to Suresh's Jan 14 performance\ntesting results). Not much more than 2x, but more.\n",
            "creator": "phil@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-28T04:11:34Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Putting on PDT+ radar for beta1.",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-29T01:47:28Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "why is a top-level tracking bug marked PDT+? this is a meta-bug, not related to \nany task AFAICT. Removing \"PDT+\" and \"beta1\". What am I missing here?",
            "creator": "waterson@maubi.net",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-31T16:40:25Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Mass moving to M16 to get these off the M15 radar.  Please let me know if this\nis really an M15 stopper.\n",
            "creator": "selmer@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-05T02:57:16Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Not M16 stopper.  Marking M17.",
            "creator": "selmer@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-16T21:26:15Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "moving to M18, though to be honest it's not as if I'm going to forget this bug \nexists :-)",
            "creator": "scottputterman@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-06-21T05:04:05Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Downloading 50 additional messages into INBOX (which already has 1000+) messages\ntakes around 202 secs, thats pretty slow. \nTested using build 2000-08-02-04, M18 on Linux (performance system). \n\nOther Platforms (same build dates)\nMac: 10.20 seconds. \nWindows: 20.72\n\n",
            "creator": "pratikd@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-07T18:14:40Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Putterman, you haven't forgotten about this bug have you?  It's got a milestone\nof M18, is apparently a tracker and has no unresolved dependencies.  Come on,\nyou said you wouldn't forget about it.  =)",
            "creator": "matty_is_a_geek@fastmail.fm",
            "timestamp": "2001-02-18T01:40:24Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Rest assured, we haven't forgotten about it, in fact we are working very\ndilligently on this.  Wish I could say more.",
            "creator": "stephend@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2001-02-18T01:43:28Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "reassigning to sspitzer.  This is in the process of being fixed.",
            "creator": "scottputterman@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2001-02-18T08:50:14Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "For those of you interested, check out\nhttp://www.mozilla.org/mailnews/performance/speed.html and keep track of the\nnewsgroups on news.mozilla.org:119 (groups netscape.public.mozilla.mail-news and\nnetscape.public.mozilla.performance)",
            "creator": "stephend@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2001-02-19T14:05:51Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "please reconsider the milestone on this bug; it's kinda hard to go back in time. :)",
            "creator": "hwaara@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2001-02-19T14:12:58Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This *will* be vastly improved with the thread pane re-write.  See the URL above.",
            "creator": "stephend@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2001-03-03T01:38:44Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "this is a dup (the dup is later but it's already got all of the markings on it.)\n\n*** This bug has been marked as a duplicate of 26456 ***",
            "creator": "scottputterman@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2001-03-06T05:53:31Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "verified dup, \"Folder load performance is slow\" bug 26456",
            "creator": "stephend@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2001-03-06T05:57:27Z"
        }
    ]
}

{
    "bug_id": 8014,
    "summary": "[FEATURE][PP] Can't tab caret between form text fields.",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "using 6/11 build of apprunner on linux\n\n1) launch apprunner\n2) go to any page that has multiple form fields.\nOne URL is given above.\n3) click in the first form field\n4) hit Tab key to get to the next field.\n\ndoesn't work. I could have sworn this was working sometime ago.\n\nworks fine on Mac and Windows...",
            "creator": "sujay@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-11T19:58:06Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "resummarizing.",
            "creator": "mcafee@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-11T20:08:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Putting on the M8 radar.",
            "creator": "mcafee@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-17T23:59:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "moving to m9 after discussion with ramiro",
            "creator": "chofmann@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-12T22:49:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Alex Larsson was helping me with this, but hes on vacation now.  Marking m10.",
            "creator": "ramiro@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-11T16:08:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "m11, but not really a blocker.",
            "creator": "ramiro@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-02T06:53:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Marking dup of 6750.\n\n*** This bug has been marked as a duplicate of 6750 ***",
            "creator": "ramiro@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-08T16:06:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Re-opening. This bug states that keyboard shortcuts aren't working. Bug 6750\nsays that there should be a visual cue when switching between form elements.\nTabbing is given as an example, however it would seem that clicking with the\nmouse would produce the same effect for that bug. (although one would hope you\nknew what form element you were in if you used your moust.)\n\nIt's one thing if you can't tab between fields, it's another if you can but you\ncan't tell where you're at.",
            "creator": "jelwell@singleclick.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-14T23:49:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Clearing DUPLICATE resolution due to reopen.",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-15T01:49:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "ramiro, will you be working on this?  if not, who?\n\nIf you will fix, what milestone should this be.  Due to reopen, this needs to be\non M12 (which is closing down tonight) or later.\n\nThanks!",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-15T02:09:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "tabbing works for me, there's a focus problem though;\nhitting return only happens on the first form element\nwhere you started tabbing.",
            "creator": "mcafee@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-15T05:26:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Oh no, not another morphing bug!  This one was written up as an inability to tab\nbetween form fields, with the bugzilla query page used as an example.  I take\nthis to mean that you cannot move the caret from one text field to another using\nthe tab key. Is that right?  Latest summary is overly broad, and duplicates a\nbug that saari just fixed today, resummarizing.  This tab defect is happening\nfor me today on Win98, MacOS 8.6 and Linux.  I expect 4.x behavior, where the\ncaret moves between text fields.  What I get is a growing outline selection (as\nif I was doing a discontiguous selection) moving between successive elements,\nincluding URLs, but no movement of the caret.\npossibly related to 21536.  reassigning to saari as p3 for m13",
            "creator": "trudelle@acm.org",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-16T01:21:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This sounds like a bug on Eric Pollmann's plate.  Adding myself and him to cc\nlist.",
            "creator": "brade@comcast.net",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-16T23:14:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 21893 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "vparthas@netscape.net",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-17T00:45:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 21896 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "vparthas@netscape.net",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-17T01:08:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "The 'discontiguous selection' bug is already reported as 20322.\n\nThis bug applies only to the caret not appearing in text inputs/text areas that\nreceive focus through tabbing in to them.",
            "creator": "pollmann@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-17T01:42:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This might sound like ambiguo-bug 9784, which is actually an older issue that\nwas fixed - tabbing doesn't work at all with GFX widgets.  I'm going to close\nout 9784 because tabbing works for the most part.  The only remaining issues I\ncan see are:\n\n20322 - Fields don't erase their border when they loose focus\n8014 - Tabbing into text areas doesn't move the caret.\n\nMaybe Steve would know more about this recent bug?",
            "creator": "pollmann@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-17T01:48:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Tabbing between <input> and <textarea> seems to work in the browser, except that\nthere are focus issues.  I think these are the issues that saari and hyatt are\nalready dealing with in bug 21887.",
            "creator": "buster@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-17T07:49:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Sorry: I need to update this to diagnose a mail bug...IGNORE THIS COMMENT:\n\nTabbing between <input> and <textarea> seems to work in the browser, except\nthat there are focus issues.  I think these are the issues that saari and hyatt\nare already dealing with in bug 21887.",
            "creator": "rhp@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-17T18:15:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "My bug (21893) was marked a duplicate of this so I just wanted to make sure that\nthe specific behavior I noticed was included here.  When asked for a username\nand password (such as for a .htaccess protected site) the tab doesn't work to go\nbetween the username and password boxes.  This behavior was noticed on Windows\n98 SE using build number 199121314 (even tho this bug is marked as being for\nlinux).",
            "creator": "jacob@steenhagen.us",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-17T22:56:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Adding pmock@netscape.com to cc: list",
            "creator": "pmock@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-17T23:24:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Changing platform/os to ALL since this has been reported on all platforms (I see\n\non Mac).",
            "creator": "brade@comcast.net",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-20T15:01:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 22317 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "pollmann@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-22T00:12:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I believe this is fixed now.  I've tested on windows and mac. Claudius, can you\nverify ***** on all 3 platforms ****  Thanks.",
            "creator": "buster@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-23T22:09:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 22565 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "pollmann@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-24T05:34:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 22741 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "sidr@albedo.net",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-07T04:17:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 23469 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "pollmann@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-11T00:05:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Massive QA Contact update.",
            "creator": "ckritzer@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-03-08T13:43:58Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "verified.",
            "creator": "sujay@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2001-05-09T21:54:36Z"
        }
    ]
}

{
    "bug_id": 9041,
    "summary": "User Password dialog ( and SS dialogs ) don't work",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "Build #1999062909\n\nI appear to have the Autofill feature enabled.  I browse to Bugzilla via the\nlink on the personal toolbar, and what looks like an autofill window pops up\nover the half-loaded page.  This box never gets fully populated.  I cannot\ndismiss this box.  Even if I hide the box, I still cannot access any links on\nthe page behind the box.\n\nIf I hide the box, and then position the cursor in the location field and hit\nreturn to initiate a reload, the whole page appears to load, but I cannot access\nany links.  The only things that appear to be live and working in the chrome are\nthe \"home\" and \"my netscape\" links.  When I click the \"my\" link, I go to the\nhome page, but no links there are active.  If I hide this window and then come\nback to it, Seamonkey displays the half-loaded bugzilla page with the banner ad\nfrom the home page.\n\nOpening a new browser window does not help matters.",
            "creator": "michaell@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-29T22:18:12Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Yes, I just discoved this bug myself earlier in the week and was about to open a\nreport on it.  It is definitely a regression.\n\nHere are the conditions under which it occurs.  If you are going to a login page\nfor which you have already saved username/password, and you haven't yet unlocked\nyour database in the current session, you are supposed to get a dialog asking\nfor your database password.  You are probably on the netlib thread at this time\nand that is why the dialog is hanging.  But I can't explain why it used to work\nunless the threading has been changed.\n\nIn any event, I can't fix it yet because the necko landing will change the\nthreading again.  So let me offer you a work-around -- if you have enabled\nsingle signon, then make sure you manually unlock your database before going to\nany site for which you have previously saved username/password.  You can force\nsuch an unlock in several ways -- the simplest is to go to the signon viewer\n(edit/wallet/view-signons) and delete at least one of the saved signons that you\nsee there.\n\nBTW, the problem is only with single-signon -- never with wallet.  The reason is\nthat wallet never tries to fill in automatically but rather does so when the\nuser manually presses a button.  So this is not on the network thread.  Single\nsignon does so automatically when you return to a page for which you previously\nsaved.  And the fill-in would be seamless (no dialog) provided the data base had\nalready been unlocked.",
            "creator": "morse@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-29T22:59:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Hey, this is more general than autofill -- I just tried going to a site for\nwhich you need to be authenticated and I got the same behavior.  That is, a site\nthat puts up a username/password dialog box before it lets you enter.  If you\ndon't know any such sites, try\nhttp://www.w3.org/P3P/Group/Syntax/Drafts/WD-P3P-19980814/syntax.html.\n\nA bit of history here.  Whenever such a site is visited, the browser puts up a\nlogin form.  I used to have a call to single signon at that point so that I\ncould put up (and capture) such logins.  But apparently it was not working\nbecause the call was being done on the netlib thread.  So davidm removed my\nsingle-signon call (in mkaccess.c)and used code in the network module to put up\nthis dialog safely.  And that had been working the last time I tried it.  But\njust now when I tried it even davidm's safe dialog no longer works.\n\nSo this is more serious than wallet/single-signon.  Somebody changed something\nvery recently that broke all such dialogs.  Reassigning to davidm since this is\nnow in his domain.  Also changing the title to remove the mention of autofill\nand changing the component from autofill to html dialog.",
            "creator": "morse@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-30T02:02:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Assign but I am not going to look at it until after necko lands.",
            "creator": "davidm@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-03T03:52:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "David, is there any workaround for this for M8? Any page that requires\nauthentication will essentially hang the browser.",
            "creator": "paulmac@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-07T01:17:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Besides using a Mac I don't have a solution. I am sure it is something in netlib\nand I don't want to look at until after necko lands",
            "creator": "davidm@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-07T01:32:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Okay, will release note.",
            "creator": "paulmac@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-07T01:42:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Reassigning to don to see if this should be in m8",
            "creator": "davidm@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-08T22:59:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "David says we really can't fix this the right way until Necko lands.  Anything\nelse is just another band-aid that will no doubt break again the next day.  Move\nthis to M9 for now ...",
            "creator": "don@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-09T19:25:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 10119 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "davidm@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-19T21:00:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I am reassigning to Necko because as far as I can tell Necko is never calling\nthe FE to put up the dialog. I have bugs on the other dialog issues in this bug.\nIf this is untrue, please point me towards the code that asks for the dialog.\n\tAnd for what its worth I'll be checking in new dialog code in the next couple\nof days and I'll do a post with all the details of how to use it.",
            "creator": "davidm@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-10T04:41:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I am going to have to mark this for post M9. Since we need to finish up some\nmore critical bugs for M9 first. And the deadline is tonite!!",
            "creator": "gagan@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-11T05:23:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 6144 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "warrensomebody@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-31T23:21:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** This bug has been marked as a duplicate of 6144 ***",
            "creator": "warrensomebody@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-31T23:23:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Bulk move of all Necko (to be deleted component) bugs to new Networking\n\ncomponent.",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-14T00:39:59Z"
        }
    ]
}

{
    "bug_id": 9458,
    "summary": "Implement inline-block in layout",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "using 7/8 build of apprunner\n\n1) launch apprunner\n2) launch editor\n3) insert anchor\n\nanchor icon doesn't get inserted.\n\nall platforms",
            "creator": "sujay@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-08T22:25:30Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I've already tried all kinds of CSS tricks to do this and have discussed it\nwith Peter, so I think it's best to just hand the bug to him.\nFor background, here's most of our last exchange:\nCharles Manske wrote:\nI can't seem to morph the \"A\" tag into something visible by any of your\nsuggestions. Here's what I settled on for \"proof of concept\"  testing, even\nthough it's not inline (this is in mozilla/editor/ui/composer/skin/Editor.css):\n  a[name][href=\"\"] {\n    display: list-item;\n    list-style-image: url(chrome://editor/skin/images/ED_Left.gif);\n    list-style-position: inside;\n    line-height: 10px;\n    min-width: 10px;\n  }\n  Peter Linss wrote:\n\n    Firstly, to make it apply to only <A> tags with the name attribute use:\n\"a[name]\" for your selector (if you want to exclude hrefs that also\n    have names, use: \"a[name][href=\"\"]\").\n\n    Charles Manske wrote:\n\n     In the editor, we want to show a named anchor as a small image. To explore\nthis, I tried the following CSS:\n     a {\n       display: inline;\n       width: 10px;\n       height: 10px;\n       border: 1px solid blue;\n     }\n    Inlines have special rules about respecting width and height, in short,\nheight doesn't work (use line-height) instead. I'm not sure about if\n    width will work when the element is empty, you might try 'min-width'.\n     or:\n     a {\n       display: list-item;\n       list-style-image: url(chrome://editor/skin/images/ED_Left.gif);\n     }\n    This probably should work You should add 'list-style-position: inside' to\nkeep the image from appearing outside the element's margin.\n    But again, I'm not sure if empty list-items get bullets... Also, display:\nlist-item will create a block level frame, I presume you really want an\n    inline\n     or:\n     a {\n       display: table; // or inline-table;\n       background-image: url(chrome://editor/skin/images/ED_Left.gif);\n     }\n\n    This will probably only work in \"standard mode\", in \"quirk mode\" tables\ndon't draw backgrounds (it gets shoved into the cell). I'm also not\n    sure if inline-table is working, but that's what you really want.\n\n    I think what you really want is a bit of CSS3 that hasn't been implemented\nyet (but I think we're going to have to real soon).\n    a[name][href=\"\"] {\n      display: inline-block;    /* the new feature */\n      width: 10px;\n      height: 10px;\n      background-image: url(...);\n      border: 1px solid blue;\n    }",
            "creator": "cmanske@jivamedia.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-08T23:21:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "One problem is that width doesn't apply to inline elements, so attempts to force\nit will fail.  I see two solutions:\n\n* wait for inline-block or inline-table\n* use :before or :after and get joki to fix bug 5886 if you need it (i.e., check\nin the fix attached to the bug)\n\nAnd does [href=\"\"] select elements without an href attribute?  I don't think it\nshould.\n\nSo I would think:\n\na[name]:before {\n  content: url(....gif);\n  border: 2px solid blue;\n  }\n\na[name][href]:before {\n  content: \"\";\n  border: none;\n  }\n\nwould be closer to what you want.  Also, since a elements with a name attribute\nstill enclose text, you probably want that text to still be visible, so I think\n:before is a good choice.  (Note, however, that :before is really a first child,\nnot a previous sibling, so the style applied to the a applies to the :before.)\nHowever, what if the document already has a :before pseudo-element for\nanchors...?",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-21T20:40:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I applied the patch for bug 5886. Using \":before\" does indeed display an\nimage like we want. BUT it won't work because we don't allow selecting\ngenerated content. The whole purpose of making the anchor visible is to allow\nthe user to click on it (thus selecting it) so they can delete it, copy\nit, or bring up the property dialog for it.",
            "creator": "cmanske@jivamedia.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-22T00:54:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "inline-block is in the style system. Waiting for Nisheeth and/or Troy to hook it\nup to layout.",
            "creator": "peterl-retired@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-28T21:18:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Accepting bug and setting target milestone to M9...",
            "creator": "nisheeth_mozilla@yahoo.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-29T00:39:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Kipp has certain questions about the semantics of inline-block that he wants to\ndiscuss with Peter once he gets back from the W3C CSS working group meeting.\nWe'll scope this out more for M10...",
            "creator": "nisheeth_mozilla@yahoo.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-10T22:03:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Updating summary and setting milestone to M11.  I need to work on this when I\nget back from vacation.",
            "creator": "nisheeth_mozilla@yahoo.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-28T06:08:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "[Adding a radar... Hmm, first time I've put in a {css3} radar...]",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-05T21:23:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Is it really a good idea to be implementing a draft standard?  How close is CSS3\nto proposed standard status?",
            "creator": "matty_is_a_geek@fastmail.fm",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-06T00:58:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Adding Akkana to cc.",
            "creator": "cmanske@jivamedia.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-21T19:18:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "The named anchor tag currently in the editor init page looks very bad on Linux\n-- it draws on top of some of the text on that line and the next line.  Charley\nsays it doesn't do that on Windows, and that perhaps this has something to do\nwith the style not being fully implemented yet.  When working on this bug, it\nmight be useful to look at the named anchor in the editor init page on several\nplatforms and compare their presentations.",
            "creator": "akkzilla@shallowsky.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-21T19:21:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "The style code is 100% cross platform, so the linux issue in not likely that.\nPerhaps a font metrics issue?",
            "creator": "peterl-retired@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-21T19:32:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I've split the Linux rendering issue off into bug 14474.",
            "creator": "akkzilla@shallowsky.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-21T21:58:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Charley, is this a beta blocker for you guys?  I'm moving it out to the M12\nmilestone for now...",
            "creator": "nisheeth_mozilla@yahoo.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-23T21:28:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "We must solve the problem of displaying something for normally hidden elements\nlike Named Anchor, and there doesn't seem to be any other CSS way of doing that\n*inline*, so I guess the answer is yes unless it is a lot of work.",
            "creator": "cmanske@jivamedia.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-23T21:51:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Having reread the comments above, I don't really see how inline-block _will_\nhelp, actually. I think David's use of generated content is probably best; why\ncan we not select generated content?\n\nAlternatively, use this:\n   a[name] { padding-left: 20px; background: url(...gif) 5px 50% no-repeat; }\nThere are some issues with 'background-position' on inline elements, though.\n(I will split them off into another bug.)",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-23T22:31:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Adding dependency to 16515 -- selection of generated content in the editor.\nIf we can't solve that bug, then we may need the inline-block CSS attribute to\nrepresent hidden elements in the editor.",
            "creator": "cmanske@jivamedia.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-15T17:06:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Move non-PDT+ bugs to M13...",
            "creator": "nisheeth_mozilla@yahoo.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-01T23:44:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Moving non-blockers for beta to M15...",
            "creator": "nisheeth_mozilla@yahoo.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-14T19:13:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Just got word from charley that he is no longer blocked by this.  Moving off to \nM20.",
            "creator": "nisheeth_mozilla@yahoo.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-03-29T00:34:39Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This bug has been marked \"future\" because the original netscape engineer working \non this is over-burdened. If you feel this is an error, that you or another\nknown resource will be working on this bug,or if it blocks your work in some way \n-- please attach your concern to the bug for reconsideration. ",
            "creator": "nisheeth_mozilla@yahoo.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-06-08T23:30:40Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I also ran into this. The problem is, that without inline-block, it's impossible \nto generate an inline element that has a certain (specified) width. As Mozilla \nsupports other CSS3 properties, the question if or if not supporting CSS3 seems \nto be answered in the meantime. \nFrom my opinion there are two possible workarounds which should allow setting a \npredefined width: inline-table (which does not work) or using a table and \nsetting the col-widths to the desired values (it's such an ugly workaround ...). \nI would like to hear, if there are other solutions, which I may have missed.",
            "creator": "make@gmx.li",
            "timestamp": "2000-07-15T20:18:41Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "As per meeting with ChrisD today, taking QA.",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "2000-07-26T03:43:31Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 118711 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "Daniel.Steinberger@gmx.de",
            "timestamp": "2002-07-08T00:19:19Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "i've read (bug 3935, comment 108: ...I did disable 'inline-block' and\n'inline-table'...) that we once had an implementation of this display style.\nwhere there problems with that? if not, why was it removed?\n\nIE (at least v6) does support 'display: inline-block' and i find it a very\nelegant way for some design-ideas (though i wouldn't use it, unil it's supported\nby some real browsers :-). i do know that this property is only in the cc3-wd,\nso i've read it over and found that imho IE's implementation seems correct. and\ni guess that it's not very hard to implement. \n\ni've also notived that there is a '-moz-inline-block' property that simply seems\nto act like 'block' but does not honor the 'display-role: inline; display-model:\nblock-inside;' stuff.\n\n\nthe question is simply: are you going to wait till there is some css3-box-model\nlast call for comments or later, or is this just because of resource-shortage?\n(last comment before: 2000-07-25)",
            "creator": "Daniel.Steinberger@gmx.de",
            "timestamp": "2002-07-08T00:40:31Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "resource shortage.\n\nWhat used to be display:inline-block; is not display:-moz-inline-block; so you\ncan determine for yourself how badly broken it is (very).",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "2002-07-08T13:37:47Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "CSS2.1 includes inline-block\n\ninline-block is also needed for lots of form elements. These are today marked as\ninline which is obviously incorrect since inline elements cannot have any width.\n\nIncreasing priority...",
            "creator": "erik@eae.net",
            "timestamp": "2002-09-02T13:06:58Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Form elements are \"replaced elements\" and CSS 2.1 doesn't say what to do with them.",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "2002-09-10T18:54:09Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Hixie, you wrote: \"What used to be display:inline-block; is not\ndisplay:-moz-inline-block;\", should \"not\" be \"now\"?\n\nReassigning to a better component.",
            "creator": "samuel@sieb.net",
            "timestamp": "2003-01-21T05:45:38Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 204010 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "bzbarsky@mit.edu",
            "timestamp": "2003-05-01T03:38:08Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Unless I misunderstand, inline-block allows you to nest block-level elements \nwithin, for example, a span.  The span continues to be displayed inline, but \nits contents are treated as a block-level \"black box\" that doesn't affect how \nthe span is rendered (ie., you can imbed block-level constructs, such as UL).  \nAn example of a clean solution that would be very difficult without \"inline-\nblock\": http://www.bigtrouble.com/inline_block_1.htm (multiple columns, \"shrink \nwrapped widths\", centered horizontally).",
            "creator": "bryn@bigtrouble.com",
            "timestamp": "2003-06-29T23:35:31Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "(Sorry, try above link in IE6+, or Opera 7+)",
            "creator": "bryn@bigtrouble.com",
            "timestamp": "2003-06-29T23:36:47Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 217675 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "bzbarsky@mit.edu",
            "timestamp": "2003-08-29T04:08:36Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 135852\nTestcase for showing inline-block and moz-inline-block behaviour\n\nThis test-case shows the inline-block (and -moz-inline-block) behaviour.  I\ncouldn't find a good test anywhere within Bugzilla, so I thought I'd place it\nhere for others to use.\n\nBTW- any ideas on how to \"fake\" this behaviour using XBL?  I would imagine that\nthere's an element somewhere within Mozilla that affects layout like the <img>\ntag, but can contain arbitrary HTML markup.",
            "creator": "matthew@mastracci.com",
            "timestamp": "2003-11-18T23:04:11Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 135898\nTestcase for showing inline-block and moz-inline-block behaviour\n\nAdding a <br> inside the inline blocks to make it clearer. Also made sure that\nthe document validates to HTML 4.01 Strict",
            "creator": "erik@eae.net",
            "timestamp": "2003-11-19T09:49:26Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 135929\n\"hack\" to implement inline-block w/<button> (Mozilla-only)\n\nThanks for the testcase update!  I've found a hacky (but virtually\nindistiguishable) way to implement inline-block: use a <button>.  The <button>\ntag is an arbitrary HTML container.  With the following CSS styles, the\n\"button\"-esque nature of the element is removed, leaving an unstyled,\ninline-block HTML element.  \n\nMight there be a way to use the button rendering code to render <button> tags,\ninline-blocks and inline-tables?  AFAIK, these should render with the same\nlayout rules.  Perhaps Hixie might know if this is a valid assumption.\n\nbutton.E\n{\n\twidth: 100pt;\n\tborder: 1px solid black;\n\tbackground: inherit;\n\tfont: inherit;\n\tcolor: inherit;\n\tvertical-align: bottom;\n}\n\nSee my new attachment for a demonstration of how this looks.  The only issue is\nthat the text within the <button> is unselectable.",
            "creator": "matthew@mastracci.com",
            "timestamp": "2003-11-19T16:56:06Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 135942\nAnother test case that shows a possible hack using -moz-inline-box containing a block element\n\nI modified the test case again to use a hack that I found on the net. I already\nlost the URI and it is not included in my Firebird history :'( The hack uses a\n-moz-inline-box containing a block element. I guess this is basically what\nbutton is doing.\n\nAlthough one can achieve the desired layout using this technique it is really\nnot possible to use XBL to solve this problem. This really needs to be\nsupported natively in the layout engine.",
            "creator": "erik@eae.net",
            "timestamp": "2003-11-19T20:13:41Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 135946\ninline-block XBL hack",
            "creator": "matthew@mastracci.com",
            "timestamp": "2003-11-19T20:58:23Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 135947\nHTML that uses previous XBL hackery to fix inline-block\n\nUsing previously mentioned -moz-inline-box w/ block XBL hack.  Uses the XBL\nfrom the previous attachment.",
            "creator": "matthew@mastracci.com",
            "timestamp": "2003-11-19T21:00:23Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Using XBL and doing workarounds might be fun but this will not solve the real\nissues here:\n\n1. Will not support DOM Level 2 CSS\n2. Not compatible with CSS2\n\n\nI think I've done enough spamming of this bug so I'll keep quite now.",
            "creator": "erik@eae.net",
            "timestamp": "2003-11-19T21:15:31Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "It would be great if mozilla supported this. Opera does, Safari does, and hyatt\nsez that WinIE does.",
            "creator": "sfraser_bugs@smfr.org",
            "timestamp": "2004-03-25T19:57:46Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "http://www.w3.org/TR/2004/CR-CSS21-20040225/changes.html#q3",
            "creator": "gellert.gyuris@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2004-03-29T21:57:29Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This is valid CSS that we don't support and IE of all things does. Please?",
            "creator": "bugzilla1@dougweb.org",
            "timestamp": "2004-08-19T12:32:10Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 156506\ntest case\n\nTest case to show that only Opera has some native support for\n'display:inline-block'.\n\nPlease don't spam this bug any futher with useless comments.",
            "creator": "annevk@annevk.nl",
            "timestamp": "2004-08-19T12:42:07Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I was basing my remark about IE on the tests in comments #31 and #35, as well as\ncomment #25 - none of which anyone has repudiated. If these tests are wrong then\nI apologise, if not I stand by my comment.",
            "creator": "bugzilla1@dougweb.org",
            "timestamp": "2004-08-19T13:01:49Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "It would be nice to have support for inline-block - not only to call Firefox a\nstandards-compliant browser (it does not comply with CSS2.1), but also because\nusing handfuls of table cells etc. to do formatting is getting old.",
            "creator": "lpb+moz@kandl.houston.tx.us",
            "timestamp": "2004-10-27T03:09:58Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Could somebody with enough knowledge about the core.layout part of the gecko engine point the rest \nof us to a document or something, that exlains the difficulty with implementing display:inline-block?\n\nAren't there already some elements that behave so similar (button, fieldset), that a proper \nimplementation of display:inline-block seems achievable?",
            "creator": "aljoscha@weisshuhn.de",
            "timestamp": "2004-10-27T10:15:07Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Please fix this bug, it's crucial for web apps and it works (almost) perfectly\nin IE (no support in DIVs, yes support in SPAN and A).  If we want\nFirefox/Mozilla to deliver on its promise this bug should not be allowed to be\nalive for 5 years.\n",
            "creator": "acr@cs.stanford.edu",
            "timestamp": "2004-11-18T07:18:33Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Test case: \nhttp://yansanmo.no-ip.org:8080/test/css/display_inline-block.utf8.htm \n \nDisplay in Konqueror: \nhttp://yansanmo.no-ip.org:8080/test/css/display_inline-block.khtml.png ",
            "creator": "yan.morin@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2004-12-14T20:18:31Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I think this bug needs to be changed from enchantment to normal. Firefox is\nsupposed to support CSS2.1 for starters. And this is also a CSS attribute that\nwould be very useful because it's implementation would reduce the need to use\nhackish techniques such as using the float attribute to create tabbed interfaces\nand other similar items.",
            "creator": "mozilla@soupisgoodfood.net",
            "timestamp": "2004-12-20T17:12:03Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "As much as I enjoy using this bug to knock haughty firefox fanatics down a few \npegs, I would much rather be able to use inline-block while coding. How about \na status report, if nothing else?",
            "creator": "magnusrk+bugzilla@pvv.org",
            "timestamp": "2005-03-01T23:20:56Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Can anyone comment if this is fixable in the Firefox 1.1 timeframe? We have a\nload of other new CSS features, and probably over two months for regression\nchecking. This is my only main gripe with Firefox/Mozilla's current level of CSS\nsupport. The hackarounds necessary are up there with the solutions for some of\nIE's hideous CSS problems.",
            "creator": "bugzilla@basson.at",
            "timestamp": "2005-03-07T01:44:57Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "It's not (correctly, at least).",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2005-03-07T02:01:36Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I know nothing of the layout engine, but I still think this should be an easy\nfix. An image is similar to a block element, as in, it's not text. Yet images\nare already in-line by default and behave according to the specs.\nIs treating a block element really that much more different than an image? Is it\nto do with size calculation?",
            "creator": "mozilla@soupisgoodfood.net",
            "timestamp": "2005-03-07T05:58:13Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Asa Dotzler <asa@mozilla.org> has denied Steve England\n<steve.england@gmail.com>'s request for blocking1.8b2: Bug 9458: Implement\ninline-block in layout. 9th April 2005. I guess re-requesting blocking isn't\ngoing to achieve anything.",
            "creator": "steve.england@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2005-04-11T18:05:58Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Note to self (on the off chance that I'll ever even see it in between all the\ncomments on this bug that don't belong here):\n\nIn addition to being careful about shrink wrapping (which is the main reason\nthis hasn't been done yet), we also need to be careful about getting z-ordering\nright (NS_FRAME_PAINT_LAYER_* stuff).  See http://www.w3.org/TR/CSS21/zindex.html .",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2005-04-14T08:16:08Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 298384 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "peter.vanderwoude@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2005-06-21T20:15:46Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 299276 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "elmar.ludwig@uos.de",
            "timestamp": "2005-06-30T19:00:32Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "see comment 53, not fixable in this timeframe, moving on",
            "creator": "mconnor@mozilla.com",
            "timestamp": "2005-07-11T18:10:21Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 301072 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "martijn.martijn@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2005-07-17T07:33:48Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 302637 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "bugzilla@spray.se",
            "timestamp": "2005-07-29T14:39:16Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "just faked a tabulation class using the -moz-inline-box hack thus\n\nspan.tab\n{\n\t\tdisplay: -moz-inline-box;\n\t\tdisplay: inline-block;\n\t\twidth:\t150px;\n}\n\nin html\n\n<span class=\"tab\">zeroth tab</span><spn class=\"tab\">first tab</span><spn\nclass=\"tab\">second tab</span>\n\nworks fine in opera,netscape,ie5,ie6 and firefox. though i havent attempted a \npixel matching test, nor do i plan to. otherwise surely if there's a class that\nemulates it already all you have to do is a string replace!?\n",
            "creator": "me@cycloid.f9.co.uk",
            "timestamp": "2005-08-09T13:39:20Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "-moz-inline-box is very different from inline-block.  -moz-inline-block is more\nsimilar and less likely to cause problems in the future.",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2005-08-09T16:13:34Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "If you do a pixel matching test, you will find that just using a width is not\npossible. In terms of height, padding, wrapping etc. spans behave much\ndifferently to blocks. I've already tried using spans with padding etc. to\nsimulate in-line blocks, but have always found problems in different browsers.",
            "creator": "mozilla@soupisgoodfood.net",
            "timestamp": "2005-08-09T18:23:58Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "(In reply to comment #63)\n> -moz-inline-box is very different from inline-block.  -moz-inline-block is more\n> similar and less likely to cause problems in the future.\n\ntried -block but it inserts a carriage return after it, ergo: not inline\n\n",
            "creator": "me@cycloid.f9.co.uk",
            "timestamp": "2005-08-10T11:00:50Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 304681 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "uriber@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2005-08-15T17:25:41Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "For god's sake, please fix this NOW!  This bug actually has fan sites.  Firefox is notorious as being the ONE BROWSER unable to perform this simple function.\nhttp://www.bigtrouble.com/inline_block.htm",
            "creator": "spagmoid@yahoo.com",
            "timestamp": "2005-12-02T12:48:32Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Since this is the single most important RFE this should realy be checked in ASAP...\nAFAIK this bug is dependent on the reflow changes dbaron is working on since more than a year, which is not quite ready, right?\nBut it sounds better to throw in a 80% finished patch and let a majority of people sqeeze out the last 20% of bugs generated by the patch instead of letting one single man complete this patch to 95% before checkin, which could take another year...\nAnyone wants to give this bug a blocking1.9a1+ ?\njust my 2 cents... and please dont burn me alive for moaning so much :D",
            "creator": "arpad.borsos@googlemail.com",
            "timestamp": "2005-12-02T15:11:28Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "(In reply to comment #68)\n> Since this is the single most important RFE this should realy be checked in\n> ASAP...\n\nIn Open Source communities, such demands sound rude. Please, consider never again writing them.\n\n> Anyone wants to give this bug a blocking1.9a1+ ?\n\nI doubt so. There is no patch nor any developer agreed to track the task. Dbaron said he don't know how long it'll take him, and if you think you can handle, go on, write down your proposal, with patches if possible.\n\n> just my 2 cents...\n\nIf not, consider making a better use of your 2 cents, without rude demands and absolutely useless comments like those two above. This bug, like any other is not the place where people can share their frustrations and describe the reasons for why they so much want the bug to be fixed. Thank you for not replaing in this bug anymore if you don't have a patch proposal or other value to add. (my email is public if you want to discuss this comment)",
            "creator": "zibi@braniecki.net",
            "timestamp": "2005-12-02T15:19:28Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Guys, keep the advocacy out of this thread. It's clearly on the developer's radar, so adding more \"Fix this bug now!\" posts to it just increases the signal to noise ratio and makes it harder to find useful information in the discussion (which is the point of Bugzilla). Take the advocacy to Mozillazine. I'm also going to request that you guys please read the Bugzilla etiquitte page.\nhttps://bugzilla.mozilla.org/page.cgi?id=etiquette.html\n\nThat being said, since the next official build coming off the current trunk is looking to be version 3.0, it seems to me that we've got time to get this fixed correctly on the trunk. I'm sure David will create the necessary patch as soon as he feels it's ready and fairly regression-free. Now can we please leave discussion in this thread to useful posts only?",
            "creator": "ryanvm@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2005-12-02T15:21:14Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 327658 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "enndeakin@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2006-02-17T22:43:15Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 212291\nJavascript test for inline-block",
            "creator": "compufly@caramail.com",
            "timestamp": "2006-02-18T05:29:07Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Comment on attachment 212291\nJavascript test for inline-block\n\nThe prompt is supposed to show the content of \"display\" in Firefox\nWorking fine in MSIE 6 if you want a reference of what I'm trying to do...",
            "creator": "compufly@caramail.com",
            "timestamp": "2006-02-18T05:33:55Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Comment on attachment 212291\nJavascript test for inline-block\n\nThe prompt is supposed to show the content of \"display\" in Firefox\nWorking fine in MSIE 6 if you want a reference of what I'm trying to do...",
            "creator": "compufly@caramail.com",
            "timestamp": "2006-02-18T05:34:31Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "> The prompt is supposed to show the content of \"display\" in Firefox\n> Working fine in MSIE 6 if you want a reference of what I'm trying to do...\n\nvar divns6 = document.getElementsByTagName('tr');\n\ngetElementsByTagName: Returns a NodeList (...)\nhttp://www.w3.org/TR/2000/REC-DOM-Level-2-Core-20001113/core.html#ID-A6C9094\n\n\"The items in the NodeList are accessible via an integral index, starting from 0.\"\nhttp://www.w3.org/TR/2000/REC-DOM-Level-2-Core-20001113/core.html#ID-536297177\n\nprompt(divns6[nObjet].style.display); \n\nYour testcase is not correct. Besides, this bugfile has a testcase and is about implementing inline-block.",
            "creator": "bugzilla@gtalbot.org",
            "timestamp": "2006-02-18T15:27:30Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "So one of my main concerns was shrink-wrapping, which is now fixed thanks to bug 300030.  Also, one of the frame construction issues I was worried about was filed as bug 337426 and is now fixed on the trunk.  I still need to look into comment 56.\n\nWith all this whining about how we absolutely must implement inline-block, I assume there's already a comprehensive test suite for it.  Could somebody point me to the URL so we don't have to spend a few days duplicating the effort that went into writing it?\n\nA comprehensive test suite would cover:\n * dynamic changes to/from inline-block, to content inside of them, etc.\n * interaction with other properties (z-ordering)\n * putting various things inside of it\n * shrink-wrapping\n * any other conformance statements in CSS 2.1\nand would generally be written as closely as possible to the CSS2.1 test suite authoring guidelines.\n\n(And I really need the same for inline-table.)",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2006-12-11T22:50:46Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 248305\npatch v0.1",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2006-12-11T22:53:43Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "(In reply to comment #76)\n> With all this whining about how we absolutely must implement inline-block, I\n> assume there's already a comprehensive test suite for it.  Could somebody point\n> me to the URL so we don't have to spend a few days duplicating the effort that\n> went into writing it?\n\nNot quite a test suite but have a look at this article on alistapart: http://www.alistapart.com/articles/prettyaccessibleforms/ that gives you a good example of how it can be used and what it should do. Also, it comes with a piece of Javascript to tweak the DOM and fix the problem in Firefox so that may give you an idea of how to solve it.",
            "creator": "brunogirin@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2006-12-11T23:15:49Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "So I definitely don't need to add support for -moz-inline-table, since that was actually a parse error before; I just need to add support for inline-table, which is what the next version of the patch will have.\n\nI'm not sure whether I want to keep support for -moz-inline-block in addition to inline-block; authors who are using -moz-inline-block should generally be using inline-block as well, for other browsers, and we're better off encouraging those who aren't doing so already to do so.  So my inclination is to drop support for -moz-inline-block when adding support for inline-block.  (Good practice when using -moz-inline-block has always been \"display:-moz-inline-block;display:inline-block\".)",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2006-12-11T23:23:10Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "And it looks like nsIFrame::BuildDisplayListForChild should already handle the stacking context stuff correctly.",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2006-12-12T23:06:56Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 248456\npatch (work in progress)\n\nThis is the current state of my patch and tests.  Note that 6 of the tests fail:\n * 9458-width-1a fails because the shrink-wrapping behavior is actually incorrect, since I added aAvailableWidth to nsIFrame::ComputeSize\n * the 5 9458-zorder-* tests fail because of a vertical positioning issue that I need to figure out\n\nI haven't started testing inline-table yet, but it needs the 9458-* tests copied, plus perhaps some additional tests of anonymous box construction (although we already have one, from bug 360065.",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2006-12-13T00:26:05Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 249318\nvertical alignment testcase",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2006-12-21T00:42:20Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 252006\npatch (work in progress)",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2007-01-19T03:43:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 252022\npatch (work in progress)\n\nThis has the tests fixed.  There's still one actual failure, and that's in one of the width tests.  I think we change \"available width\" during inline reflow in ways that we shouldn't, at least not for anything other than inlines and text.",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2007-01-19T07:15:38Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 252099\npatch\n\nThis fixes the test failure by making the availableWidth munging in nsLineLayout happen only for true inlines, and also adds more tests.",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2007-01-19T22:06:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "It's worth noting that this bug also now depends on bug 163504 and bug 367247, because I've put related bug fixes to inline-block and inline-table in to those patches along with the uses.",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2007-01-26T06:21:00Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Comment on attachment 252099\npatch\n\n>diff -r 5df1530b6fe3 layout/base/nsCSSFrameConstructor.cpp\n>@@ -6378,6 +6387,7 @@ nsCSSFrameConstructor::ConstructFrameByD\n>   // XXX Ignore tables for the time being\n>   if (aDisplay->IsBlockLevel() &&\n>       aDisplay->mDisplay != NS_STYLE_DISPLAY_TABLE &&\n>+      aDisplay->mDisplay != NS_STYLE_DISPLAY_INLINE_TABLE &&\n>       aDisplay->IsScrollableOverflow() &&\n>       !propagatedScrollToViewport) {\n> \n\nMaybe that condition could be a method on nsStyleDisplay or something? E.g. part of IsScrollableOverflow()?\n\nFollowup bug if you agree.\n\nAlso a followup bug for all the NS_STYLE_DISPLAY_TABLE stuff in MathML code?  I don't know what behavior rbs wants for inline-table and all.\n\nDo we need to add NS_STYLE_DISPLAY_INLINE_TABLE in the condition in PageBreakBefore()?  Then again, inline-table is not a block-level element, but I don't see where we restrict page-break to those...\n\n>diff -r 5df1530b6fe3 layout/generic/nsFrame.cpp\n\n>@@ -3773,6 +3773,7 @@ nsFrame::IsFrameTreeTooDeep(const nsHTML\n>   // Absolute positioning causes |display->mDisplay| to be set to block,\n>   // if needed.\n>   return display->mDisplay == NS_STYLE_DISPLAY_BLOCK || \n>+         display->mDisplay == NS_STYLE_DISPLAY_INLINE_BLOCK || \n>          display->mDisplay == NS_STYLE_DISPLAY_LIST_ITEM ||\n>          display->mDisplay == NS_STYLE_DISPLAY_TABLE_CELL;\n\nHuh.  The function name in that \"@@ .... @@\" line is such a lie!\n\nShould the condition here basically be something like IsBlockInside()?\n\nThat said, nsBlockFrame overrides this function, so what are the cases when we'll hit this code with a non-nsBlockFrame that has NS_STYLE_DISPLAY_INLINE_BLOCK?\n\n> nsLineLayout.cpp\n\nWhile I was looking at this stuff, it occurs to me that nsLineLayout::TreatFrameAsBlock should probably be a method on nsStyleDisplay...\n\nI assume we want to make generated content kids of inline-block inline for now (that's what this patch does)?\n\nI didn't review the tests in detail.  Let me know if you want me to.\n\nr+sr=bzbarsky",
            "creator": "bzbarsky@mit.edu",
            "timestamp": "2007-01-27T07:30:41Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I have been building with thei patch included for a bit now and noticed that the code in nsLineLayout needs some changed due to bug 367442.\n\nmCOmputedWidth stuff.",
            "creator": "wgianopoulos@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2007-01-27T12:27:56Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I already have that fixed in my tree; it was too minor to bother commenting or including a new patch.",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2007-01-27T17:34:28Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "(though probably worth warning me about, so thanks)",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2007-01-27T17:36:40Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "(In reply to comment #87)\n> Do we need to add NS_STYLE_DISPLAY_INLINE_TABLE in the condition in\n> PageBreakBefore()?  Then again, inline-table is not a block-level element, but\n> I don't see where we restrict page-break to those...\n\nWe really should restrict it to block-level elements; if we don't, that's a bug.\n\nBut I did notice while looking into this that I should fix IsSpecialFrameReframe as follows:\n\n-    childIsBlock = display->IsBlockLevel() || IsTableRelated(display->mDisplay, PR_TRUE);\n+    childIsBlock = display->IsBlockLevel();\n\nsince anonymous table objects force an inline-table when they're within an inline (as does inline-table itself, which is IsTableRelated).\n\n> >diff -r 5df1530b6fe3 layout/generic/nsFrame.cpp\n> \n> >@@ -3773,6 +3773,7 @@ nsFrame::IsFrameTreeTooDeep(const nsHTML\n> >   // Absolute positioning causes |display->mDisplay| to be set to block,\n> >   // if needed.\n> >   return display->mDisplay == NS_STYLE_DISPLAY_BLOCK || \n> >+         display->mDisplay == NS_STYLE_DISPLAY_INLINE_BLOCK || \n> >          display->mDisplay == NS_STYLE_DISPLAY_LIST_ITEM ||\n> >          display->mDisplay == NS_STYLE_DISPLAY_TABLE_CELL;\n> \n> Huh.  The function name in that \"@@ .... @@\" line is such a lie!\n> \n> Should the condition here basically be something like IsBlockInside()?\n\nYeah, I should fix that once I land IsBlockInside in the next patch...\n\n> That said, nsBlockFrame overrides this function, so what are the cases when\n> we'll hit this code with a non-nsBlockFrame that has\n> NS_STYLE_DISPLAY_INLINE_BLOCK?\n\nProbably pretty low.  I suppose it should perhaps even just return PR_FALSE so that we don't say that something that can't be a containing block is one.\n\n> > nsLineLayout.cpp\n> \n> While I was looking at this stuff, it occurs to me that\n> nsLineLayout::TreatFrameAsBlock should probably be a method on\n> nsStyleDisplay...\n\nI'm not so sure, since it has only one caller and doesn't seem generally useful (it's a rather odd combination).\n\n> I assume we want to make generated content kids of inline-block inline for now\n> (that's what this patch does)?\n\nHrm.  No, actually.  12.1 of CSS2.1 doesn't have those restrictions anymore, so we should at least allow block inside inline-block.  I'll fix that (in nsRuleNode::ComputeDisplayData).\n\n> I didn't review the tests in detail.  Let me know if you want me to.\n\nNo need.",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2007-01-27T18:14:04Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "(In reply to comment #91)\n> (In reply to comment #87)\n> > Should the condition here basically be something like IsBlockInside()?\n> \n> Yeah, I should fix that once I land IsBlockInside in the next patch...\n> \n> > That said, nsBlockFrame overrides this function, so what are the cases when\n> > we'll hit this code with a non-nsBlockFrame that has\n> > NS_STYLE_DISPLAY_INLINE_BLOCK?\n> \n> Probably pretty low.  I suppose it should perhaps even just return PR_FALSE so\n> that we don't say that something that can't be a containing block is one.\n\nIn the patch to bug 367247 I decided to make it do the latter -- just return PR_FALSE, and add an IsContainingBlock to nsTableCellFrame.",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2007-01-27T18:26:32Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "(In reply to comment #92)\n> In the patch to bug 367247 I decided to make it do the latter -- just return\n> PR_FALSE, and add an IsContainingBlock to nsTableCellFrame.\n\nI had to back the nsFrame part of that out due to orange; probably need to add overrides on nsViewportFrame / nsHTMLFrame or something similar.\n",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2007-01-27T19:56:47Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "> Yeah, I should fix that once I land IsBlockInside in the next patch...\n\nDid this ever get a bug report?  And the MathML stuff?\n\nAlso, there's some code (or rather misleading comments) in ProcessInlineChildren() that we talked about going away:\n\n12640     // recompute allKidsInline to take into account new child frames\n12641     // XXX we DON'T do this yet because anonymous table children should\n\netc.",
            "creator": "bzbarsky@mit.edu",
            "timestamp": "2007-02-04T09:52:55Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Yeah, I haven't resolved this yet because I haven't had a chance to file all the necessary followup bugs.",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2007-02-04T19:21:46Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "(In reply to comment #87)\n> Followup bug if you agree.\n\nFiled bug 371446.\n\n> Also a followup bug for all the NS_STYLE_DISPLAY_TABLE stuff in MathML code?  I\n> don't know what behavior rbs wants for inline-table and all.\n\nFiled bug 371448.\n\n> Do we need to add NS_STYLE_DISPLAY_INLINE_TABLE in the condition in\n> PageBreakBefore()?  Then again, inline-table is not a block-level element, but\n> I don't see where we restrict page-break to those...\n\nFiled bug 371449.\n\n> >@@ -3773,6 +3773,7 @@ nsFrame::IsFrameTreeTooDeep(const nsHTML\n> >   // Absolute positioning causes |display->mDisplay| to be set to block,\n> >   // if needed.\n> >   return display->mDisplay == NS_STYLE_DISPLAY_BLOCK || \n> >+         display->mDisplay == NS_STYLE_DISPLAY_INLINE_BLOCK || \n> >          display->mDisplay == NS_STYLE_DISPLAY_LIST_ITEM ||\n> >          display->mDisplay == NS_STYLE_DISPLAY_TABLE_CELL;\n> \n> Huh.  The function name in that \"@@ .... @@\" line is such a lie!\n> \n> Should the condition here basically be something like IsBlockInside()?\n\nFiled bug 371450.\n\n> That said, nsBlockFrame overrides this function, so what are the cases when\n> we'll hit this code with a non-nsBlockFrame that has\n> NS_STYLE_DISPLAY_INLINE_BLOCK?\n\nFiled bug 371452.\n\n\nChecked in to trunk on 2007-01-27.  Marking fixed.",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2007-02-23T23:57:18Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 377003 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
