{
    "bug_id": 10016,
    "summary": "[PP] [DOGFOOD] Tooltips crash on linux",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "Mozilla M8 crashes when moving the mouse into a pulldown item in the bar on the\nbottom of the browser window. It shows some menu, without items (only the gray\nrectangle), then coredumps. It seems 100% reproducable.\n\nMessages in the xterm where M8 was started:\n\nDocument: Done (4.17 secs)\nnsWindow::WidgetToScreen\n  x = 2, y = 47\nnsWindow::WidgetToScreen\n  x = 2, y = 47\nnsWindow::WidgetToScreen\n  x = 2, y = 47\nnsWindow::WidgetToScreen\n  x = 2, y = 47\n***creating XUL popup at 2 47\nborder style is:  eBorderStyle_BorderlessTopLevel\nborder style is:  eBorderStyle_window\nnsWidget::RealizeSignal(0x8516048)\ngenerating focus event\n\nStacktrace in gdb:\n\n#0  0x4010afac in nsWebShellWindow::HandleEvent ()\n#1  0x401ae10a in nsWidget::DispatchEvent ()\n#2  0x401ae031 in nsWidget::DispatchWindowEvent ()\n#3  0x401ad5cd in nsWidget::OnResize ()\n#4  0x401abe00 in UninitKeyEvent ()\n#5  0x80e7c33 in g_main_iteration ()\n#6  0x80e7060 in g_list_length ()\n#7  0x80e74db in g_list_length ()\n#8  0x80e75f5 in g_main_iteration ()\n#9  0x808551b in gtk_main ()\n#10 0x401a3aa3 in nsAppShell::Run ()\n#11 0x4010a16a in nsAppShellService::Run ()\n#12 0x80523c6 in main ()",
            "creator": "erik@bigmama.xtdnet.nl",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-16T18:47:08Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Yeah, this happens for me too with today's build.  Some weird flashing is\nhappening on Windows but it doesn't crash.\n\nPink, David says you added a tooltip on the \"DayPlanner\" button?",
            "creator": "don@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-19T23:25:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "this is the resize event problem coming in after the tooltip has gone away that\nwe've talked about a lot. reassigning to pavlov.",
            "creator": "mikepinkerton@mac.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-20T01:47:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This looks like a dupe of bug 9223 or maybe 9451.",
            "creator": "matty_is_a_geek@fastmail.fm",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-26T02:35:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "i just closed out 9223, let's use this one as the real bug since it holds the\ncorrect stack trace (the crash resizing the tip that has closed).",
            "creator": "mikepinkerton@mac.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-26T14:56:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "cpratt...is this Linux only?  If so, please put on [PP] list",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-27T05:05:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "so this is no longer needed to fix for m9. I updated the xul to make the tooltip\nappear at the bottom right of the button (not under the mouse).\n\nHowever, if the user (in the xul) messes up and either doesn't specify the\npopupanchor attribute or sets it to \"topLeft\", it will still crash because the\ntooltip will go away too quickly. Therefore, this is still a problem, but it's\nnot critical.\n\nmoving off to m10.",
            "creator": "mikepinkerton@mac.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-06T20:41:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 9451 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "pavlov@pavlov.net",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-06T21:01:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I believe this is fixed.  I need a test case that has the mouse on top of the\ntooltip when it popsup.  this probably means tooltips need to be turned back on.",
            "creator": "pavlov@pavlov.net",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-26T07:15:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "in the overlay for the bottom toolbar (i forget the file), there is a tooltip\nwhich is aligned to the bottom right corner of the associated button. Remove the\nalignment attribute and it will come up right over the button, allowing you to\ntest.",
            "creator": "mikepinkerton@mac.com",
