{
    "bug_id": 10140,
    "summary": "captions are expanding size of tables",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "In the first three tests in the above page, captions seem to be setting the size\nof tables.  The widths of the caption and the table should instead be\nindependent.  The width property on the table is being ignored.\n\nExpected: widths of first three tests are as described\n\nActual: table is always just bigger than the caption, based on what the caption\nwidth should be.  The difference seems to be double the border width of the\ntable.\n\nTested on: viewer and apprunner, 1999-07-17, Linux.",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-19T21:18:07Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "The widths of the captions and the tables now seem to be independent in the\nlatest builds, marking it WORKSFORME.\n\nTested on apprunner, 1999073008 Linux, 1999073011 Windows 95",
            "creator": "dave532@uklinux.net",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-31T16:48:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Verified fixed.",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-15T01:15:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Reopening.  This bug has partially regressed.  The second test case in the above\npage is now wrong.  Captions are expanding the widths of tables.  See\nhttp://www.w3.org/TR/REC-CSS2/tables.html#q5 for why this is wrong.",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-08T16:27:18Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Steve, the caption frame is a block frame. In the 2nd table, the caption has a \nstyle width set and is saying that its max element size is 600px (the same as \nits desired size) which is wrong.\n\nIf, I am not mis-using the block frame class here, then this problem must surely \nbe causing a bunch of other block related problems.",
            "creator": "karnaze@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-10T16:15:51Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Please update the TFV from the current M11 state.",
            "creator": "jar@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-10T16:51:19Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "seems pretty important.  will look into this for M16.\n",
            "creator": "buster@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-10T22:01:16Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "chris: this is the bug we talked about this afternoon.  I think the block frame\nis doing the right thing returning it's CSS-specified width as its max element\nwidth.  Please investigate further.  Troy, does that sound like the right\ndefinition of \"max-element-size?\"\n",
            "creator": "buster@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-11T00:28:34Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This is fixed. There is still a problem where the caption is not honoring \nbox-sizing (so the caption will appear wider than the table) but I have a fix \nfor that and will check it in shortly.\n",
            "creator": "karnaze@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-28T23:29:12Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Verifying this bug based on the first three tables/captions displaying \ncorrectly.",
            "creator": "christinehoff4@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-07-14T20:37:00Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Pushed by ctuns@mozilla.com:\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/b7ed668ce605\n[components] Issue https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/android-components/issues/10140 - Part 1: Refactor autocomplete extension functions into ext/Login.kt\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/0c0a71772d6a\n[components] Issue https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/android-components/issues/10140 - Part 2: Make a copy of GeckoLoginDelegateWrapper as GeckoAutocompleteStorageDelegate\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/f32c05ff8f9e\n[components] Issue https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/android-components/issues/10140 - Part 3: Implement the new Autocomplete.StorageDelegate interface in GeckoAutocompleteStorageDelegate",
            "creator": "pulsebot@bmo.tld",
            "timestamp": "2024-03-18T17:54:44Z"
        }
    ]
