{
    "bug_id": 10261,
    "summary": "UpdateView() drops dirty rects",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "The UpdateView() function just returns if refresh is disabled, and doesn't\naccumulate the dirty rects and then trigger a repaint once refresh is enabled.\n\nHere's the offending code:\n\n  NS_PRECONDITION(nsnull != aView, \"null view\");\n  if (!mRefreshEnabled && 0 == mUpdateBatchCnt) {\n    return NS_OK;\n  }",
            "creator": "troy@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-21T05:08:50Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Troy and I agree we should combine the two approaches to updating we currently\nhave to accumulate updates.",
            "creator": "beard@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-22T22:50:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This probably explains why freshly created browser windows don't draw everything\ncorrectly, initially.",
            "creator": "beard@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-01T05:33:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I've fixed this by buffering the dirty regions in each view, and when\nnsViewManager::EnableRefresh() is called passing the regions to\nnsIWidget::Invalidate() for each view. I've coopted nsIView's SetDirtyRegion/\nGetDirtyRegion calls for this task. I added the ProcessPendingUpdates method to\nnsViewManager to do the recursive invalidates. Checked in as nsViewManager,3.115\nand nsViewManager.h,3.38.",
            "creator": "beard@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-03T02:34:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Based on Beard's comments, marking verified fixed in the Sept 9th build.",
            "creator": "chrispetersen@mac.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-10T17:20:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Pushed by ctuns@mozilla.com:\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/10571b4c69fb\n[fenix] For https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/issues/10261: PWA Telemetry (https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/pull/11859)",
            "creator": "pulsebot@bmo.tld",
            "timestamp": "2024-03-18T18:32:52Z"
        }
    ]
}

