{
    "bug_id": 9897,
    "summary": "NECKO: Download TGZ file: No selection dialog appears, loaded as ASCII data",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "Apprunner Build ID: 1999070614\n\n(The build was downloaded from today's new 1999-07-14-08-M8 directory... yet the\ndate of the application is labeled as above. Who may parse?)\n\nUnlike the arrogant, superior Enforcer 5.0, the beast does not generate a file\n\"Save As...\" dialog upon click-selecting \"cookiecutter-0.1.1.tgz\" (an HTTP, NOT\na FTP, link), and proceeds to straightwise process the file as ASCII data,\nloading a new page with said ASCII bytes.",
            "creator": "Crysgem@crosswinds.net",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-15T02:34:02Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "mcmullen@netscape.com (requiescat in pace) is named as the XP File Handling\nmaster... by Allah, this should be made right.",
            "creator": "Crysgem@hotmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-15T02:39:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I agree, but you should reassign mcmullen bugs to don@netscape.com, who manages\nthe group to which John belonged.  Did some who2bug page mislead you to give\nthis to me?\n\n/be",
            "creator": "brendan-obsolete@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-15T02:53:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Bill, who should get this bug?",
            "creator": "don@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-19T23:42:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This bug might should be re-assigned to the webmaster at www.qis.net :-).  It\nappears that this URL has mime type text/plain, so the browser is naively\naccepting that.\n\nI believe that other browsers might presume they know more and intuit that URLs\nwith \"extensions\" like \".tgz\" might really be something else.\n\nIf one adhered to that philosophy, then it's a matter for the netlib code, I\nsuspect.  I'm reassigning to that component.",
            "creator": "law@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-20T18:45:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Changing all Networking Library/Browser bugs to Networking-Core component for\nBrowser.\n\nOccasionally, Bugzilla will burp and cause Verified bugs to reopen when I do\nthis in a bulk change.  If this happens, I will fix. ;-)",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-20T19:14:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "May have dependency on the MIME table (Jud?) Please check with Necko.",
            "creator": "gagan@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-25T23:47:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "if the MIME-table can't find a content type (currently it won't becase TGZ\nisn't regsitered) for a file extension, the app needs to decide what to do (this\nis based on context); such as throw a save as dialog.",
            "creator": "jud@me.dium.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-26T15:35:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Back to you don...",
            "creator": "gagan@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-03T08:28:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 11120 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "rhp@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-05T04:51:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "<added myself to the cc: list so that I can be reminded to check the mail case\nspecified in bug 11120 when this bug gets marked fixed.>",
            "creator": "lchiang@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-05T06:22:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Resetting QA Contact",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-31T04:36:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "It looks like this bug was mistakenly assigned to the OJI area.  I don't see\nany mention of OJI or Java in the bug history, so I'm making my best guess and\nre-assigning to the Necko area, which *is* mentioned in the bug report.",
            "creator": "drapeau@eng.sun.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-04T02:09:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Radha, we'll need to fix this when the URL dispatching/MIME handling stuff is\nready.",
            "creator": "don@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-21T21:49:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Bulk move of all Necko (to be deleted component) bugs to new Networking\n\ncomponent.",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-14T00:45:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Not a dogfood requirement",
            "creator": "radha@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-17T21:42:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "setting shrir as qa contact\n\nI actually don't know what the behavior should be, i.e. what takes precedence,\nmime-type or extension. This URL doesn't exist anymore, however.",
            "creator": "paulmac@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-12T03:39:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This has to do with the uriloader. Don't see a component for that. Passing to \nmscott for further evaluation.",
            "creator": "radha@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-05-11T21:29:57Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Putting on [nsbeta2-] radar for beta2 fix.   Seems like a weird edgecase.",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-05-23T22:46:50Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Not nominated for beta2 so pushing out.\n",
            "creator": "mscott@mozilla.org",
            "timestamp": "2000-05-24T22:59:11Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Not a beta3 bug. helper app (w/ save as dialog) is working for the basic cases\nnow.  Also, the URL is now invalid.....",
            "creator": "mscott@mozilla.org",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-10T23:26:17Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Is this still a problem?  I am able to download .tgz files without any problems\nin current builds.  ",
            "creator": "asa@piercedotzler.com",
            "timestamp": "2001-03-13T23:06:24Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Four months without any comments...  I haven't had any trouble downloading .tgz\nfiles either, and the URL mentioned in the bug is a 404.  Mark as WORKSFORME?\n",
            "creator": "caustin@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2001-07-27T04:09:22Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "test url is dead..but yeah I can download tgz file with no problm. WfM",
            "creator": "shrir@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2001-08-23T00:16:14Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "v",
            "creator": "shrir@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2001-08-23T00:16:22Z"
        }
    ]
}

{
    "bug_id": 10037,
    "summary": "Install.exe does not run if COMCTL32.DLL version is 4.0 in Win95",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "Tested 7-16 Win32 build.\n\nInstall.exe does not run under Win95 (4.00.950 and 4.00.950A).\nWin95 (4.00.950 and 4.00.950A) has COMCTL32.DLL 4.00 version.\n\nWhen you click on Install.exe, the error \"The SETUP.EXE file is linked to missing export\nCOMCTL32.DLL: InitCommon ControlsEX.\" message shows up.  Install.exe cannot be run.\n\nI checked the version of COMCTL32.DLL is 4.00.\nI checked this on the different machines.  INSTALL.EXE runs with COMCTL32.DLL version 4.7.\nIt seems that Windows 95 service pack 2 or better has this file.\n\nhttp://client/seamonkey/prd/seamonkey_platforms.htm\ndoes not say which Windows 95 service pack supports.",
            "creator": "teruko@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-17T00:05:11Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I have already updated the install code to not need comctl32.dll anymore.  I\nwill check it in along with other features when I'm done.",
            "creator": "ssu0262@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-26T20:31:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "fix is checked in.",
            "creator": "ssu0262@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-27T22:22:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Teruko,\nWill you verify this?  I have the correct version of comctl32.dll on my machines\nand cannot reproduce.\n\nthanks,\nGrace",
            "creator": "agracebush@netscape.net",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-28T16:04:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Changed QA contact to teruko@netscape.com.  Today's build (7-28-09) did not get this fix.\nI will verify this in next build.",
            "creator": "teruko@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-28T21:22:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I verified this in 7-29-08 Win32 build.",
            "creator": "teruko@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-29T18:51:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Updating component from Install Wizard to Installer",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-08T22:57:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Pushed by ctuns@mozilla.com:\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/52afc4b24dd2\n[components] For https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/android-components/issues/10037: Adjust BrowserMenuImageTextCheckboxButton item to fit UX specs.",
            "creator": "pulsebot@bmo.tld",
            "timestamp": "2024-03-18T17:53:56Z"
        }
    ]
}

{
    "bug_id": 10050,
    "summary": "File download non-functional: Win98",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "M8 Apprunner. Pretty-pretty dialog boxes appear. Pretty-pretty dialog boxes\n(\"Unknown File Type\", native Windows \"Save File\", \"Saving File\") function.\n\nNo file is however saved on disk... oh no.\n\n* Expected Results:\n\n*Grumble*... known issue, see Bug 6141... *grumble*... await the swallowing of\nNecko.\n\nI shall indeed do so, tracking the status of this functionality *on MICROSOFT\nWINDOWS 98* (Bug 6141 speaks only of Linux) via this report.",
            "creator": "Crysgem@crosswinds.net",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-17T06:56:44Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "As of the 1999072108 Apprunner, the beast makes no pretense of initiating a file\noperation. No network request is sent (tested by terminating the\nnetwork connection, which in all other known cases causes a Dial-Up Connection\ndialog to appear). This may be a seperate bug, as I conceive to recall notable\nbytetraffic and progress window feedback when this report was first filed; but\nuntil this latest issue is resolved, the initial (seperate?) bug cannot be\ntested. If necessary, I will file a seperate bug.",
            "creator": "Crysgem@hotmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-22T02:01:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "crysgem..could this be a dup of 5854 or 6141?",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-23T00:05:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Bug 6141 concerns a [CRASH] at the House FTP machine; no crash is here reported\nor was witnessed. If this bug is related to Bug 5854, the root cause of both is\na Secret of the Universe, and astronomy professors everywhere will fight each\nother for it.\nAs stated, this report is referent to a total failure to even attempt to\ninitiate a file operation. No behavior so dismal was noted at the bugs in\nconsideration.",
            "creator": "Crysgem@hotmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-23T07:00:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "The 1999080312 Apprunner build, despite it's stonily silent dialogs, performs\nthe download.\nResolving--Fixed.",
            "creator": "Crysgem@hotmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-04T02:16:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "since reporter marked fixed -- marking verified",
            "creator": "rubydoo123@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-06T04:37:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Pushed by ctuns@mozilla.com:\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/59d736323151\n[components] Close https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/android-components/issues/10050: Upstream AbstractBinding from consuming applications",
            "creator": "pulsebot@bmo.tld",
            "timestamp": "2024-03-18T17:54:40Z"
        }
    ]
}

{
    "bug_id": 10180,
    "summary": "[PP]CompareVersion is not implemented",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "CompareVersion is not implemented.  This is needed for feature complete.  This\nalso blocks the feature complete of the Software Notifier.",
            "creator": "doug.turner@gmail.com",
