{
    "bug_id": 10205,
    "summary": "Progress cancel button doesn't work",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "See nsInstallProgressDialog::GetCancelStatus(PRBool *_retval).",
            "creator": "doug.turner@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-20T15:09:00Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "moving to m10",
            "creator": "doug.turner@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-22T19:35:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Setting Priority and Serverity per Jan's email.",
            "creator": "doug.turner@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-23T17:07:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Polling the dialog is probably not the way we want to do it, thus we would\nremove this function entirely.  One alternative is to implement an\nnsIDOMDocumentObserver to call us when something has changed (but it might call\nus everytime *we* changed the dlg, which would be bad!), or pass in our own\ninterface purely for use by the cancel button.",
            "creator": "dveditz@mozilla.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-23T21:04:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "reassign to Dan, per today's meeting.",
            "creator": "cathleennscp@netscape.net",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-24T00:06:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Samir is now working on this. nsXPInstallManager needs to support a private\n(nsPIXPI..) interface that allows the dialog to poke the cancel value into the\nmanager. The manager should then stop the downloads if we're in that phase\n(send errors to Necko?) and if during an install should send signals back to\nthe install script (via the notifier functions?).",
            "creator": "dveditz@mozilla.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-02T00:51:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Pushing this out since new dialog is not in",
            "creator": "dveditz@mozilla.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-06T22:50:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Bulk move of XPInstall (component to be deleted) bugs to Installer: XPInstall\nEngine",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-08T23:28:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Fix should surface in today's builds.\n\nYou can cancel during download. Once teh download phase completes and the\ninstall phase starts the cancel button is disabled. This is a design decision to\naccomodate multitriggers.",
            "creator": "samir_bugzilla@yahoo.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-22T19:08:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Verified in build 1999122023.",
            "creator": "pawyskoczka@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-22T22:58:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Sorry, made a mistake and verified the wrong bug.",
            "creator": "pawyskoczka@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-22T23:00:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Ummm, like I marked this RESOLVED/FIXED earlier today.",
            "creator": "samir_bugzilla@yahoo.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-22T23:27:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Build 2000-01-03-09-M13(WIN), 2000-01-03-08-M13(MAC), 2000-01-03-08-M13(LINUX)\n\nCancel button automatically appears disabled from progress dialog for all\nplatforms.",
            "creator": "jimmykenlee@yahoo.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-03T22:55:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Per my comment you can only cancel during download, not during install. You need\nto download something large. The cancel button will be enabled during download.\nAs soon as extraction of files begins the cancel button is disabled. This is by\ndesign: during a multitrigger, say of a.xpi, b.xpi, and c.xpi, respectively,\nonce a.xpi upgrades software package a, and you are in the middle of b.xpi, if\nyou cancel during install there is no way to revert the upgrade action for\na.xpi. Thus, our design decision after some deliberation was to disable\nteh cancel button once extraction begins.\n\nResolving bug as fixed again.",
            "creator": "samir_bugzilla@yahoo.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-03T23:24:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Note that the dialog heading will change from \"Downloading\" to \"Installing\" at\nthe point where the cancel button becomes inoperable in the future, to signal\nthe change in state. We will review this with the UE guys, perhaps the cancel\nbutton needs to disappear rather than get disabled.",
            "creator": "dveditz@mozilla.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-03T23:43:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Build 2000-01-03-09-M13(WIN), 2000-01-03-08-M13(MAC), 2000-01-03-08-M13(LINUX)\n\nUh, yeah.  It's working.",
            "creator": "jimmykenlee@yahoo.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-04T00:04:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Pushed by ctuns@mozilla.com:\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/6b0dbe96136c\n[components] Issue https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/android-components/issues/10205: Add support for select credit card prompt",
            "creator": "pulsebot@bmo.tld",
            "timestamp": "2024-03-18T17:54:51Z"
        }
    ]
}

{
    "bug_id": 10207,
    "summary": "vertical-align: baseline not implemented for table cells",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "vertical-align: baseline is not yet working on tables.  Test case to be\nattached.  Also see bug 2886 for other examples, except you can't see the\ndifference there...",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-20T17:51:33Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 944\ntestcase.",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-20T17:52:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Note that you should be sure the testcase works with the window very narrow so\nthe cells carry to multiple lines.  Probably, more complicated testcases are\nneeded.\n\nAlso, the rules governing this weren't formally given until CSS2, even though\nthe properties existed in CSS1.  So this isn't technically a CSS1 bug.",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-20T17:54:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Marking [TESTCASE].",
            "creator": "run2000@geocities.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-25T06:58:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Many further tests for this are in\nhttp://www.fas.harvard.edu/~dbaron/css/test/sec170503 (which crashes in builds\nbefore (and possibly including) the August 10 build).\n\nThis page also tests that the values 'sub', 'super', 'text-top', 'text-bottom'\n(see CSS2 17.5.3) and length and percentage values (see\nhttp://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/www-style/1999Jul/0083.html ) should be\ntreated as baseline, not top as they are currently treated.  Once 'baseline' is\nimplemented, this is trivial to fix.",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-10T21:12:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Bug 2886 (for which the fix is attached) also causes problems on the above test\npage.",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-13T16:21:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "mass move to m14.",
            "creator": "karnaze@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-01T21:21:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This bug is currently a severe hindrance to the progress of MathML. That's why\nI have increased the severity to critical. By default, all MathML alignments \ninvolve the baseline. Expressions are difficult do decipher if their alignments \nare wrong. Moreover, we cannot properly layout matrices, arrays, commutative \ndiagrams and such.\n\nChris, I don't know when you were planning to address this bug. If it is not \nin your \"urgent\" list, I would really like to start helping to get it fixed.\nIf you provide me with some directions as to where to look at, I could try\nto investigative further. Please help.\n\nWhat is needed:\n- each cell should cache its ascent (presently, they don't cache their ascent)\n- each row should cache the max-ascent amongst all cells which have \nvertical-align: baseline (presently each row is only caching the max height\nof cells).\n\nFrom my reading of the code, it is not trivial to get the ascent out of the \ninnards of layout. Acccording to CSS, the \"ascent\" of the cell should be the \nascent of the first linebox on that cell. But this information seems to be\nlost in the entrails of layout.\n\nPS: I will probably submit other issues to your consideration later on. But\nfor now, this is the most urgent thing that the MathML effort needs help for. ",
            "creator": "rbs@maths.uq.edu.au",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-21T04:52:49Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "The stumbling block is that the nsTableCellFrame code has no way to know the \nascent of its content. Layout doesn't seem to care about this information. If it\nis possible to export that information when the table row code is reflowing its\nchildren, then the cell can cache its ascent and the table row code can later\npass the max of the ascents when it is doing VerticallyAlignChild().",
            "creator": "rbs@maths.uq.edu.au",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-21T06:01:58Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "rbs, I've asked the folks who are working on the block code how to get the \nbaseline of the table cell's block. If it isn't being set, I'm hoping it won't \nbe difficult for the block code to set it, since lines understand how to align \ntext on baselines and the block's baseline should just be the baseline of its \nfirst line.",
            "creator": "karnaze@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-21T06:33:51Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Apparently, the block code is not yet setting the ascent. Printing aDesiredSize \nin the table cell code gives invariably zero for the descent. But indeed, if the \nblock code properly set the ascent, then getting the vertical-align on the \nbaseline should be fine.",
            "creator": "rbs@maths.uq.edu.au",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-21T07:08:09Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Troy said that ascent of the block should be the baseline. In the following \nhtml, the ascent of the cell's block during reflow is always equal to its \ndesired height. Reassigning to Kipp and CCing the block busters (pun intended, \nSteve).\n\n<table border width=100>\n <tr>\n  <td>some wrapped text some wrapped text some wrapped text some</td>\n </tr>\n</table> \n",
            "creator": "karnaze@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-21T16:19:52Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Bulk moving [testcase] code to new testcase keyword. Sorry for the spam!",
            "creator": "ekrock@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-21T21:49:23Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Yes, Chris. Agreed. The ascent is (presently) always set to the height (and \nthat's why the descent is zero). ",
            "creator": "rbs@maths.uq.edu.au",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-22T01:53:51Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Block folks, any comments/good news? Is this a demaning job for you?",
            "creator": "rbs@maths.uq.edu.au",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-24T06:34:58Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Fixing this will require that the block frame cache the first line's \"ascent\" \ninformation, because when doing an incremental reflow we'll need to recover that \ninformation.\n\nIt's not a large job, but it's a days worth of work, and I know Steve has more \nurgent things to deal with like the compatibility problem with <FONT size=1> \nproblem. Nisheeth is working on finishing up reflow command coalescing",
            "creator": "troy@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-24T21:22:49Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "As MathML QA, I'm switching from critical to blocker, since it is blocking \nMathML work. As CSS QA, I'm flagging this as CSS2 compliance. \n\nI'm also marking this 4xp as IE5 does this correctly (!).\n",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-31T13:39:45Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "adding beta1 keyword to potential beta blockers",
            "creator": "buster@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-31T17:31:57Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Removing beta1 keyword. Come on guys, this is not a beta1 blocker. We have \nhundreds of bugs, real compatibility issues to resolve, and enough performance \nissues to keep us all busy for many months",
            "creator": "troy@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-31T21:16:26Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "here's the deal:  as I grovel through the block/inline reflow code, I'll keep \nthis in mind. If it just falls out, I'll do it.  But I can't commit to it until \nM16.  I haven't been working with the code long enough to know just how big this \njob might become.  Sorry to be vague, but it's all I can offer today.  If \nsomeone else is interested in working on this, I'd be happy to guide them as \nbest I can.",
            "creator": "buster@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-31T21:38:39Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Making summary clearer.",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "2000-02-20T21:38:52Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "mine! mine mine mine!  all mine!  whoo-hoo!",
            "creator": "buster@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-03-04T00:06:45Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 32436 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "jrgmorrison@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-03-20T00:40:50Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "sorry, there's no way I can get this in for M16.  Hoping for M16",
            "creator": "buster@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-05-08T22:56:01Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "OK Steve, I can see that there is a lot of pressure in the air...\n\nI have now managed to get the ascent of the first line, and it gets\npropagated quite well out of the block reflow operation up into the table-cell.\nIt has turned that it is no necessary to worry about incremental reflows since\nthe first line is either clean (in which case the ascent doesn't change),\nor it is dirty (in which case it is reflowed anyway so that the ascent\nis recomputed by the reflow code).\n\nI am attaching the patch. There is one thing that is still unclear\nto me regarding what the code is doing when there is these line-height and\nmin/max values. Perhaps, the CSS experts (David and Ian) would have more \ninsights as to what to do?\n\nThe other part in the table-cell is a bit circonvoluted since the\nbaseline can change the height of the cell... I am not yet done with that\ntable-cell part yet.\n",
            "creator": "rbs@maths.uq.edu.au",
            "timestamp": "2000-05-10T09:06:07Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 8509\nDiff to export the baseline out of the block frame code",
            "creator": "rbs@maths.uq.edu.au",
            "timestamp": "2000-05-10T09:07:53Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 8577\nTescase examples of 'vertical-align:baseline' in table cells",
            "creator": "rbs@maths.uq.edu.au",
            "timestamp": "2000-05-12T02:50:57Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Just attached a screenshot of what I got so far. Recovering state\nfor incremental reflow and the fact that a rowgroup can fire ReflowCellFrame() \nare not yet tuned up.\n\n[The ascent should stay the same, no matter what happens when applying the \nline-height and min-max values to the block frame, right? In this case,\neveything is fine with the block frame code then.]",
            "creator": "rbs@maths.uq.edu.au",
            "timestamp": "2000-05-12T03:01:33Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 9321\nDiff to support 'vertical-align: baseline' in the table code",
            "creator": "rbs@maths.uq.edu.au",
            "timestamp": "2000-05-30T13:09:45Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "While testing the testcase attached on bug 32436, I have observed that the\ndiff that I attached for the block code doesn't take care of special cases\nwhere the code path executed by the block code does not involve\nVerticalAlignFrames(). This happens, for example, when the first child\nof <td> is a block, as in <td><div>...</div></td>.\n\nI have made a further change to test the case where mLines->IsBlock(),\nand fetch the ascent of mLines->mFisrtChild. Unfortunately, this still\ndoesn't fix the problem. Any clues as to remaining missing link? I will\nbe attaching a screenshot to demonstrate the problem.",
            "creator": "rbs@maths.uq.edu.au",
            "timestamp": "2000-05-30T13:26:03Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 9322\nDiff with change to fetch the ascent of mLines->mFirstChild",
            "creator": "rbs@maths.uq.edu.au",
            "timestamp": "2000-05-30T13:30:18Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 9323\nTestcase with rowspans blocks inside <td>",
            "creator": "rbs@maths.uq.edu.au",
            "timestamp": "2000-05-30T13:35:10Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 9325\nScreenshot: rendering of the testcase",
            "creator": "rbs@maths.uq.edu.au",
            "timestamp": "2000-05-30T14:00:04Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Adding chris to the Cc list so that he may have a look at the table code.\n(I used cvs diff -u10 to produce a wider context and have kept everything\nin #ifdef MOZ_MATHML for now to ease development/identification).\n",
            "creator": "rbs@maths.uq.edu.au",
            "timestamp": "2000-05-30T14:07:04Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Checked-in",
            "creator": "rbs@maths.uq.edu.au",
            "timestamp": "2000-06-05T08:38:09Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Note: Although the code was reviewed by buster and karnaze, it is still in \n#ifdef MOZ_MATHML and so 'vertical-align: baseline' is still not available for\nnormal HTML documents, pending QA after M16.\n",
            "creator": "rbs@maths.uq.edu.au",
            "timestamp": "2000-06-05T08:54:43Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I suggest we check this in as soon as beta2 ships",
            "creator": "buster@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-06-16T22:10:56Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Pursuing further the issue I mentioned on 2000-05-30 06:26, I have observed\nthat the problem is due to the fact that the dectection of the case where the\nfirst child of <td> is a block was insufficient.\n\nIf on the test case, I remove all the whitespace/blank-lines before <div>,\ni.e, if \n\n<td> \n  <div> ... </div>\n</td>\n\nbecomes\n\n<td><div>\n       ... </div>\n</td>\n\nthen the code works as expected. I will try to attach a screenshot if I can.\n(On the screenshot, all the <td><div>...</div></td> are represented\nby red rectangles inside green rectangles. Of note is the fact the\nbaselines from inside the red <div>s are aligned properly.)\n\nTherefore, it is not enough to just check\n\n+    if (mLines && mLines->mFirstChild && mLines->IsBlock()) {\n\nbecause the real first line may be something else.",
            "creator": "rbs@maths.uq.edu.au",
            "timestamp": "2000-06-21T10:02:06Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 10448\nScreenshot after removing the whitespace between <td> and <div>",
            "creator": "rbs@maths.uq.edu.au",
            "timestamp": "2000-06-21T10:09:56Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Index: nsBlockFrame.cpp\n===================================================================\nRCS file: /cvsroot/mozilla/layout/html/base/src/nsBlockFrame.cpp,v\nretrieving revision 3.389\ndiff -u -r3.389 nsBlockFrame.cpp\n--- nsBlockFrame.cpp\t2000/06/14 23:15:58\t3.389\n+++ nsBlockFrame.cpp\t2000/06/22 06:20:50\n@@ -2330,11 +2330,20 @@\n     aMetrics.ascent = aMetrics.height;\n     aMetrics.descent = 0;\n #else\n-    if (mLines && mLines->mFirstChild && mLines->IsBlock()) {\n-      // mAscent is not yet set because we didn't call VerticalAlignFrames()\n-      // on mLines. So we need to fetch the ascent of the first child of mLines\n+    // Need to check for special cases where mAscent is not yet properly set.\n+    // There are two cases to consider: when the first line is a block, or\n+    // when the first line is empty and is followed by a second line that\n+    // is a block (e.g., <td>\\n<div>). In these two cases, we need to fetch\n+    // the ascent of the first child of the line.\n+    nsLineBox* line = mLines;\n+    // see if this first line is empty. if so, move on to the second line\n+    if (line && (0 == line->GetHeight())) {\n+      line = line->mNext;\n+    }\n+    // see if the line contains a block. if so, fetch the ascent of the block\n+    if (line && line->mFirstChild && line->IsBlock()) {\n       nsBlockFrame* bf;\n-      nsresult res = mLines->mFirstChild->QueryInterface(kBlockFrameCID, \n(void**)&bf);\n+      nsresult res = line->mFirstChild->QueryInterface(kBlockFrameCID, \n(void**)&bf);\n       if (NS_SUCCEEDED(res) && bf) {\n         mAscent = bf->GetAscent();\n       }\n\nChange to account for the special cases.\nNeed to fill r=? before heading to waterson!",
            "creator": "rbs@maths.uq.edu.au",
            "timestamp": "2000-06-22T06:26:09Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Do you want to initialize mAscent to 0 in case there are no lines?  Or is it \nsomehow set correctly already (in PlaceLine?)?  Also, do you want to change the \nway mAscent is set in nsBlockFrame::PlaceLine to correspond to these changes?  \n(Also, I assume the comment you removed about VerticalAlignFrames() not having \nbeen called was wrong, since you have to call VerticalAlignFrames before you \nknow what the ascent is.)",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2000-06-22T17:57:05Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "> Do you want to initialize mAscent to 0 in case there are no lines?  Or is it \n> somehow set correctly already (in PlaceLine?)?\nbuster, do you want to chime in here? None of the other data members of the\nblock frame (like mLines itself) are initialized. Is there a zeroing new\nsomewhere in the hierarchy? Or should I put 'mAscent = 0' in the constructor\nto account for this special case that dbaron mentions?\n\n>  Also, do you want to change the \n> way mAscent is set in nsBlockFrame::PlaceLine to correspond to these changes? \n> (Also, I assume the comment you removed about VerticalAlignFrames() not having \n> been called was wrong, since you have to call VerticalAlignFrames before you \n> know what the ascent is.)\n\nThere are some code-paths that don't lead to VerticalAlignFrames(), so the\ncomment wasn't wrong. Perhaps I should put that comment back...\nnsBlockFrame::PlaceLine() is fine. If we ever get there, that will mean\nthat mLines is not a block, so mAscent will be set properly.\nIf we don't get there (or if the first line was empty), then the\nfinal adjustments that I added will take care of setting mAscent properly.",
            "creator": "rbs@maths.uq.edu.au",
            "timestamp": "2000-06-22T21:28:50Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "> (... since you have to call VerticalAlignFrames before you \n> know what the ascent is.)\nYep, that's right. But in the case of a containing block, mAscent just\nneeds to 'bubble up'. (In this case, VerticalAlignFrames() would have called \nin the inner-most block frame for which mLines wasn't a containing block).",
            "creator": "rbs@maths.uq.edu.au",
            "timestamp": "2000-06-22T21:40:57Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "BTW, after enabling this patch, it will remain one important piece of\nthe puzzle before this bug is nailed down for HTML/CSS tables. The remaing\ncase is that of <td> <table> ... </table> </td>. This other special case (but\nfrequent case) won't work because the table code is not yet honoring the ascent.\nHence the table code still needs some further tuning so that it returns its\nascent (i.e., the ascent of its first row).\n",
            "creator": "rbs@maths.uq.edu.au",
            "timestamp": "2000-06-23T02:47:18Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "rbs, should these changes get turned on now?  (Since it looks like, from\nprevious comments, you have an r= but not an a=, adding approval keyword.)",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2000-07-27T15:03:06Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Now got a=waterson. Will check-in once I have updated my tree to the tip with\nthe latest flood of changes that have followed the branch.",
            "creator": "rbs@maths.uq.edu.au",
            "timestamp": "2000-07-28T01:40:26Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Checked-in. Code to support valign=baseline is now active in default builds.",
            "creator": "rbs@maths.uq.edu.au",
            "timestamp": "2000-07-28T09:56:22Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "dbaron, your tests with invalid length and percentage values will not work as\nyou documented because the Style System layer is filtering invalid length and\npercentage values and mapping the corresponding valign to a default or whatever\nis inherited from the parent (i.e., middle in most case).\n\nThe only invalid values that reach the table code are 'sub', 'super',\n'text-top', 'text-bottom', which the code will remap to baseline as per \nyour comments of 1999-08-10 14:12.",
            "creator": "rbs@maths.uq.edu.au",
            "timestamp": "2000-07-28T10:22:07Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "rbs:  Are you sure it's not coming through from the style system?  Isn't it just\na bug in nsTableCellFrame::VerticallyAlignChild - the \"default:\" in the case\nstatement should be the same as BASELINE instead of the same as MIDDLE, right?",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-15T16:34:26Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Yep. When I was unit-testing the code, my printfs couldn't catch length and \npercentage values and I had a quick look at the Style System (though I don't \nremember the section). In fact, the \"default:\" in the case is not effective \nbecause the verticalAlignFlags used in the switch is defaulted to BASELINE\nearlier, for any value other than top, middle, bottom. (the same goes for the\nHasVerticalAlignBaseline() function that are queried by parent frames).",
            "creator": "rbs@maths.uq.edu.au",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-15T18:20:45Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "What's the state of this bug?  According to:\nAdditional Comments From rbs@maths.uq.edu.au 2000-07-28 02:56\nsounds like a fix was checked in.\nBut it's still assigned to me and marked \"NEW\", with no nsbeta specification.\nNeed an update, please.  And thanks for carrying the torch on this while I was \nout!",
            "creator": "buster@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-28T04:14:06Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Yes the fix is in, and is gaining some maturity. So the bug can be closed.\nBut for things to work right, all frames should honor the ascent information.\nCurrently, <table> is the remaining HTML frame that is not honoring that \ninformation, and \n   <td valign=\"baseline\"> <table>...</table> </td>\ndoesn't mean anything.\n\nSo the table code should return the ascent of its first row. But this is a \ndifferent problem and should probably be filed as a separate bug. dbaron\nalso asked for clarifications about the mapping of erroneous valign values.\nThis is a separate issue (from the Style System) and the fix is not going to be\naffected.",
            "creator": "rbs@maths.uq.edu.au",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-28T08:07:58Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Verified fixed in MacOS 9.0.4 build 2000-09-04-08, Linux  2000-09-06-08, and Win \n98 2000-09-06-08.\n",
            "creator": "bugzillaabuse@lorcas.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-09-07T01:01:05Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Actually folks, I take that back.  baseline works in most places but not in <col> \nor <colgroup>.\n\nTestcase URLs:\nhttp://slip/projects/marvin/html/col_valign_baseline.html\nhttp://slip/projects/marvin/html/colgroup_valign_baseline.html\n",
            "creator": "bugzillaabuse@lorcas.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-09-26T22:32:55Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Ummm...  why *should* it work for col or colgroup?  CSS properties inherit\nthrough the document tree.",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2000-09-27T01:08:50Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This bug should be marked fixed. Valign is working but, as stated, not for COL \nand COLRGROUP (and HTML attribute for these elements). However, that problem is \nwritten up 12 bug #915.",
            "creator": "christinehoff4@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-09-27T22:27:01Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I actually ran into the problem with baseline info not propagating out of nested\ntables in a real world page yesterday. :-/\n\nIs there a bug on that issue? Chris?",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "2000-09-27T23:44:58Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "fixed, per chrid d's comment.  thanks, chris.\nthis bug is a request for support, and we support it now.  if there are bugs\nwith specific aspects of that support, please open a new bug with a focused test\ncase.\n",
            "creator": "buster@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-10-05T22:57:49Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Verified fixed.",
            "creator": "christinehoff4@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-10-06T19:32:44Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Pushed by ctuns@mozilla.com:\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/40300ddedad7\n[components] Close https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/android-components/issues/10207: Add support for private requests in Glean",
            "creator": "pulsebot@bmo.tld",
            "timestamp": "2024-03-18T17:54:36Z"
        }
    ]
}

