{
    "bug_id": 10321,
    "summary": "Using the Exit menu causes Shutdown to get called twice.",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "If you use the Exit menu to quit Messenger, every nsIAppShellComponent's\nShutdown gets called twice.  This is because the implementation of Exit and main\ncall nsAppShellService::Shutdown.  What ends up happening is that the component\ngets destroyed the first time and then gets recreated and destroyed again the\nsecond time.  It seems wasteful if it can be avoided.\n\nI've cc'd Steve and Paul because right now it looks like the XUL Overlay version\nof Exit calls EditShell::Exit.  It seems stranger to be using the Editor's\nimplementation of Exit to shutdown Messenger, for example (even if at the moment\nthey would do the same thing).  I wonder if we need some other version of Exit?",
            "creator": "scottputterman@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-22T17:54:25Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "cc'ing Simon.  Simon, please work with Paul, Don, Scott to make this right.  Is\nthis a mail-specific problem, or do we have the same problem in ender itself?",
            "creator": "buster@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-22T18:21:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Bill Law is working on the exit process, so should probably figure out what the\nbest thing is here.",
            "creator": "sfraser_bugs@smfr.org",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-22T18:27:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This is not just a Messenger problem.  It's everywhere.  I just used Messenger\nas an example because that's what I was testing.  I tried it from the Editor and\nthe components get Shutdown twice.\n\nI cc'd the editor team because I noticed that your version of Exit is getting\nused.  I just didn't think that seemed correct.",
            "creator": "scottputterman@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-22T18:28:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "The owner of this bug should feel free to modify the globalOverlay.xul in such a\n\nway as to be able to quit from any window in the application.  The current code\n\nwas copied from the messenger window's JavaScript.  This code will soon be\n\nexecuted from the browser window as well.",
            "creator": "hangas@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-22T18:52:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Bill, how bad is this really?",
            "creator": "don@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-12T08:03:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Reassigning to me since I am working on shutdown. This will be real easy to fix.",
            "creator": "davidm@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-15T07:09:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Fix checked in. Broke shutdown into the Quit ui command and the shutdown cleanup\nfunction. All quiting ( from the UI ) should use the command in globalOverlay.js",
            "creator": "davidm@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-16T23:49:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Can't verify this (developer issue); taking davidm's word for it and marking it\nverified.",
            "creator": "cpratt@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-18T18:31:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Pushed by ctuns@mozilla.com:\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/a55c8d94a5b2\n[fenix] For https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/issues/10321: Wire up play and pause buttons in tab tray (https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/pull/10422)",
            "creator": "pulsebot@bmo.tld",
            "timestamp": "2024-03-18T18:18:45Z"
        }
    ]
}

{
    "bug_id": 10342,
    "summary": "Crash when loading this page",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "When loading this URL page, Apprunner crashes.\n\nStep of reproduce\n1. Launch Apprunner\n2. Go to above URL\nApprunner crashes.\n\nTested 7-21-16-NECKO Win32 build.  This does not happen in 7-22-08-M9 Win32\nbuild.\n\nI send Talkback report. I cannot access the server now. Once I can access the\nserver, I will put the stack info in this bug report.",
            "creator": "teruko@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-22T21:42:54Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Talkback Incident 11470341\nTrigger Type:  Program Crash\n Trigger Reason:  Access violation\n\n Call Stack:    (Signature = RAPTORGFXWIN.DLL + 0xd3e7 (0x6081d3e7) bfcb6040)\n   RAPTORGFXWIN.DLL + 0xd3e7 (0x6081d3e7)\n   RAPTORGFXWIN.DLL + 0xd31b (0x6081d31b)\n   NECKO_HTTP.DLL + 0x3574 (0x60293574)\n   NECKO.DLL + 0x464d (0x6015464d)\n   NECKO.DLL + 0x4359 (0x60154359)\n   PLDS3.DLL + 0x18ee (0x607f18ee)\n   PLDS3.DLL + 0x186a (0x607f186a)\n   PLDS3.DLL + 0x1b18 (0x607f1b18)\n   KERNEL32.DLL + 0x3663 (0xbff73663)\n   KERNEL32.DLL + 0x2297c (0xbff9297c)\n   0x00638c18",
            "creator": "teruko@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-22T23:29:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I think I know whats going on here... looking into this.",
            "creator": "gagan@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-03T03:21:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "OK fix checked in.",
            "creator": "gagan@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-03T03:25:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I tested this in 8-03-09 Win32 build.   Apprunner does not crash anymore, but it does not stop loading.",
            "creator": "teruko@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-03T18:59:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 1109\nThis is the Dos Prompt console.",
            "creator": "teruko@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-03T19:03:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "If the only problem here is that the animation doesn't stop, then this is the\nsame problem that Radha and I have been battling in the doc loader.\n\nMarking as duplicate.\n\n*** This bug has been marked as a duplicate of 10335 ***",
            "creator": "warrensomebody@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-03T21:31:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "verified dup",
            "creator": "jaymoz@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-16T20:49:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Bulk move of all Necko (to be deleted component) bugs to new Networking\n\ncomponent.",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-14T00:34:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Pushed by ctuns@mozilla.com:\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/a80dd299f449\n[fenix] For https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/issues/10342 - Part 1: Remove top sites prefetch and observation of live data\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/0fc842fd2ec7\n[fenix] For https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/issues/10342 - Part 2: Replace the local TopSiteStorage with the A-C DefaultTopSiteStorage\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/a01a8298ddb5\n[fenix] For https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/issues/10342 - Part 3: Use the TopSitesUseCase in the BrowserToolbarController and SessionControlController\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/e6c328d2b326\n[fenix] For https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/issues/10342 - Part 4: Use the TopSitesFeature in the HomeFragment for displaying top sites\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/8ad60ff86871\n[fenix] For https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/issues/10342 - Part 5: Fix DefaultSessionControlControllerTest and DefaultBrowserToolbarControllerTest\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/ecb3e9da112a\n[fenix] For https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/issues/10342 - Part 6: Show \"Delete from history\" instead of \"Remove\" for top frecent sites in the top site menu\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/835f84306c1f\n[fenix] For https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/issues/10342 - Part 7: Fix TopSiteViewHolderTest and TopSiteItemViewHolderTest",
