{
    "bug_id": 6565,
    "summary": "[PP] Mac only now-Default location for cursor when opening a mail compose window is wrong",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "Using 1999051709 on win95, 1999051708 on linux, 1999051709 on mac build\n1999051708 the default loction of the cursor is wrong when a New Msg window\ncomes up.  It's in the Body should be in the Addressing field To:\n\n1. Launch messenger\n2. Click New Msg\n3. Notice the cursor is in the Body of the message, it should be in the\nAddressing field.",
            "creator": "esther@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-05-17T18:51:12Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 4469 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "bugzilla@ducarroz.org",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-02T23:29:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Update:  Using 1999060708 on Win & linux this bug has changed a little.  With\nthis build the cursor doesn't appear at all.  The user needs to click on the To:\nfield.",
            "creator": "esther@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
