        },
        {
            "text": "I'm reopening this... here are results using jul12 m8 builds on all platforms\n(html and plain text windows):\n\nLinux rh 5.2:  Compose window launches with one cursor blinking in the body of\nthe compose window.  Begin typing without clicking to change focus yields\nnothing -- no characters are typed in either addressee or body fields.\nMac OS 8.51:   same results as linux.\nNT 4.0:        Compose window launches showing two cursors flashing, one in\naddressee line and one in body.  Typing focus is actually in addressee line,\nwhich is correct, but the two blinking cursors is not correct.",
            "creator": "laurel@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-12T20:23:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I don't think we should hold m8 for this.",
            "creator": "mozilla@davidbienvenu.org",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-12T22:39:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Agreed.  I'll change to M9.",
            "creator": "lchiang@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-12T22:42:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Moving to M10.",
            "creator": "scottputterman@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-03T21:42:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Should try to fix this for PR1",
            "creator": "sol@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-13T22:57:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Fixed.",
            "creator": "bugzilla@ducarroz.org",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-31T01:13:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Using 1999100420m10 on win98 and 1999100118m10 on linux this is fixed.  However\nit is not fixed for mac 1999100120M10.  I will reopen and make it a Platform\nParity.",
            "creator": "esther@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-05T22:12:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Right, is due to bug 12991.",
