{
    "bug_id": 6647,
    "summary": "CSS2 'outline' property",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "The CSS2 outline property would allow widget focus to be drawn using\nspec compliant methods.\n\nThere is a test page here:\n   http://www.bath.ac.uk/%7Epy8ieh/internet/eviltests/outline.html\n\nSee bug 1859.",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "1999-05-18T14:01:09Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "The property data is ready for use in the style context.",
            "creator": "peterl-retired@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-05-20T19:33:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Reassigning to Pierre.",
            "creator": "karnaze@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-03T04:11:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 7291 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "peterl-retired@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-07T21:47:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Moving all Widget Set bugs, past and present, to new HTML Form Controls\ncomponent per request from karnaze.  Widget Set component will be retired\nshortly.",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-22T00:45:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This should be implemented for frames in general. It is not a form element\nspecific bug. The CSS border rendering code needs to be modified to include\nsupport for rendering the outline border.",
            "creator": "kmcclusk@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-07T00:20:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I'm leaving 3 weeks on vacation. Pushing M9 bugs to M11.",
            "creator": "pierre@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-07T18:11:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** This bug has been marked as a duplicate of 9816 ***",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-02T22:50:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Verified dup of #9816",
            "creator": "christinehoff4@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-03T22:05:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Since bug 9816 turned into the 'remove CSS2 for FCS' bug, and is already \nlittered with comments, I think we should make this the bug for FUTURE support \nof the 'outline' property.\n\nIan's comments from bug 9816 about remaining issues:\n\n1. It appears that we don't support 'dotted' and 'dashed' outline-styles at all.\n   This is wrong, IIRC we should treat them as 'solid' if we are not able to\n   actually treat them as dotted or dashed styles (BUT I MAY BE WRONG THIS NEEDS\n   TO BE CHECKED!!!).\n\n2. We do not appear to support the 'invert' outline-color.\n\n3. We have major drawing errors with inset and outset outline-styles.\n\n4. We have some odd, annoying repaint problems (as I understand it, this is\n   quite a major problem code-wise). This is bug 9809, marked Future, mostfreq.\n\n5. We interpret 'groove' and 'ridge' the wrong way round.\n\n6. We do not support outline on inline elements (the main use of outline!!!)\n\n7. We draw the outline in the wrong place (as far as I can tell?).\n\n8. According to bug 22892, we don't do 'outline' on XUL -- which I would \n   guess is one of the major uses of outline as far as we are concerned",
            "creator": "bugzilla@blakeross.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-13T18:44:28Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Taking QA per managerial policy.",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "2000-10-01T23:46:57Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 67966 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "verbal@myrealbox.com",
            "timestamp": "2001-02-17T21:29:04Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Nominating this bug for nsbeta1 on behalf of gerardok@netscape.com.",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "2001-04-27T00:08:01Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "--> Style System (which may not be correct, but this sure ain't a Form Controls bug)",
            "creator": "mpt@postinbox.com",
            "timestamp": "2001-06-04T14:49:32Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "To implement we would need to be able to draw to the outside of the frame. This\nwould require some major modifications.\nMarking nsbeta1-.",
            "creator": "kmcclusk@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2002-02-13T01:21:50Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Assigning pierre's remaining Style System-related bugs to myself.",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2002-06-20T04:06:05Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Just curious: why does -moz-outline work, but the standard outline does not?\nThey have the same effect as far as I can tell.",
            "creator": "mozilla@bakerweb.biz",
            "timestamp": "2002-08-17T03:05:24Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Jerry: The reasons are listed in comment #9. This feature is just not ready for\nthe prime time. \n\nSorry for the spam.",
            "creator": "piskozub@iopan.gda.pl",
            "timestamp": "2002-08-17T07:16:16Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "9. We don't merge outlines for inline elements correctly (bug 133165)",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2002-08-17T11:46:26Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 189464 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "croo@nm.ru",
            "timestamp": "2003-01-17T17:05:45Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Taking.",
            "creator": "roc@ocallahan.org",
            "timestamp": "2003-03-19T20:43:20Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 21354 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "roc@ocallahan.org",
            "timestamp": "2003-03-19T20:43:41Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "seems like the current -moz-outline is rendered inside the border but the web\nstandards outline property should be rendered over the border.",
            "creator": "sekundes@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2003-12-27T09:57:02Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "It's worth pointing out that this property is in the default HTML 4.0 stylesheet\n(*:focus). Hence, Moz should support it at least enough that a designer can\nmanipulate the default setting or turn it off.",
            "creator": "felipe@felipegasper.com",
            "timestamp": "2004-06-02T02:35:26Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 22892 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "aaronlev@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2004-10-26T13:24:49Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "-moz-outline-offset is now implemented\nNegative offsets are allowed",
            "creator": "aaronlev@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2004-10-26T13:57:28Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I think we're ready to turn this on with the real 'outline' name. I will write a\nstyle system patch to do that.",
            "creator": "roc@ocallahan.org",
            "timestamp": "2005-03-24T01:36:06Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "See bug 93156 for the aliasing stuff I did for -moz-opacity, which you'll want\nhere as well, I suspect.",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2005-03-24T01:45:27Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "It looks like Mats did this in bug 281972.",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2005-03-26T19:22:28Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Yep. Thanks mats!\n\n*** This bug has been marked as a duplicate of 281972 ***",
            "creator": "roc@ocallahan.org",
            "timestamp": "2005-03-26T20:51:40Z"
        }
    ]
}

{
    "bug_id": 7189,
    "summary": "Speed up RDF initialization",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "TO DO for Performance:\nWhen the code to initialize RDF gets hit.  It seems to take quite a\n  while.  Is there anything we can do to speed up RDF initialization?",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-05-27T02:05:46Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "How do we know that this is the case? Is there a Quantify trace around that\nindicates this?",
            "creator": "waterson@maubi.net",
            "timestamp": "1999-05-28T12:00:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "jevering or phillip, can we get a Quantify trace please?",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-09T16:10:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "i'd give you one if i knew how to run quantify. it's on my list of things to\nfigure out... (is there some tutorial out there i can look at?)",
            "creator": "phillip@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-09T21:38:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Moving to M8, when DP and I plan to do some focused startup performance\nanalysis.",
            "creator": "waterson@maubi.net",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-11T22:21:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Clobbering this bug. No specifics. Not useful.",
            "creator": "waterson@maubi.net",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-29T23:37:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Let's not \"bag the bug\" because we don't have enough for you yet.\n\nwaterson, I'll assign to me while I get you some quantify data, then throw back\nover to you...",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-01T01:08:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Clearing Invalid...phillip come see me regarding quantify",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-01T01:09:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I think it _is_ bogus to re-open this as a bug. We have _no evidence_ that \"RDF\ninitialization\" is a bottleneck. How do I know that? Well, there is no such\nthing as \"RDF initialization\". So this is sort of like sending somebody out to\nhunt for snipe. :)",
            "creator": "waterson@maubi.net",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-01T01:18:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This bug was given to me by jevering...jevering, do you want to mark this\nInvalid?",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-06T18:33:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "waterson,  if RDF doesn't get initialized how does it run? ;-)\n  -snipe hunter's anonymous",
            "creator": "chofmann@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-07T04:34:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "My point is, there is no \"globally initialize RDF now\" routine that gets\ncalled. Each _individual_ datasource does initialization when it gets created.\nThe RDF service creates some hashtables when it's created (but that's about\nit).",
            "creator": "waterson@maubi.net",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-07T04:40:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "moving over to dp.  if dp can find something here lets reassign\nto waterson, otherwise lets close this.",
            "creator": "chofmann@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-04T04:55:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "We have done sufficient performance analysis to rule this one out now.  The\nproblems are more registry related at this point.. closing out.  This may have\nbeen filed without fully understanding the problem (yes, from my report).",
            "creator": "jevering@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-04T05:36:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "marking verified per jevering's comments.",
            "creator": "phillip@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-04T17:56:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Pushed by ctuns@mozilla.com:\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/afe86cbaa4a0\n[fenix] Bug 7189 - Provide page title in website information dialog (https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/pull/7255)",
            "creator": "pulsebot@bmo.tld",
            "timestamp": "2024-03-18T18:15:38Z"
        }
    ]
}

