{
    "bug_id": 7297,
    "summary": "native MacOS context menus on editor toolbar include \"Help\"--why?",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "I updated my build this morning.\nGo into the editor and click any of the popup menus on the toolbar.\nNotice that the first item in the menu is \"Help\" followed by a separator.\n\nThe next time you click on a popup menu the \"Help\" item and its separator will be\ngone.",
            "creator": "brade@comcast.net",
            "timestamp": "1999-05-28T18:25:07Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Targeting M7",
            "creator": "saari@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-08T02:20:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I'll probably end up fixing this in M8",
            "creator": "saari@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-14T17:06:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I'll fix this in M8 since it isn't critical",
            "creator": "saari@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-15T21:33:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Moving all Widget Set bugs, past and present, to new HTML Form Controls\ncomponent per request from karnaze.  Widget Set component will be retired\nshortly.",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-22T00:45:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Pushing to M9 as this isn't critical",
            "creator": "saari@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-09T18:52:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "They include Help because the the Mac contextual menu manager puts that there\n\nfor you automatically.",
            "creator": "sfraser_bugs@smfr.org",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-09T18:53:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Ooops, collision. Putting M9 in there.",
            "creator": "sfraser_bugs@smfr.org",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-09T18:53:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Yeah, I know that is why Help is there, I just need to duplicate the class,\ngenerate new GUIDs and change appropriate calls.\n\nI just havn't done it yet, and I'm also waiting for some modifications Pav is\ndoing to the API to help GTK along.",
            "creator": "saari@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-09T20:47:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Non critical so I'm moving it to M10. (easy to fix, but no time)",
            "creator": "saari@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-05T21:00:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Pushing this to M11 after hyatt's rearchitecture of popups (problem should go\n\naway)",
            "creator": "saari@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-28T19:06:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "All popups will be XP for beta. Pushing past beta",
            "creator": "saari@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-11T01:55:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 8220 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "brade@comcast.net",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-14T04:51:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "mass moving m14 bugs to m15",
            "creator": "trudelle@acm.org",
            "timestamp": "1999-11-02T22:58:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "are we ever going back to native context menus? (i kinda hope so). do you want to\ncontinue owning this as it's native menu stuff?",
            "creator": "mikepinkerton@mac.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-20T04:29:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Well, we could go back, probably should. Yeah, I'll keep this one",
            "creator": "saari@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-20T04:53:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Mass moving M18 bugs to M19",
            "creator": "trudelle@acm.org",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-05T04:05:53Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "product UI completeness. nsbeta2.",
            "creator": "ekrock@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-05-21T07:08:07Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Putting on [nsbeta2-] radar. ",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-05-25T00:42:33Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "changed summary to be more percise. \n",
            "creator": "saari@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-05-25T00:50:00Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Am I understanding this bug, that it's currently a theoretical bug which will \nonly reappear when native context menus are re-enabled?\n\nIf so, it shouldn't block bug 12670, it should block bug 34572 instead.",
            "creator": "mpt@postinbox.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-13T02:34:35Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Correct, it only involves native context menus",
            "creator": "saari@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-13T19:58:26Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Right-o. Changing dependencies.\n",
            "creator": "mpt@postinbox.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-14T23:50:58Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "XPAPPs & XPToolkit are jrgm's area",
            "creator": "ckritzer@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-12-29T18:57:05Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "While I'm always willing to share my incredible wealth of knowledge \nof MacOS APIs, I think I shall give this bug back to saari.",
            "creator": "jrgmorrison@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-12-31T04:34:11Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Okay, not only am I an idiot, I'm an embarrassed idiot.\n\nSorry guys, I meant to change the QAContact, not Assigned field.",
            "creator": "ckritzer@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2001-01-02T17:55:13Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Mozilla CFM build is dead.\nhttp://groups.google.com/groups?threadm=avkj4k%24ihs2%40ripley.netscape.com",
            "creator": "francis.uy@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2003-02-09T19:09:47Z"
        }
    ]
}

{
    "bug_id": 7378,
    "summary": "Mozilla M6 for Linux mis-identifies itself",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "Netscape 4.6 for Linux identifies itself as:\n\nNetscape\n4.6 [en] (X11; I; Linux 2.2.9-19mdk i586)\n\nMozilla M6 for Linux identifies itself as\n\nNetscape\n5.0 [en] (Unix; I)\n\n\nShouldn't it identify itself as\n\n5.0 [en] (X11; I; Linux 2.2.9-19mdk i586)\n\n\nI entered a similar bug for Mozilla mis-identiying itself in Windows NT earlier,\nbut I entered this as a new bug since it's running on a different OS.",
            "creator": "rekle@yahoo.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-05-31T03:59:20Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Ramiro -- this one's right up your alley; and an easy kill",
            "creator": "rickg@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-03T22:20:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "shaver, can you deal with this ?",
            "creator": "ramiro@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-02T05:20:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I'll take it, but I'm not going to worry about it until after beta unless\nsomeone can make me believe it's a dogfood issue.",
            "creator": "mike.shaver@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-02T05:25:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "As an additional comment, I've heard from a few people who think that the\ncurrent behaviour is better, in that it doesn't provide as much information\nabout the running system.  (They were thinking of automated attack programs\nkeyed to known bugs in given OS versions.)\n\nThat said, I'll still work to fix the bug, eventually.",
            "creator": "mike.shaver@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-11-29T17:51:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "How come this is still M14? M14 is already out!",
            "creator": "moshev@easybase.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-27T17:55:08Z"
