{
    "bug_id": 7439,
    "summary": "bad cast in appcore shutdown -> change appcores into components",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "nsAppCoresManager:::Shutdown static casts each of the appcores in its list of active cores to an\nnsIDOMBaseAppCore, then calls Release() on the resulting pointer.  Of all our appcores, only one\nof them (nsBaseAppCore) actually inherits from nsIDOMBaseAppCore.  Oddly enough, Release()\nseems to be called correctly on Windows, at least for some appcores.  Other platforms are not so ...\nforgiving.  They seem to just hang up after getting a wrong number.  How civilized.  Still, seems like\nthere's a problem here.\n\nI'm making this a bug, rather than just fixing it, because Scott's work to change appcores into\ncomponents should neatly sidestep this problem.  So I'm ignoring it for now, but making a note...",
            "creator": "danm.moz@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-02T00:42:24Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I'll take care of this as part of converting AppCores to components",
            "creator": "scc-obsolete@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-02T18:11:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "move to later milestone?",
            "creator": "chofmann@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-16T23:21:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "this has moved to m8",
            "creator": "chofmann@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-17T19:39:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Moving all Apprunner bugs past and present to Other component temporarily whilst\ndon and I set correct component.  Apprunner component will be deleted/retired\nshortly.",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-23T00:51:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Moving to M9, when the rest of this change can be checked in.",
            "creator": "scc-obsolete@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-07T15:12:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Moving to M11 per today's bug triage.",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-24T22:58:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "following bug #13021, as usual",
            "creator": "scc-obsolete@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-21T18:53:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "According to Bill Law in bug #13021, AppCores are no longer used (though they are\nstill part of the build till he gets some makefile stuff checked in).  Therefore,\nthis bad code in |nsAppCoresManager::Shutdown| is now dead code and so no longer\na problem.",
            "creator": "scc-obsolete@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-12T16:39:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "According to developer's comments this bug is marked as verified. If you think\nthe resolution is wrong please reopen.",
            "creator": "gerardok@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-12T18:47:59Z"
        }
    ]
}

{
    "bug_id": 5416,
    "summary": "should restrict (or warn) about structs passed by value",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "The 'native' declaration syntax allows for declaring type aliases for structs\nwithout tagging them as ptr or ref.\n\nnative foo(JSContext);\n  rather than\n[ptr] native foo(JSContext);\n\nSuch types used in params will result in generate a C++ header in which the\nstruct is passed by value. *Usually* this would be bad. However, there are small\nstructs (like longlongs on some platforms and point structs) that fit in a word\nand *perhaps* ought to be allowed in interfaces. Still, more often than not such\na declaration is a mistake that ought to be flagged.",
            "creator": "jband_mozilla@rattlebrain.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-04-23T04:01:32Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Marking these as ASSIGNED.  Pesky bugzilla-daemon.",
            "creator": "mike+mozilla@meer.net",
            "timestamp": "1999-05-04T08:06:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "[SPAM] Marking milestone 'future' as part of nsbeta3 triage.",
            "creator": "mike+mozilla@meer.net",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-08T20:58:37Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Mass-reassigning mccabe's non-JS, non-Rhino bugs to jband (34 total). \n\nWould like to cc mccabe; but the mass-reassign page does not allow this. \nI'll leave it up to mccabe to decide if he wants to be cc'ed on these - ",
            "creator": "pschwartau@meer.net",
            "timestamp": "2001-03-12T22:39:08Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "mass reassign of xpidl bugs to dbradley@netscape.com",
            "creator": "jband_mozilla@rattlebrain.com",
            "timestamp": "2001-05-07T06:37:50Z"
        }
    ]
}

{
    "bug_id": 10026,
    "summary": "Scrollbar on tree scrolls too far",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "The vertical scrollbar on a tree scrolls the tree past the bottom of the tree.\nIt should really stop when the last row is displayed at the bottom of the\nscrollable area, instead it continues to scroll until the last row is all the way\nto the top of the scrollable area.  The address book window can demonstrate this\nbug, just add a number of cards with New Card until the scrollbar appears, then\nscroll down until it stops scrolling.",
            "creator": "hangas@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-16T20:45:41Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "That's debatable, but consistent with 4.x behavior. CC'ing german, assigning to\nhyatt as p4 for m15",
            "creator": "trudelle@acm.org",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-16T21:28:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I agree with Paul, it should not be allowed to scroll into white space.",
            "creator": "german@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-16T22:24:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "is this mac only?",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-21T02:31:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I have seen this on Windows NT, but never tested Linux.",
            "creator": "hangas@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-21T07:15:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "this happens on linux too. changing platform/os.",
            "creator": "phillip@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-21T21:45:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Fixed.",
            "creator": "hyatt@mozilla.org",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-29T07:41:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Sorry for spam, re-assigning phillip's QA contact XPToolkit/XPWidget bugs to\nclaudius due to restructure",
            "creator": "paulmac@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-28T00:27:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "VERIFIED (with long ago builds)",
            "creator": "cmaximus@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-11-17T03:20:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Pushed by ctuns@mozilla.com:\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/1fc82f06bf8c\n[components] Issue https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/android-components/issues/10026: Make the CreditCard data class parcelable\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/46c8a41eb5f2\n[fenix] For https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/issues/10026: Add Context extension to get AccessibilityManager.\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/4eb7e68577f0\n[fenix] For https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/issues/10026: Add a11y state listener to BaseBrowserFragment.\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/2b03de60a424\n[fenix] For https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/issues/10026: Update scroll flags on a11y state change.",
            "creator": "pulsebot@bmo.tld",
            "timestamp": "2024-03-18T17:53:49Z"
        }
    ]
}

{
    "bug_id": 11229,
    "summary": "Mozilla incorrectly allows TABLE to inherit properties from P",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "TABLE should not inherit properties from P, since P cannot contain TABLE.\n\nNB:Both IE5 and NN4.6 get this right.",
            "creator": "braden@endoframe.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-04T04:36:27Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "The above URL rendered the same in Mozilla, Nav4.6, and IE5.!!",
            "creator": "harishd@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-04T16:43:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "???\n\nNo they do not. Both IE5 and NN4.6 correctly render the first line red and the\nsecond line black. Mozilla renders both lines red.",
            "creator": "braden@endoframe.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-04T20:12:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "ok, you're right.  I see what you saying in apprunner.  I was checking with\nviewer.",
            "creator": "harishd@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-04T21:04:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "The problem is that the layout is functioning in the standards mode while the\nparser is inclined to the quirks mode.\n\nBTW, work needs to be done in setting appropriate modes from document's DOCTYPE.\n\nAssigning bug to peterl@netscape.com\n\nAdding hyatt, and myself to the CC list.",
            "creator": "harishd@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-04T22:14:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Should go away when you finish hooking up parser mode to document DTD mode",
            "creator": "peterl-retired@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-04T00:48:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Setting prority to P1.",
            "creator": "harishd@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-09T16:57:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "DTD modes are hooked up.\n\nThe above URL should render ok.\n\nMarking bug FIXED.",
            "creator": "harishd@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-15T20:19:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Using 9/16 Apprunner, verified bug fixed. Table does not inherit from P.",
            "creator": "christinehoff4@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-17T02:36:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Second line should be black even if we are in standard mode.\nBecause P element SHOULD close before the TABLE element in standard mode.\nreopen.",
            "creator": "VYV03354@nifty.ne.jp",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-05T03:59:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 1986\ntestcase for standard mode",
            "creator": "VYV03354@nifty.ne.jp",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-05T04:00:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Clearing FIXED resolution due to Reopen.",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-05T13:09:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Actually, you're right?  P shouldn't contain TABLE in noquirks mode.  I'll\ninvestigate the problem.  Thanx Braden.",
            "creator": "harishd@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-05T16:26:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "In quirks mode:\nP may contain TABLE for compatibility, but TABLE does not inherit\nproperties from P for compatibility.\n\nIn standard mode:\nTABLE inherit properties from parent, but P cannot contain TABLE.\n\nSecond line should be black in either case after all.\nBut the underlying reason is different.",
            "creator": "VYV03354@nifty.ne.jp",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-07T05:25:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "The attachement renders ok, and the test case renders ok. What is the problem???\n\nI'm guessing this got fixed by some of the other DOCTYPE and quirk mode fixes\nthat have happened these past few weeks.\n\nShould this now be marked WORKSFORME?",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-10T02:28:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This is still not fixed on latest build using cvs.\nSecond text in the attachment should be black, but it is red.",
            "creator": "VYV03354@nifty.ne.jp",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-10T18:43:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Tested using 12/10 build on  Win 95. Using a 'transitional' doctype, page\nrenders as Nav 4. Using a 'strict' doctype, page renders the table text in red\nwhich is incorrect for the reasons reported stated. Bug is reproduced on Win 95.\nI agree with reporter.",
            "creator": "christinehoff4@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-10T20:28:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 3492\nScreenshot of attachement using 1999-12-14-08 build on Win98",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-15T00:18:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 3493\ntestcase for quirks mode (transitional DTD)",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-15T00:19:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 3494\nScreenshot of third attachement using 1999-12-14-08 build on Win98",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-15T00:21:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I have attached screenshots for both the standard mode test case and the\nquirks mode (transitional DTD) test case (also newly attached). They render\ncorrectly AFAICT (table text is never red). This is on Win98.\n\nIs Win95 really rendering this differently? If so I am *very* surprised and\nthis should be marked [PP], with the Platform/OS fields filled in correctly.\n\nOtherwise, this bug is either WORKSFORME or I have an error in my understanding\nof the issue. Can someone work out which it is?",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-15T00:25:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I've also tested on Win98, but table text was red in standard mode.\nI Don't know why my result is different from yours.",
            "creator": "VYV03354@nifty.ne.jp",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-15T16:11:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Are you using AppRunner or Viewer?",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-15T16:38:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 3508\nTestcase: another compatibility mode test",
            "creator": "VYV03354@nifty.ne.jp",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-15T17:22:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I found mode detection was broken now.\nI'm really confused since \"You are in Compatible mode\" is displayed, but table\ntext is red on my environment...",
            "creator": "VYV03354@nifty.ne.jp",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-15T17:24:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Tested using 12/15 build on Win 95 and Win 98. I am testing in Apprunner with\nthe testcase from 12/15 (containing a 'strict' DTD). In strict (standard) mode\nin Apprunner, I still see the problem. Text in the paragraph and in the table\nare both red. I have attached a screenshot from Win 95 but Win 98 is the same.",
            "creator": "christinehoff4@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-16T00:05:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 3520\nscreenshot from Win 95 - 11/15 build",
            "creator": "christinehoff4@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-16T00:06:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Ian: If your prefs.js has the following line, please remove it.\n\nuser_pref(\"nglayout.compatibility.mode\", 2);\n\n Viewer will write this line when Style/Compatibility Mode Pref menu was\nselected. Apprunner would never write it, but it also affect apprunner's\nbehaivior.\n\nNote: Apprunner and viewer will incorrectly display \"You are in Compatible\nmode\" regardless of the \"nglayout.compatibility.mode\" pref. This is another\nbug.",
            "creator": "VYV03354@nifty.ne.jp",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-17T15:06:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Pierre -- this is a css error, not a parser bug. The style is coming from CSS.",
            "creator": "rickg@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-21T01:45:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "We have in fact 2 problems, one in the parser, one in style:\n- In standard mode, the HTML parser should close the P when reaching the TABLE.\n- In quirks mode, the style system should not make TABLE inherit the style from\nthe parent if the parent is P.\n\nCCing Rick, in case he wants to fix the first issue before I take care of the\nsecond one.",
            "creator": "pierre@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-21T23:07:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Moving table bugs to M15 just to see how many we have.",
            "creator": "pierre@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-23T04:43:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Migrating from {css1} to css1 keyword. The {css1}, {css2}, {css3} and {css-moz}\nradars should now be considered deprecated in favour of keywords.\nI am *really* sorry about the spam...",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-13T23:57:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Block-moved to attinasi the bugs related to style inside tables\n",
            "creator": "pierre@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-02-21T22:25:58Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This appears to be fixed now. In standard and quirks mode the table renders\ncorrectly (ie. P is red, table is black). Tested in Viewer and Mozilla, checked\nand I have no nglayout prefs set in either case.\n\nMarking WORKSFORME - please advise if this is not working for you.\n",
            "creator": "attinasi@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-03-21T00:47:35Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Yup, looks good to me.\n",
            "creator": "braden@endoframe.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-05-09T08:05:50Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Pushed by ctuns@mozilla.com:\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/cf02c5dd4935\n[fenix] For https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/issues/11229: Update onboarding ETP copy.\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/71ed28a7ab77\n[fenix] For https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/issues/11229: Update settings ETP copy.\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/df1ef666e64b\n[fenix] For https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/issues/11229: Update ETP cfr string and behaviour.\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/d7f3357951b0\n[fenix] For https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/issues/11229: Update etp strict option title content description.",
            "creator": "pulsebot@bmo.tld",
            "timestamp": "2024-03-18T18:21:47Z"
        }
    ]
}

