        {
            "text": "make sure rod hooked up :drag-over correctly. I don't think he did, but i could\nbe reading the code incorrectly.",
            "creator": "mikepinkerton@mac.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-13T00:46:46Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "m10.",
            "creator": "mikepinkerton@mac.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-13T00:46:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "reassigning to pink for m14",
            "creator": "trudelle@acm.org",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-14T22:33:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "accepting",
            "creator": "mikepinkerton@mac.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-12T20:32:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "moving dogfood-related d&d stuff back to M12. woohoo!",
            "creator": "mikepinkerton@mac.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-26T18:45:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "mass-moving all m12 bugs to m13",
            "creator": "trudelle@acm.org",
            "timestamp": "1999-11-02T23:03:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "dividing up phillips qa contact bugs, he no longer works here",
            "creator": "paulmac@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-02T06:23:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "drag&drop is once again post-beta according to marketing. moving all d&d bugs to\nM15.",
            "creator": "trudelle@acm.org",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-17T23:04:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "not essential.\n",
            "creator": "mikepinkerton@mac.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-03-17T00:42:36Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Mass moving M17 bugs to M18",
            "creator": "trudelle@acm.org",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-05T04:14:14Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "mass-moving all bugs to m21 that are not dofood+, or nsbeta2+",
            "creator": "trudelle@acm.org",
            "timestamp": "2000-05-25T23:52:14Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "all the code appears to be written, but for some reason the state isn't always\nbeing set in the ESM. we only set it when the handling of the dom event !=\nconsumeNoDefault, which is never the case when we're over the chrome for drag\nevents.\n\na good testcase of this is to change ben's rules for the home button in\n  mozilla/themes/modern/communicator/button.css\nto use :drag-over instead of having the JS set an attribute.\n\ncc'ing saari.",
            "creator": "mikepinkerton@mac.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-07-25T18:47:48Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "adding nsbeta3+  -- part of basic toolkit functionality ",
            "creator": "trudelle@acm.org",
            "timestamp": "2000-07-27T21:27:54Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "alas, I don't think i'll be able to get to this. futuring.\n",
            "creator": "mikepinkerton@mac.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-01T00:54:44Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "-> me for investigation",
            "creator": "bugs@bengoodger.com",
            "timestamp": "2001-05-25T06:42:10Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Boy do I suck. Accepting. I'll get to this some day. ",
            "creator": "bugs@bengoodger.com",
            "timestamp": "2001-10-03T06:47:01Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Mass reassign of my non-Firefox bugs to ben_seamonkey@hotmail.com",
            "creator": "bugs@bengoodger.com",
            "timestamp": "2004-02-18T00:46:18Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "psuedo class was renamed to -moz-drag-over, but still doesn't work on chrome afaict.",
            "creator": "highmind63@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2009-06-14T18:47:28Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "The check that pink mentioned in comment 11 is still in nsEventStateManager::FireDragEnterOrExit .\n\nI also think :-moz-drag-over should probably be hierarchical just like :active and :hover.  (This involves changing nsEventStateManager::GetContentState and nsEventStateManager::SetContentState.)\n\nWe might also want to make sure that nsEventStateManager::GenerateDragDropEnterExit makes sense.",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2009-07-07T21:01:55Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Apparently works on chrome now, at least for me.  Are there also cases where it doesn't work?\n\nComment 18 still applies though.  This selector is useless as currently implemented, due to not selecting when dragging over anonymous children (or any other children for that matter).  Perhaps this is masking the fact that it actually does work in its own limited fashion?",
            "creator": "mozilla@virginmedia.com",
            "timestamp": "2012-12-26T12:18:08Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "It doesn't appear to work for background-image (at least when using a gradient), and the same applies in Postbox. Can be tested by using QuickFolders and setting a palette entry for the drag over style.",
            "creator": "axelg@gofree.indigo.ie",
            "timestamp": "2013-09-21T15:09:32Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "(In reply to Axel Grude [:realRaven] from comment #20)\n> It doesn't appear to work for background-image (at least when using a\n> gradient), and the same applies in Postbox. Can be tested by using\n> QuickFolders and setting a palette entry for the drag over style.\n\nSorry. to be more precise: it works in Thunderbird (chrome) but not in SeaMonkey and Postbox (chrome). I am adding the dragover rules dynamically.",
            "creator": "axelg@gofree.indigo.ie",
            "timestamp": "2013-09-21T15:11:23Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Pushed by ctuns@mozilla.com:\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/72bb988bcbb1\n[fenix] Add tests for ContextKt (https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/pull/11824)",
            "creator": "pulsebot@bmo.tld",
            "timestamp": "2024-03-18T18:23:55Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "XUL + no activity for a while. Closing.",
            "creator": "sledru@mozilla.com",
            "timestamp": "2024-06-04T09:50:33Z"
        }
    ]
}

{
    "bug_id": 12939,
    "summary": "Modification request to Makefile for installation.",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "Several files and directories are not created in the install directory for\nTinderbox.  Most systems administrators would know enough to make the\nadjustments, but missing items could delay installation as it did in our case.\n\nRecommended changes include the following 'cvs diff':\n\nIndex: Makefile\n===================================================================\nRCS file: /cvsroot/mozilla/webtools/tinderbox/Makefile,v\nretrieving revision 1.3\ndiff -r1.3 Makefile\n25,30c25,30\n< #BONSAI = /home/httpd/html/bonsai\n< #CVSROOT = /cvsroot\n< #GZIP = /usr/bin/gzip\n< #PERL = /usr/bin/perl\n< #PREFIX = /home/httpd/html/tinderbox\n< #UUDECODE = /usr/bin/uudecode\n---\n> BONSAI = /home/httpd/html/bonsai\n> CVSROOT = /home/cvsroot\n> GZIP = /usr/bin/gzip\n> PERL = /usr/bin/perl\n> PREFIX = /home/httpd/html/tinderbox\n> UUDECODE = /usr/bin/uudecode\n52a53,54\n> examples/build-moz-smoke.pl \\\n> examples/buildit.config \\\n62a65\n>       mkdir -p $(PREFIX)/examples && \\\nEOF",
            "creator": "hittjw@navair.navy.mil",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-01T14:18:21Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "In addition to the file requeted to be added to the Makefile, the file\n'Backwards.pm' will also need to be installed to improve the chances of a\ncorrect installation the first time.  This file can just be added to the install\nlist.",
            "creator": "hittjw@navair.navy.mil",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-01T14:42:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Marking assigned. Hopefully I can clean up tinderbox install after mozilla beta.",
            "creator": "slamm@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-20T22:06:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I applied the changes except for the variable settings. We should use autoconf\nto set those. Marking fixed.",
            "creator": "slamm@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-22T18:52:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Thank you for the patch.",
            "creator": "slamm@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-22T18:56:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Unsetting target milestone so we can delete the old (inappropriate)\nMozilla target milestones from Webtools.",
            "creator": "endico@mozilla.org",
            "timestamp": "2001-03-01T21:23:29Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Pushed by ctuns@mozilla.com:\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/f33f6df1506d\n[components] Issue https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/android-components/issues/12939: Address all ktlint issues\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/6741123558cd\n[components] Issue https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/android-components/issues/12939: Renegerate detekt-baseline.xml and ktlint-baseline.xml\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/4a2ad1c9d1aa\n[components] Issue https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/android-components/issues/12939 - Add ktlint commits to .git-blame-ignore-revs",
            "creator": "pulsebot@bmo.tld",
            "timestamp": "2024-03-18T18:08:56Z"
        }
    ]
}

{
    "bug_id": 13068,
    "summary": "Page Source delivers bad markup when copied to clipboard (generated content)",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "To repeat:\n1. Load http://www.w3.org (or any page of your choice)\n2. Click menu-item View -> Page Source\n3. Select the text. Here's how I did it:\n   Scroll to the bottom, click to the right of \"</HTML>\" and drag left and keep\n   dragging left (even outside window) until the content is selected.\n4. Click menu-item Edit -> Copy\n5. Paste into the text editor of your choice (emacs 20.4 in my case)\n\nObservations:\nAll start and end tags have a space after the initial \"<\".\nAll named entities have a space between the \"&\" and the name, e.g. \"& reg;\".\nLine breaks are converted to space. Tabs are converted to 8 spaces.\nThere is an extra space after all end tags and most of the named entities.\nThe HTML end tag is not properly closed (I get \"< /HTML\" but no \">\").\nThere is a space between attribute names and the \"=\".\nThe CONTENT attribute name in the META tags are missing, for example:\n< META http-equiv =\"Content-Type\" =\"text/html; charset=iso-8859-1\">\n\nVersion and OS:\nNightly build 1999-09-01-09-M10 on Windows NT. (Also tried on Aug 31. build on\nSun/solaris 2.6/sparc and it core dumped, I will attach a stack trace.)",
            "creator": "MatsPalmgren_bugz@use.startmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-03T00:31:37Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 1522\nSolaris stack trace",
            "creator": "MatsPalmgren_bugz@use.startmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-03T00:37:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "mats, this is an excellent and through bug report; thank you!\n\nReassigning to Akkana; reproduced on 1999 9/2/99 Mac OS build. Akkana, I'll play\naround with this a bit in the next few minutes.",
            "creator": "elig@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-03T23:39:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "<duh, \"thorough\" bug report. friday afternoon it is. ;->",
            "creator": "elig@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-03T23:40:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "BTW, I copied some HTML to a foo.txt file, loaded it within Mozilla, copied it,\nand pasted it to a text editor (BBEdit), and it didn't result in the below-\ndescribed problem.\n\nThis only occurs from View Source.",
            "creator": "elig@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-03T23:53:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "adding myself a cc since i first implemented this",
            "creator": "sford4@netscape.net",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-04T04:49:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "i am looking at this now, i think it is a combination of switching dtd's and\nusing the editor to display the source,",
            "creator": "sford4@netscape.net",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-04T22:43:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I'll work with sford on figuring out what's going on.",
            "creator": "akkzilla@shallowsky.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-07T21:18:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Please note 13278, which may either be a subissue of this bug, or a duplicate.",
            "creator": "elig@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-08T17:56:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Changing Component to Output.",
            "creator": "akkzilla@shallowsky.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-07T01:34:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Currently the clipboard isn't working at all (Build: 1999110911) , so I can't\ntest this theory. But, this looks a lot like a bug that I reported earlier that\nis now fixed. Check bug 16175",
            "creator": "jelwell@singleclick.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-11-10T19:06:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "MozMacM14 (01.28.2000) shows similar problem - text is copied w/o the brackets \"<>\" and line breaks are represented by spaces.  Copying \nfrom Page Source window unusable.\n",
            "creator": "devsin@outlook.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-29T11:22:54Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Selection basically doesn't work in the view source window, because view source\nwas implemented using generated content, which we don't know how to support in\nselection.  This is a problem Mike Judge is working on.  ",
            "creator": "akkzilla@shallowsky.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-31T18:53:07Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "hmm yes we need to make the iterators for copy/serialize to use the new \ngeneratedcontent iterators. I will talk to akkana about this. m16",
            "creator": "mjudge@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-08T00:39:07Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "this is dependent on 12460",
            "creator": "rubydoo123@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-05-09T16:40:06Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "adding help wanted to the keywords",
            "creator": "rubydoo123@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-07-27T21:49:15Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "oops -- wrong copy string there: setting to nsbeta3+",
            "creator": "rubydoo123@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-07-27T21:52:35Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "adding brackets to status whiteboard",
            "creator": "rubydoo123@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-07-27T23:34:48Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "We no longer use the same View Source strategy as we used to (like the \nBrowser), so we no longer have any generated content and this problem goes \naway.",
            "creator": "cmanske@jivamedia.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-03T23:14:30Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*SPAM*: Changing the QA contact of all open/resolved Selection bugs from \nelig@netscape.com to BlakeR1234@aol.com.  After the many great years of service \nEli has given to Mozilla, it's time for him to move on; he has accepted a \nposition at Eazel.  We'll be sad to see him go, and I'll do my best to fill his \nspot...",
            "creator": "bugzilla@blakeross.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-14T23:52:21Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Yep, View Source is no longer generated content and clipboard copying works \nfine on mac, win32 and linux (today's builds) -- verified fixed",
            "creator": "bugzilla@blakeross.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-09-05T20:01:33Z"
        }
    ]
}

{
    "bug_id": 13423,
    "summary": "xpidl could use a system for declaring nsresults",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "from...\nnews://news.mozilla.org/37C353F4.B9928132%40netscape.com\n\nI would love to see us declare our nsresult codes in xpidl.\n\nIf we do this then the codes will be automatically reflected (at\ninterface scope) into all of our language mappings.\n\nThe system for constants in xpidl will do almost all the work.\nWhat I think that we need to add is a little xpidl magic to pull\nthis off.\n\n// global predefined xpcom error codes and module base codes\ninterface nsResult : nsISupports\n{\n    const nsresult OK = 0;\n    // ...\n\n    const module_base FooModule   = GenModuleBase(1);\n    const module_base OtherModule = GenModuleBase(2);\n    // ...\n    // Many interfaces can just multiplex off the generic base\n    // rather than require their vvery own module number\n    const module_base GenericInterfaceModule = GenModuleBase(10);\n    // ...\n};\n\n// my interface in my module\ninterface nsIFoo : nsISupports\n{\n    const nsresult MY_ERROR     = GenError(1,\nnsIResult::FooModule);\n    const nsresult COPIED_ERROR = nsIResult::OK;\n};\n\n\nIn C++ one would use: nsIResult::OK or nsIFoo::MY_ERROR where now\nwe say NS_OK and NS_ERROR_FOO_MY_ERROR.\n\nIn JS you could use :\nComponents.interfaces.nsIResult.OK\n ...or perhaps...\nComponents.results.nsIResult.OK\n\nIn order to implement this we need:\n\n1) support for typedef'd types in const declarations (we should\ndo this anyway).\n2) xpidl support for better parsing of the rhs of const\ndeclarations to deal with these 'function call like' and 'static\ndata member like' constructs.\n3) simple backend code to do the calculations for GenModuleBase\nand GenError.\n4) tracking of those results from included files.\n\nThen, of course, we would have to spam the tree and fix our heads\nto follow the new syntax.\n\nThe names might change, but this is the idea.\n\nI'm not really signing up to do all this right now. Brendan is\nhip deep in the compiler front end and might want to do that\npart? McCabe is hip deep in the compiler back end and... well you\nget the rest :)",
            "creator": "jband_mozilla@rattlebrain.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-09T04:27:58Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This one also should go to mccabe.\n\n/be",
            "creator": "brendan@mozilla.org",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-09T20:10:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Not needed for the short term; changing milestone.  I read your\nComponents.results documentation, and this does seem like something that'd be\nnice.",
            "creator": "mike+mozilla@meer.net",
            "timestamp": "2000-02-15T22:34:35Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "M16 has been out for a while now, these bugs target milestones need to be \nupdated.",
            "creator": "R6Agent@prodigy.net",
            "timestamp": "2000-06-21T20:43:29Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "[SPAM] Marking milestone 'future' as part of nsbeta3 triage.",
            "creator": "mike+mozilla@meer.net",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-08T22:17:41Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I had been under the impression that this was going to be done as part of the \narchitecture review sweep.  Brendan?",
            "creator": "dmosedale@mozilla.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-14T19:35:35Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Cc'ing warren.  I don't know of anyone with time to do this right now.\n\n/be",
            "creator": "brendan@mozilla.org",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-14T20:13:45Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "<http://lxr.mozilla.org/seamonkey/source/xpcom/base/nsIErrorService.idl> \ncontains the current workaround that's in use.",
            "creator": "dmosedale@mozilla.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-22T19:32:53Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 44050 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "mike+mozilla@meer.net",
            "timestamp": "2000-11-30T11:00:03Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Many good comments from Warren off in 44050.",
            "creator": "mike+mozilla@meer.net",
            "timestamp": "2000-11-30T11:01:01Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Mass-reassigning mccabe's non-JS, non-Rhino bugs to jband (34 total). \n\nWould like to cc mccabe; but the mass-reassign page does not allow this. \nI'll leave it up to mccabe to decide if he wants to be cc'ed on these - ",
            "creator": "pschwartau@meer.net",
            "timestamp": "2001-03-12T22:36:57Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "mass reassign of xpidl bugs to dbradley@netscape.com",
            "creator": "jband_mozilla@rattlebrain.com",
            "timestamp": "2001-05-07T06:40:41Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "any eta on this?",
            "creator": "basic@mozdev.org",
            "timestamp": "2004-08-07T14:52:55Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "A quick note, for anyone interested in doing this, there should be NS_SUCCEEDED\nand NS_FAILED types of functions as well provided by this.",
            "creator": "dbradley@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2005-02-06T10:35:53Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Benjamin: can you elaborate on why you WONTFIXed this bug?",
            "creator": "dmosedale@mozilla.com",
            "timestamp": "2009-07-24T19:00:51Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Because I don't believe that the future of our apps is primarily in XPCOM and I don't think we should spend effort on it.",
            "creator": "benjamin@smedbergs.us",
            "timestamp": "2009-07-24T19:07:52Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "So, you're essentially wontfixing XPCOM? I don't think that's good reasoning.\n\nXPCOM components are were so far needed for all substantial XULrunner applications, and the error codes are a massive problem when developing them.\n\nThat's not to start with the many dozens of Mozilla components, which often don't publish error codes to JS either, to my knowledge.",
            "creator": "ben.bucksch@beonex.com",
            "timestamp": "2009-07-29T15:35:30Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "(In reply to comment #16)\n> XPCOM components are were so far needed for all substantial XULrunner\n> applications\n\nI mean custom XPCOM components here, e.g. for Songbird, TomTom HOME, Birgin IDA etc., pretty much all bigger XULRunner apps I know.",
            "creator": "ben.bucksch@beonex.com",
            "timestamp": "2009-07-29T15:38:10Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I do not think we should add more complexity to the XPCOM system. The future of binary interfaces is going to be jsctypes-style code, not binary XPCOM, and I want to focus XPCOM effort where it's going to make the most difference.",
            "creator": "benjamin@smedbergs.us",
            "timestamp": "2009-07-29T15:42:58Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "(In reply to comment #17)\n> (In reply to comment #16)\n> > XPCOM components are were so far needed for all substantial XULrunner\n> > applications\n> \n> I mean custom XPCOM components here, e.g. for Songbird, TomTom HOME, Birgin IDA\n> etc., pretty much all bigger XULRunner apps I know.\n\nOk, but what does that have to do with this bug? Let's not polish a turd, or to be nicer, gild a lily.\n\n/be",
            "creator": "brendan@mozilla.org",
            "timestamp": "2009-07-29T17:02:15Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Does anyone want to remove the little comment here?\nhttp://hg.mozilla.org/mozilla-central/annotate/fc6783c960ca/xpcom/base/nsIErrorService.idl#l45",
            "creator": "ajvincent@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2010-08-14T03:10:32Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Pushed by ctuns@mozilla.com:\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/f9d2e85a6243\n[fenix] For https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/issues/13423: Pass isPrivate flag to ToolbarView",
            "creator": "pulsebot@bmo.tld",
            "timestamp": "2024-03-18T18:38:39Z"
        }
    ]
}

{
    "bug_id": 13831,
    "summary": "White text selected on a white background is invisible",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "* TITLE/SUMMARY\nWhite text selected on a white background is invisible\n\n* STEPS TO REPRODUCE\n0) Launch Apprunner\n1) View http://theforce.net/jedicouncil/trivia/\n2) Try to select the trivia answers (e.g. white text on a white background)\n\n* RESULT\n - What happened\n\nThe selected white text does not become visible.\n\n - What was expected\n\nUnlike IE 5.0 (Win32) or Navigator 4.7 (Mac OS), the white text does not become\nvisible when selected.\n\n* REGRESSION\n\n - Occurs On\n        Mac OS Apprunner (1999091409 optimized build)\n        Win32 Apprunner (1999091409 optimized build)\n        Linux Apprunner (1999091308 optimized build)\n\n\n - Doesn't Occur On\n        Communicator 4.7 (today's release candidate/RTM-ish) for Mac OS\n        Internet Explorer 5 for Win32\n\n\n* CONFIGURATIONS TESTED\n\n- [Mac] Beige Power Mac G3 (266 MHz PowerPC 750), 96 MB RAM (VM on; 1 MB of VM\nused), 1024x768 (Thousands of Colors), Mac OS 8.6\n\n- [Win32] Vectra VL (233 MHz P2), 96 MB RAM, 800x600 (True Color), NT 4.0 SP3.\n\n- [Linux] Vectra VL (266 MHz P2), 96 MB RAM. Red Hat Linux 6.0 (GNOME).",
            "creator": "elig@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
