{
    "bug_id": 15083,
    "summary": "depends and depending verbage not destinctive enough",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "The verbage when modifing a bug:\n\nBugs that bug X depends on\nBugs depending on bug X\n\nis easily confused.\n\nhow about:\n\nParent Bugs\nChild Bugs",
            "creator": "doug.turner@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-28T17:56:52Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I don't like that either, because it doesn't describe what kind of parent/child\nrelationship this is.\n\nI don't like the existing words either, but I haven't heard anything I like\nbetter.",
            "creator": "terry@mozilla.org",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-28T20:43:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "It's the extra word \"Bugs\" on each line that are the troublesome part...\nin each case the is to the left, but stands for the list of bug numbers\nto the right, of the phrase, only confusing an already topsy-turvy human \nparsing job.\n\nHow about:\n\nBug X depends on:\nBug X blocks:\n\nI think everyone can figure out that the numbers after the colon in each\ncase refer to bugs and complete the statment.\n",
            "creator": "sidr@albedo.net",
            "timestamp": "2000-02-02T06:38:50Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "OK, done!",
            "creator": "terry@mozilla.org",
            "timestamp": "2000-02-02T17:43:47Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "per Terry, auto-verifying any resolved bug that hasn't been touched since before \n2.10 was released.\n",
            "creator": "justdave@bugzilla.org",
            "timestamp": "2001-03-07T06:31:42Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Moving to Bugzilla product",
            "creator": "justdave@bugzilla.org",
            "timestamp": "2001-09-03T07:34:23Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Pushed by ffxbld-merge:\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/releases/mozilla-beta/rev/acad9813d02f\n[fenix] For #[15083]: Add multi select to recently closed tabs",
            "creator": "pulsebot@bmo.tld",
            "timestamp": "2024-04-15T08:39:39Z"
        }
    ]
}

{
    "bug_id": 15116,
    "summary": "rightmost pixels of italic text don't change on hover/blink (should set overflow area of text frames)",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "Italic text in BLINK is not rendered correctly. Load the attached\ntestcase and you will see either of two errors:\n1. The upper-right part of the '!' is not erased when the blink is \"off\".\n2. The upper-right part of the '!' is not drawn when the blink is \"on\".\n\nWhich one is in effect depends on the width of the window, try resizing\nand you will see the other error.\n\nBug occurs in both viewer and apprunner 1999-09-25-09-M11 on Windows NT4sp5.",
            "creator": "MatsPalmgren_bugz@use.startmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-28T20:55:28Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 1897\ntestcase",
            "creator": "MatsPalmgren_bugz@use.startmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-28T21:00:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This is more likely a layout bug.",
            "creator": "beard@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-18T19:01:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "No, I think it's a problem with the text measurement code. Maybe a round off\nerror? If I turn on visual debugging it's clear the text frame's frame bounds\naren't quite big enough.\n\nKevin, are you the owner of the Windows gfx code?",
            "creator": "troy@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-18T19:42:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Yes, I own gfx on WIN32 it. I'll look at this.",
            "creator": "kmcclusk@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-19T19:17:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Moving to M15",
            "creator": "kmcclusk@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-17T21:20:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Bulk moving [testcase] code to new testcase keyword. Sorry for the spam!",
            "creator": "ekrock@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-21T21:48:17Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Bulk moving to M16",
            "creator": "kmcclusk@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-06T21:17:13Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Moving to M17",
            "creator": "kmcclusk@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-07T21:20:25Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Marking FUTURE. Niceness of BLINK handling not a priority for FCS. BLINK not \nwidely used and is indeed widely hated.",
            "creator": "ekrock@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-06-06T21:42:24Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I am no longer seeing the problem in a current build on WINNT. buld id 200103904.\nMarking WORKSFORME.",
            "creator": "kmcclusk@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2001-03-10T00:50:15Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I still see this, build 2001-03-16-04 on Windows NT4.0 sp6. Please make sure you\nhave <font face=\"Snap ITC\"> installed on your system when looking at the testcase.\n\nErik: Yes, I most certainly agree with you on BLINK, but this bug points to a more\ngeneral problem (I think), namely that text-measurements/line-boxes are calculated\nwrong for certain fonts. I have seen other bugs pointing in that direction too.",
            "creator": "MatsPalmgren_bugz@use.startmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2001-03-19T22:59:07Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "WFM, today's Linux CVS. Mats, do you still see this?",
            "creator": "choess@stwing.upenn.edu",
            "timestamp": "2001-10-24T05:05:32Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Build moving all existing future-P3 bugs to future-P4.",
            "creator": "kmcclusk@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2002-02-22T15:16:03Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 75826\nTestcase without BLINK",
            "creator": "MatsPalmgren_bugz@use.startmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2002-03-24T13:59:34Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 75829\nScreenshot of testcase (Windows BMP format)",
            "creator": "MatsPalmgren_bugz@use.startmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2002-03-24T14:09:43Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "WFM. I do not see the problem described while looking at the testcase using\nmozilla 1.0 (Win98).",
            "creator": "piskozub@iopan.gda.pl",
            "timestamp": "2002-06-19T12:17:27Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Confirmed using FizzillaCFM/2002070913. The top of the exclamation point draws\nslightly outside the red-background inline box. Setting All/All.\n\nThis bug doesn't necessarily have anything to do with blink. Rather, the\ncalculation of the width of italicized text doesn't match the inline box that\ncontains it, resulting in text overdrawing the background-color area.\n\nRevising Summary.",
            "creator": "bugmail@impromptu.at",
            "timestamp": "2002-07-11T06:58:34Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "On Mac, this, like many other problems, is fixed by bug 121540.",
            "creator": "bugmail@impromptu.at",
            "timestamp": "2002-08-31T02:11:02Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Isn't this just due to the font metrics for italic text lying about the char\nwidths (or rather the fact that in italic text the glyphs will often extend\noutside the nominal \"box\" they're supposed to live in so that the spacing\nbetween them won't look too big)?\n\n",
            "creator": "bzbarsky@mit.edu",
            "timestamp": "2003-02-16T18:37:41Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Perhaps, although the metrics may have information on the italic correction.",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2003-02-16T18:39:44Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Ah, true.\n\nccing some people who may know about that whole text-measurement thing and font\nmetrics.",
            "creator": "bzbarsky@mit.edu",
            "timestamp": "2003-02-16T18:44:32Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 93572 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2003-03-30T22:22:35Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I'm not 100% is this applies, but it seems so. The italicized text if inside a\ntable also bleeds over the edges. Slashdot is an easy example where to see this,\nsince they put borders on the left side of their main content boxes, where you\ncan see letters like f and g bleed over the left edge of the table",
            "creator": "gardenofstone@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2003-03-31T19:32:04Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 215572 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "MatsPalmgren_bugz@use.startmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2003-08-08T19:12:09Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 157470 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "MatsPalmgren_bugz@use.startmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2003-08-08T19:14:49Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "As I said in bug 96041, which has collected a bunch of duplicates as well, this\nshould be solved by giving the text frames the appropriate overflow area somehow.",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2004-12-31T04:32:15Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 257208 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2004-12-31T04:34:27Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 276548 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2004-12-31T04:34:34Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "see http://ln.hixie.ch/?start=1104458648&amp;count=1 for a test case (from bug\n#276548)",
            "creator": "sspitzer@mozilla.org",
            "timestamp": "2004-12-31T04:59:23Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I'm marking this a duplicate of 79732 because it's really the same issue.\n\n*** This bug has been marked as a duplicate of 79732 ***",
            "creator": "roc@ocallahan.org",
            "timestamp": "2005-02-02T04:31:58Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I wanted to leave them separate because handling italic correction might be\nsimpler than handling all overhanging characters, but together is ok if you\nthink it's got a good chance of being fixed.",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2005-02-02T06:15:00Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 311999 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "smontagu@smontagu.org",
            "timestamp": "2005-10-11T13:30:20Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 360919 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "MatsPalmgren_bugz@use.startmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2006-11-16T15:52:45Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Pushed by ctuns@mozilla.com:\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/3219b67c5088\n[fenix] For https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/issues/15116: Use safe cast for layout params.\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/daac3d33efc3\n[fenix] For https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/issues/15116: Do not expand toolbar on PWA tabs.\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/6aeb9421bd12\n[fenix] For https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/issues/15116: Do not set bottom toolbar behavior on PWA tabs.\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/268831d774fa\n[fenix] For https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/issues/15116: Also do not expand or set bottom toolbar behavior on TWA tabs.",
            "creator": "pulsebot@bmo.tld",
            "timestamp": "2024-03-18T18:39:24Z"
        }
    ]
}

{
    "bug_id": 15284,
    "summary": "caret code should respect style context settings",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "today, caret painting is boolean based on the frame type and the pres shell\nsetting.\nall the UI properties from CSS-3 are implemented in gecko, so we should start\nusing them.  Caret painting can be controlled by looking at the\nnsStyleUserInterface part of the nsStyleContext.  In particular,\nthe user_modifiable property implies whether the caret should be displayed or\nnot.",
            "creator": "buster@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-30T21:04:01Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "change to all platforms; set to M14 (post-beta)",
            "creator": "brade@comcast.net",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-04T15:10:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "M16\n",
            "creator": "sfraser_bugs@smfr.org",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-04T01:07:02Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "m17",
            "creator": "rubydoo123@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-05-09T16:38:03Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "this should also include the caret height, this is correctness and polish",
            "creator": "rubydoo123@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-07-19T23:24:25Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "setting to nsbeta3+",
            "creator": "rubydoo123@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-07-27T20:12:31Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "adding brackets to status whiteboard",
            "creator": "rubydoo123@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-07-27T23:35:16Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "setting priority in status whiteboard",
            "creator": "rubydoo123@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-07-31T20:58:09Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*SPAM*: Changing the QA contact of all open/resolved Selection bugs from \nelig@netscape.com to BlakeR1234@aol.com.  After the many great years of service \nEli has given to Mozilla, it's time for him to move on; he has accepted a \nposition at Eazel.  We'll be sad to see him go, and I'll do my best to fill his \nspot...",
            "creator": "bugzilla@blakeross.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-14T23:52:31Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "It turns out that user-modify style is set to NS_STYLE_USER_MODIFY_READ_ONLY for \nthe content of text fields and in composer, since this is the default. To make \nthis work, we'd need to have CSS that sets user-modify \nNS_STYLE_USER_MODIFY_READ_WRITE wherever we do editing. This seems like too big a \nchange to do now. I'll leave some code #ifdeffed in nsCaret to support this.\n\nRemoving status whiteboard entries.\n",
            "creator": "sfraser_bugs@smfr.org",
            "timestamp": "2000-09-07T06:35:05Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "excellent debugging and analysis -- setting to nsbeta3-",
            "creator": "rubydoo123@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-09-07T18:42:13Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "removing myself from the cc list",
            "creator": "rubydoo123@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "2002-03-08T19:58:05Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Note that at least on Windows the caret is always visible in textfields whether\nthey are editable or not, and IMHO it is a bug that this isn't true in Mozilla.",
            "creator": "neil@httl.net",
            "timestamp": "2002-09-20T08:55:28Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Pushed by ctuns@mozilla.com:\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/b1a48d2ee510\n[fenix] For https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/issues/15284: Process root titles when creating new folders",
            "creator": "pulsebot@bmo.tld",
            "timestamp": "2024-03-18T18:40:25Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Reading the comments, it sounded to me this was for editor/composer application, which is a very different scope of this Gecko component. Please file a new issue under the proper component.  If this was about some defects in caret related CSS properties, please file a new issue with a minimum test case. Thanks.",
            "creator": "htsai@mozilla.com",
            "timestamp": "2024-03-21T07:25:38Z"
        }
    ]
}

{
    "bug_id": 15286,
    "summary": "selection needs to swap highlight foreground/background color based on background color",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "Nav 4 has an algorithm that will swap foreground and background highlight color\nif the background highlight and the document background color are within a small\ntolerance of each other.  This allows the selection to be visible regardless of\nthe background.",
            "creator": "buster@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-30T21:09:51Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "buster, could you possibly provide a URL in which this is an issue? (I thought\nwe're doing correctly what you're referring to --- e.g. how does this differ from\n9960 or 13831?)\n\nThanks!",
            "creator": "elig@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-30T21:15:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "this is probably a dup of 13831 or 9960",
            "creator": "buster@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-30T21:22:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I'm guessing that buster@netscape.com intended this to be dup'ed of #9960 (which\nhas been marked fixed) which is for xor'ing the selection.  Please re-open if you\nintended this bug to be something else.\n\n\n*** This bug has been marked as a duplicate of 9960 ***",
            "creator": "brade@comcast.net",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-12T20:29:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "No, this is meant for something else. The issue is when selection code uses\nstyle data for selection colors it still needs to detect foreground/bachground\ncollisions and swap foreground/background (not xor).",
            "creator": "peterl-retired@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-12T21:08:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "setting to M15, this can wait until after the beta push",
            "creator": "rubydoo123@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-14T22:55:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 25622 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "rubydoo123@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-02-01T00:43:11Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "until the spec in CSS3 allows us to use this system of letting the OS decide \nwhat the colors are depending on the current foreground and background I am \nleaving the deciding of color to CSS3.  This will probably mean that the DEFAULT \nstyle of CSS will be the default foreground andbackground of the OS. then any \npage that wishes to override this can do so.  Until CSS3 has some specs on how \nto in a XP way allow the system to be handed the current color and style then \nreturn the new background and foreground color, this will be the case. no XOR \nfor now in other words.",
            "creator": "mjudge@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-03T21:05:15Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*SPAM*: Changing the QA contact of all open/resolved Selection bugs from \nelig@netscape.com to BlakeR1234@aol.com.  After the many great years of service \nEli has given to Mozilla, it's time for him to move on; he has accepted a \nposition at Eazel.  We'll be sad to see him go, and I'll do my best to fill his \nspot...",
