{
    "bug_id": 17089,
    "summary": "Resize browser window to short heights -> corrupted vertical scroll bar",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "* TITLE/SUMMARY\n[PP] Resize browser window to short heights -> corrupted vertical scroll bar\n\n(split out of bug #5548)\n\n* STEPS TO REPRODUCE\n0) Launch Apprunner\n1) Using any web page (I used www.mozilla.org), reduce the height of the browser\nwindow to the minimum allowed.\n\n* RESULT\n - What happened\n\nThe vertical scroll arrow gets replaced with either a horiontal scroll arrow, or\ntwo miniature scroll arrows. Sometimes, you may need to shrink the width of the\nbrowser window to see it.\n\n - What was expected\n\nUltimately, we shouldn't be allowing users to shrink the window on Mac beyond a\ncertain size. It can take a minute to reproduce; for examples, see the screen\nshots attached --- PICT format to save time, and since anyone trying to fix this\nwill have a Mac. ;)\n\nOther Mac apps don't allow this --- when we did the Mac OS 8 Appearance Manager\nway back in 1996-1997, I don't think any consideration was given to the effects\nof shrinking a window to the dimensions at which scroll arrows don't fit.\nCertainly, we didn't test it, as no applications in use invoked that behavior.\n\n(It was possible --- I forget how --- within the Finder due to a bug, but that\nwas fixed in 8.5.)\n\n* REGRESSION\n\n - Occurs On\n        Mac OS Apprunner (1999102211 Mozilla build & 1999102109 Commercial build\n[Mac OS 8.6])\n\n - Doesn't Occur On\n        Win32 Apprunner (999102208 build [NT 4, Service Pack 5])\n        Linux Apprunner (1999102208 build [RH 6.0/GNOME])\n\n\n* CONFIGURATIONS TESTED\n\n- [Mac] Beige Power Mac G3 (266 MHz PowerPC 750), 96 MB RAM (VM on; 1 MB of VM\nused), 1024x768 (Thousands of Colors), Mac OS 8.6\n\n- [Win32] Vectra VL (233 MHz P2), 96 MB RAM, 800x600 (True Color), NT 4.0 SP5.\n\n- [Linux] Vectra VL (266 MHz P2), 96 MB RAM. Red Hat Linux 6.0 (GNOME).",
            "creator": "elig@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-22T21:53:24Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "[QA Assigning to self as a service to Claudius, who has way too many bugs.\nClaudius, if you want to be QA Assigned on this, please feel free to have it\nback. ;-]",
            "creator": "elig@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-22T21:53:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 2369\nVertical scroll arrow replaced with -> arrow",
            "creator": "elig@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-22T21:55:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 2370\nVertical scroll bar replaced with mini <- -> arrows",
            "creator": "elig@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-22T21:56:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I can't reproduce this on my PB3400, 8.6, same build & page.  I can get the\nlower arrow to disappear if I resize to minimal height, then expand width until\nhorizontal scrollbar is gone.\nreassigning to evaughan as p4 for m14",
            "creator": "trudelle@acm.org",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-22T23:21:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Eli's bug reproduction clinic is always open if needed; walk-in hours are 9:00 AM\n- 6:00 M-F. ;)",
            "creator": "elig@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-22T23:44:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "mass moving m14 bugs to m15",
            "creator": "trudelle@acm.org",
            "timestamp": "1999-11-02T22:58:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "cc'ing myself",
            "creator": "cmaximus@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-11-04T03:30:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "targeting",
            "creator": "eric@droidlogic.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-03-21T21:07:18Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "targeting",
            "creator": "eric@droidlogic.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-03-21T21:07:32Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Mass moving M17 bugs to M18",
            "creator": "trudelle@acm.org",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-05T04:14:25Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "We currently aren't putting restrictions on window min size. We should. But \ncurrenly the scrollbars just dissappear if they get too small to render. When we \nget a new feature called flexdepth into boxes we will actually be able to \nmake squeeze into tiny little arrows. But a min size on the window would be \nnice eventually.",
            "creator": "eric@droidlogic.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-05-16T21:19:14Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Mass-moving all M20-M30 XPToolkit bugs to Future",
            "creator": "trudelle@acm.org",
            "timestamp": "2000-05-25T22:21:50Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Still no minimum size in 20030311 OSX. And 20030306 Win98 exhibits equally bad\nbehavior.\n\n*** This bug has been marked as a duplicate of 48798 ***",
            "creator": "francis.uy@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2003-03-12T21:25:11Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Pushed by ffxbld-merge:\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/releases/mozilla-beta/rev/1b2900ed0457\n[fenix] Closes https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/issues/17089: Add metric to track both normal and private URI opened (https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/pull/17935)",
            "creator": "pulsebot@bmo.tld",
            "timestamp": "2024-04-15T08:29:27Z"
        }
    ]
}

{
    "bug_id": 17092,
    "summary": "Shrinking height of browser yields premature scroll bar disappearance",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "* TITLE/SUMMARY\n[PP] Shrinking height of browser yields premature scroll bar disappearance\n\n(broken out of bug #5548)\n\n* STEPS TO REPRODUCE\n0) Launch Apprunner. View a URL (e.g. www.mozilla.org)\n1) Shrink the width of the browser window sufficiently to invoke a horizontal\nscroll bar.\n2) Shrink the height of the browser window so that the page content region comes\nwithin 100 pixels or so of the minimum height.\n3) Slowly shrink the height of the browser window until you've reached the\nminimum height.\n\n* RESULT\n - What happened\n\nThe horizontal scroll bar disappears, roughly when a 60-80 pixels height's worth\nof page content remains.\n\n - What was expected\n\nBehavior equivalent to Communicator 4.x; the last of the browser window content\nshould disappear before the scroll bars do.\n\n - Occurs On\n        Linux Apprunner (1999102208 build [RH 6.0/GNOME])\n\n - Doesn't Occur On\n        Win32 Apprunner (999102208 build [NT 4, Service Pack 5])\n        Mac OS Apprunner (1999102211 Mozilla build & 1999102109 Commercial build\n[Mac OS 8.6])\n\n* CONFIGURATIONS TESTED\n\n- [Mac] Beige Power Mac G3 (266 MHz PowerPC 750), 96 MB RAM (VM on; 1 MB of VM\nused), 1024x768 (Thousands of Colors), Mac OS 8.6\n\n- [Win32] Vectra VL (233 MHz P2), 96 MB RAM, 800x600 (True Color), NT 4.0 SP5.\n\n- [Linux] Vectra VL (266 MHz P2), 96 MB RAM. Red Hat Linux 6.0 (GNOME).",
            "creator": "elig@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-22T22:31:44Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "[QA Assigning to self to reduce Claudius's enormous bug load.]",
            "creator": "elig@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-22T22:32:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Can only reproduce using GFX scrollbars. reassigning to evaughan as p4 for m16",
            "creator": "trudelle@acm.org",
            "timestamp": "1999-11-01T23:51:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "targeting",
            "creator": "eric@droidlogic.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-03-22T20:12:19Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Mass moving M17 bugs to M18",
            "creator": "trudelle@acm.org",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-05T04:14:50Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "mass-moving all bugs to m21 that are not dofood+, or nsbeta2+",
            "creator": "trudelle@acm.org",
            "timestamp": "2000-05-25T23:52:51Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "(per trudelle). mass-moving all evaughan non-nsbeta3+ bugs to 'Future'\nmilestone",
            "creator": "jrgmorrison@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-02T03:27:50Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This does not happen when the sidebar is removed. If there is a side bar its \nbecause the sidebars splitter's grippy can't shrink past its min size which is \nthe height of the image. This is up to the skin designer to fix. To fix:\n\nThe vertical splitter (like in the sidebar) should have a min-height of 1px\nThe horizontal splitter (like in mail) should have a min-width of 1px\n\nThis will allow the window to shrink in height.\n",
            "creator": "eric@droidlogic.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-09-14T23:31:19Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This is probably due to a min-width setting on the browser tag in \nnavigator.xul... I'll have a look shortly.",
            "creator": "hewitt@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-09-14T23:52:41Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "\n\n*** This bug has been marked as a duplicate of 55368 ***",
            "creator": "hewitt@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2001-03-16T04:53:07Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Verified dup.\n",
            "creator": "jg@jmkg.net",
            "timestamp": "2001-03-21T20:01:06Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Pushed by ffxbld-merge:\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/releases/mozilla-beta/rev/4f2af6da5a83\n[fenix] For https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/issues/17092: Dismiss toolbar menu when configuration change occurs (https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/pull/17682)",
            "creator": "pulsebot@bmo.tld",
            "timestamp": "2024-04-15T08:27:32Z"
        }
    ]
}

