{
    "bug_id": 1859,
    "summary": "No visual indication of focus on forms or links",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "Assigning to rickg - who owns focus?\n\nI suspect the best way to accomplish this would be through a :focus pseudo class\naddition to our CSS selector implementation, along with support for CSS2's\n\"outline\" property. Then we could add code like this to our ua.css:\n\nLABEL:focus { outline: 1px dotted black; }",
            "creator": "angus@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1998-12-10T23:57:20Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "See\nhttp://www.w3.org/TR/REC-CSS2/selector.html#dynamic-pseudo-classes\nfor information on the CSS2 :focus pseudo-class.  It is in the spec,\nbasically as you described it :-)",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "1998-12-23T04:04:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Need to work with Tom Pixley to handle focus of non native controls",
            "creator": "karnaze@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-01-04T17:58:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Setting all current Open/Normal to M4.",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-02-03T16:08:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "per leger, assigning QA contacts to all open bugs without QA contacts according\nto list at http://bugzilla.mozilla.org/describecomponents.cgi?product=Browser",
            "creator": "paulmac@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-03-06T06:13:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "See 6647 for an RFE for the 'outline' property.",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "1999-05-18T14:02:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 7058 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "kmcclusk@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-06-02T23:15:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Moving to M9",
            "creator": "kmcclusk@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-01T21:11:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Moving to M10",
            "creator": "kmcclusk@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-16T23:03:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Rod, here is a focus bug to check the gfx-form elements against.",
            "creator": "kmcclusk@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-26T21:58:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Fixed. some form of visual notification has been added.",
            "creator": "rods@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-19T15:28:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I can't currently verify the fix (using the 1999082616 build with GFX widgets\nenabled under NT) as I can't navigate using the Tab key. I would expect that I\ncould tab through, say, this Bugzilla bug using that build and see links\nvisually indicated through that thin dotted line, but it isn't working. I will\nverify this as soon as possible.",
            "creator": "cpratt@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-27T18:32:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I may have a slightly older build but I see this working with one bug, when\ntabbing through bugzilla the links will show that they are focus but when focus\nleaves them they do not return to their previous state.",
            "creator": "joki@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-27T18:42:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 12777 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "joki@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-30T17:48:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I'm going to reopen this and clear the resolution. Using the 1999091310 M10\nbuild on Win32 (Windows NT), I still don't see any visual indication of which\nfield is currently active on a form. Using the above URL, for example, no matter\nwhich text input control you click into, they all look the same. Tab still isn't\nworking either but that's no reason to not reopen this. FWIW my build has gfx\nwidgets enabled.",
            "creator": "cpratt@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-13T20:49:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 1645\nSample form from FrontPage Express - test case for 1859",
            "creator": "cpratt@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-13T20:50:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "THis is related to two other bugs that need to be looked up. One is a joki bug,\nit has to do with the physical window not grabbing the focus when you click on a\nform control. If you click on \"white space\" in the window first and then click\non a form control, then hit the tab key it moves around from control to control\nand it does show visual indication of focus.\n\nThe second bug (abuster bug), is that the text field and text area's \"eat\" the\ntab. Once you tab into them, you can't tab out. He suppose to be fixing it for\nbeta.\n\nSo I don't mind leaving this open, but on my end it is fixed.\n\nRemoved peterl, troy and karnaze from cc list and added buster.",
            "creator": "rods@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-14T21:03:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Changing to M12",
            "creator": "rods@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-21T21:03:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "fixed",
            "creator": "rods@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-24T02:15:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Verified fixed in the 1999102908 build under Windows 98. There are still quite\na few problems in this area (see bug 17605, bug 17606 for preliminary examples)\nbut this issue is gone.",
            "creator": "cpratt@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-30T01:41:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I can't check Windows NT but this does not work for the 2000-08-09-09m18 build \nfor windows 98. If you mouse to a Form item you get an indication of focus but \nwith out tab working there is no indication of focus for link items. I also \nchecked out an earlier version of Linux and though tabbing was somewhat \nimplimented focus for links were not visable thought they seemed to work. Focus \nfor form items in Linus worked though.\n\nChanged the OS to Win 98 but this may be more pervasive than that.\n",
            "creator": "lake@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-09T20:29:32Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "With outlines not working, I can't see how this will be fixed for nsbeta3 or \neven RTM. And we aren't going to do outlines until 6.1",
            "creator": "rods@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-10T13:31:01Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Based on Rods comments about outline marking nsbeta3-",
            "creator": "kmcclusk@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-10T23:00:27Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This is acutally a very big deal! Remonimating for nsbeta3. This lack of \nfeedback and functionality greatly impacts the usability of our product. I am \nalso adding Matthew Thomas to the CC list and adding to acessability tracking \nbug 24413. If you can't what the keyboard is activating then the user can't use \nthe keyboard for web page interaction except for typing in a form field. ",
            "creator": "lake@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-11T04:34:54Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "So I'm the accessibility expert now, am I? <gulp/>\n\nWe're in trouble here. This depends on bug 6647, support for CSS2 `outline'. But \nthat was marked as a dup of bug 9816, which was `fixed' by *removing* all support \nfor CSS2 `outline' because it's too buggy for release: `To do outlines \ncorrectly is more than a few days worth of work and layout and rendering folks \nneed to sit down and discuss it', said Karnaze.\n\nChanged platform to All, component to one that's more relevant, and URL to one \nthat works.\n",
            "creator": "mpt@postinbox.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-13T12:28:38Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "(Just to clarify something: Implementing 'outline' would take several _weeks'_\nworth of engineering time, and a whole lot of QA time. If we had the cycles to\nspare to implement 'outline' then they would instead be spent on fixing our\nother much more drastic standards compliance and performance problems. 'outline'\nis simply not going to happen for rtm.)\n\nWe might be able to use border-style:dotted as a poor-man's outline? It wouldn't\nbe ideal, but considering the looming deadlines it might be a good compromise.\nOr, possibly, using a new color. 'outline' is not the only solution here - we\ndon't *have* to have a dotted border to represent focus.",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-13T12:51:31Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Could we cheat and implement a -moz-outline property that paints the outline\ninside the border (using mostly the existing code)?",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-13T15:18:00Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "The 'outline' code has a LOT more bugs than just the redraw bugs. If we have\nthe time to implement any sort of 'outline'-like functionality, then it is\nbetter spent on, say, the floater bugs.\n\nAs I said, we could just use the border (with careful use of padding) or color\nor any number of other feedback mechanisms.\n\nBlake, you're working on this, right? Do you want to take the bug, to reduce\nrod's doomage factor?",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-13T17:31:26Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I'll take it just to experiment with various visual notifications, but I don't \nhave too many ideas right now (since Outline would've been ideal...)",
            "creator": "bugzilla@blakeross.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-13T18:41:37Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "back to ian per discussion",
            "creator": "bugzilla@blakeross.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-23T06:22:23Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "we're doing what David suggested; I'm keeping this bug open to make sure I don't\nforget to keep this fixed in my html.css.",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-30T00:59:33Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 3254 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "2000-09-11T17:56:56Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "It's mostly there in the browser the outline for links the dotted line for check\nboxes, the I cursor for entry fields but there is no indication for multiple\nselect boxes only drop boxes.  Also these are not as speced but that we can wait\nfor next realease.\t\t",
            "creator": "lake@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-09-12T19:29:03Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "PDT marking P5 priority as per Lake's comment (from usability team) that this\ncan wait until the next release.",
            "creator": "lchiang@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-09-13T21:02:19Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Actually in the as specked remark I was refering only to the fact that they do \nnot look right. Not in that we don't have to show focus for all control forms. \nThis part needs to be there or the user gets lost. Lost is bad. Lost is very \nbad! How it looks can come later. ",
            "creator": "lake@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-09-13T22:54:16Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This seems fixed with Ian's *.css changes...please reopen if I'm mistaken (and \nthere's more to this bug).  Thanks.",
            "creator": "bugzilla@blakeross.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-09-22T03:05:28Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "blake: *never* mark someone else's bug as FIXED. Only the FIXER knows if it has\nbeen FIXED or not. If you want to resolve a bug as no longer occurring, that\nis what the WORKSFORME resolution is for.\n\nHowever: FIXED. Please verify.",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "2000-09-22T05:13:36Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "verified fixed along with bug 48973 -- form controls (checkbox,radio,button,select\nand <a href>) all give focus visual feedback, mac/linux/win32 branch&trunk\n",
            "creator": "jrgmorrison@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-09-30T05:33:32Z"
        }
    ]
}

{
    "bug_id": 2055,
    "summary": "[BLOCK] compact DL should be supported",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "Once you get child selectors working, you can get compact DLs by putting the\nfollowing in ua.css:\n\nDL[COMPACT] > DT {display: compact; }\n\nSee the above URL.",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "1998-12-24T18:47:12Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Setting all current Open/Normal to M4.",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-02-03T16:07:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "[QA Assigning to self.]",
            "creator": "elig@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-03-18T23:22:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "[Oops. Reassigning back to chrisd; misread this as a list issue, rather than a\nstyle sheet issue. Thanks for pointing that out, Chris.]",
            "creator": "elig@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-03-23T22:14:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "We have the child selectors now. What we really need is compact layout...",
            "creator": "peterl-retired@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-03-25T07:09:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "You've supported compact display for a while now too:\n\nhttp://www.fas.harvard.edu/~dbaron/csstest/results",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "1999-03-25T13:51:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 4740 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "kipp@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-04-08T23:27:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Simplest possible testcase:\n<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0 Transitional//EN\">\n<HTML>\n<HEAD>\n<TITLE></TITLE>\n</HEAD>\n<BODY>\n<OL compact>\n  <LI>List item 1\n  <LI>List item 2\n  <LI>List item 3\n</OL>\n\n<OL>\n  <LI>List item 1\n  <LI>List item 2\n  <LI>List item 3\n</OL>\n</BODY>\n</HTML>\n\nMarking as testcase...",
            "creator": "aswartz@upclink.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-03T04:36:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "What's happenning now is that 'display:compact' is being treated as block.\n\nFor final release, this should not happen.  Rather than treat it as block, you\nshould ignore it.  This means that the style system should treat it as an\ninvalid keyword, so that\n\n   h2 {\n     display: block;\n     display: compact;\n   }\n\n...yields block display, and\n\n   dl {\n     display: inline;\n     display: compact;\n   }\n\n...yields inline display.\n\nThis last issue is now covered by bug 15432. I am marking that bug dependent on\nthis one, but technically it is an either|or situation.\n\nNote: For HTML4 compliancy, we should support 'compact'.",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-03T22:26:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Updating to default Style System Assignee...kipp no longer with us :-(",
            "creator": "leger@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-14T21:51:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Migrating from {css2} to css2 keyword. The {css1}, {css2}, {css3} and {css-moz}\nradars should now be considered deprecated in favour of keywords.\nI am *really* sorry about the spam...",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-14T00:06:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Bulk moving [testcase] code to new testcase keyword. Sorry for the spam!",
            "creator": "ekrock@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-21T21:48:02Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "mine! mine mine mine!  all mine!  whoo-hoo!",
            "creator": "buster@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-03-04T00:05:25Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Display:marker/run-in/compact are not supported. Closed as Later like bug 2056 \nand bug 14983.\n\nThe parser drops any declaration that contains one of these display types (see \nbug 15432).\n",
            "creator": "pierre@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-03-23T14:51:37Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Does not supporting DL COMPACT mean Mozilla will not have 100% HTML 4.0 \ncompliance for final release? If so, should that be on the release notes (relnote \nkeyword)?\n",
            "creator": "mpt@postinbox.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-03-24T13:29:02Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "mpt: You are correct. BTW, you can see the list of HTML4 features which we will \nNOT be implementing by looking at the bugs blocking 7954 that are marked LATER.\n",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "2000-03-29T15:28:36Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Not supporting this does *NOT* imply noncompliance with HTML 4.0.  HTML 4.0\nneither describes the expected rendering nor requires that the rendering be\ndifferent.  The most it says about the attribute is:\n\n  When set, this boolean attribute gives a hint to visual user agents to render\n  the list in a more compact way.\n  (from http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40/struct/lists.html#h-10.2 )\n",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-02T20:37:32Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Verified LATER",
            "creator": "christinehoff4@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-24T18:26:46Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Reopening and moving to Future...",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "2000-06-07T17:19:52Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 50195 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-24T21:44:29Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Matty: Why do you think this is a mozilla0.9 blocker?\n\nThis is a CSS2 RFE, I wouldn't even put it down as a mozilla 1.0 blocker.",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "2001-02-09T23:59:22Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Probably the \"correctness\" and \"relnote\" keywords, but perhaps I was a little\ntrigger-happy.\n\nI'll respect whatever opinion you have, but I think it should probably be\nnominated for 1.1 or 1.2 at least.",
            "creator": "matty_is_a_geek@fastmail.fm",
            "timestamp": "2001-02-10T04:49:55Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "A CSS2 RFE? Um, it's expected behavior (regardless of what is *required* \nbehavior) for HTML 2.0 (regardless of whether or not an HTML 2.0 rendering engine \nuses CSS to present HTML at all).\n",
            "creator": "mpt@postinbox.com",
            "timestamp": "2001-02-10T19:22:16Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Nominating for nsbeta1 consideration because you do encounter pages from time \nto time that depend on this behavior and look strange (text lines spaced out \nwidely) because it's not supported. However, if Netscape engineering runs out \nof time before nsbeta1, this would be a good one to FUTURE.",
            "creator": "ekrock@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2001-02-24T02:11:08Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Nominating this bug for nsbeta1 on behalf of gerardok@netscape.com.",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "2001-04-27T00:07:48Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Build reassigning Buster's bugs to Marc.",
            "creator": "kmcclusk@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2001-10-04T23:28:18Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "the compact attribute has been deprecated since HTML 4.0 and is obsoleted in \nXHTML.\n\nthis should be a wontfix",
            "creator": "rubydoo123@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "2001-11-21T00:24:31Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "    Personally, I don't agree with the WONTFIX. If there was any other practical\nway to do the same kind of formating as <DL COMPACT>, that would be OK, but\nthere is just no way to do it. The HTML I \"write\" is very basic designed for\n*any* browser, including Lynx, so I don't want any XHTML or CSS solution.\n\n    Let's take a concrete example : I've got a few papers on my web page, and at\nthe end of the paper I've got a list of references :\nhttp://www.hpl.hp.com/personal/Jean_Tourrilhes/Papers/Packet.Frame.Grouping.html#References\n    <Comments on my buggy HTML for another day please>\n    The formating that I want is something like :\n-------------------------------------\n[1]     IEEE 802.11 : Wireless LAN medium access control (MAC) and physical\nlayer (PHY) specifications. IEEE.\n-------------------------------------\n    There is no notion of <TAB> or <OL> with customised headings, so I do :\n---------------------\n<dl COMPACT>\n<dt>[1]\n<dd><i>IEEE 802.11&nbsp;: Wireless LAN medium access control (MAC) and\nphysical layer (PHY) specifications</i>. IEEE.\n---------------------\n    Which is to me both logically and esthetically pleasing. Logically, because\nit's a list of attibute/value pairs, which is exactly what <DL> is supposed to\nmean. Esthetically because it display like a <OL> list.\n    All browser I tested support this the way it should be, except of course\nMozilla that break it in two lines (ugly).\n    Now, I'm pretty ignorant about HTML and all the jazz, but if you find me a\nsolution that would produce the same effect a <DL COMPACT> and works in all\nbrowsers, I'm with you. Otherwise, I just have to disagree...\n    FUTURE is ok with me, it doesn't have to be fix *right now*, it can wait 1.1\nor later, but I just disagree in you saying it's not worth fixing (and that's\nwhy I voted for this bug).\n    <By the way, what's involved in fixing that ? It seems that both front-end\nand back-end for it are already implemented ?>\n    Jean",
            "creator": "jt@hpl.hp.com",
            "timestamp": "2001-11-21T00:59:57Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Sorry, I thought I had explained that I marked this as wontfix based on the \ndeprecation of this attribute in HTML 4.0 Spec and the obsoletion of the \nattribute in the XHTML Spec. I guess we could reopen, keep in future and mark it \nas a quirks only issue. ",
            "creator": "rubydoo123@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "2001-11-21T01:45:50Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 111936 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "timeless@bemail.org",
            "timestamp": "2001-11-26T16:09:22Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "ok",
            "creator": "timeless@bemail.org",
            "timestamp": "2001-11-26T16:10:10Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Please don't make quirks mode and standards mode diverge any more.  Standards\nmode should follow the standards -- and implementing deprecated features is\ncertainly within the standards.  Quirks mode should only differ from standards\nmode when we *need* to break standard behavior in order to get real pages on the\nweb to display correctly.\n\nHaving said that, I think wontfix is an appropriate resolution here since we've\nremoved our support for 'display: compact' and since compact DLs aren't used on\nthe web and are deprecated.  When i initially filed this bug it would have taken\na single rule in ua.css to fix this bug.",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2001-11-26T17:36:21Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I'm with David on this one, reclosing as wontfix",
            "creator": "rubydoo123@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "2001-11-26T18:58:14Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 133022 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "caillon@redhat.com",
            "timestamp": "2002-03-23T23:24:16Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "VERIFIED that we have decided not to support HTML 3.2's \"compact\" attribute on\nDL elements.",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "2002-03-23T23:36:44Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "<DL COMPACT> is deprecated, but not obsolete in HTML 4.01.\nDeprecated attributes should still be rendered in browsers for backward \ncompatibility.\n\nIs there a way to specify compact rendering of DL in style-sheets?\nI fear not!  One more reason to still support <DL COMPACT>.\n\nAaron Swarz (comment #7) is wrong by supposing COMPACT an attribute of OL \ninstead of DL\n\nI agree with jt@hpl.hp.com (comment #27) that this bug should NOT be a WONTFIX \nas COMPACT DL helps a lot when dealing with lists - I too use(d) this attribute \na lot.\n\nI disagree with David Baron (comment #31) believing compact DLs aren't used on \nthe web.  I even hope, compact DL will be put back in the standard and be used \n*more*, instead of the widespread use to put cumbersome nested tables everywhere \nto control layout...\n",
            "creator": "markus@dnet.it",
            "timestamp": "2002-03-24T15:29:00Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 133022 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "bzbarsky@mit.edu",
            "timestamp": "2002-04-14T04:00:49Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "beppe@netscape.com wrote \"I marked this as wontfix based on the \ndeprecation of this attribute in HTML 4.0 Spec and the obsoletion of the \nattribute in the XHTML Spec\".\n\nOn the other hand Netscape's developer release notes\n<URL:http://developer.netscape.com/docs/technote/gecko/n6release.html> classify\nthis bug as a CSS2 issue.\n\nThis thread has gotten very muddled and has over time raised issues from child\nselectors to support of \"display: compact\" to support of the\n(deprecated/obsolete) compact attribute. There should really be separate bugs to\ntrack these separate issues.  The last few comments as well as most (all?) of\nthe duplicate bug reports are about the compact attribute, so I think the\nfollowing actions should be taken:\n\n- Create a new bug report to track work on a future \"display: compact\"\nenhancement (I don't see an existing specific bug report for this purpose).\n\n- Make it clear that this bug is now only for the compact attribute. And remove\ncss2 from the keywords if that is possible.",
            "creator": "ccwf+bugzilla@web-i18n.net",
            "timestamp": "2002-05-26T21:47:44Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "bug 180468 is the inline: compact not implemented css2 bug.",
            "creator": "helgedt@tihlde.org",
            "timestamp": "2003-01-28T02:49:46Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 203489 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "choess@stwing.upenn.edu",
            "timestamp": "2003-04-26T19:50:57Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 234027 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "bugzilla@accessibleinter.net",
            "timestamp": "2004-02-12T16:28:30Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This bug should really be reopened, as it is not only an HTML bug, but also a\nCSS2 bug. As a deprecated HTML feature, Mozilla could drop support for the <dl\ncompact> form, but if the {display: compact} support is not achieved, Mozilla\nwill never be  able to claim CSS2 compliance (nearly six years after, now...).",
            "creator": "pierre.thierry@moine-fou.org",
            "timestamp": "2004-02-17T22:03:39Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "'display:compact' should be a separate bug.",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "2004-02-17T22:07:05Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "And it is - bug 180468\n",
            "creator": "t8m@centrum.cz",
            "timestamp": "2004-02-18T07:50:22Z"
        }
    ]
}

{
    "bug_id": 10756,
    "summary": "logging every selection doesn't allow for property changes",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "When logging, you can't replay the commands to change the style since they are\nlost when the selection is reset.\n\nFor example, in an empty document log the following steps:\n * type:  abc\n * click the bold icon\n * type:  def\n\nNotice that in the log, the selection is set between each keystroke and command.\nThis means that setting bold won't work since the editor thinks that the\nselection has changed (so the bold command is ignored).",
            "creator": "brade@comcast.net",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-29T17:20:49Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Accepting bug, setting milestone to M11.\n\nJust wanted to note that you can replay style changes that are applied to\nselected (hilighted) content. This bug happens when trying to apply a style when\nthe selection is a caret.",
            "creator": "kinmoz@netscape.net",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-29T17:27:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "By the way, the temporary workaround for this is to edit the journal.js file and\ncomment out the calls to EditorSetSelectionFromOffset() before every call to\nSetTextProperty.",
            "creator": "kinmoz@netscape.net",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-29T17:28:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Oops, screwed up on the workaround description above.\n\nComment out the call to EditorSetSelectionFromOffset() AFTER the call to\nwindow.editorShell.SetTextProperty(), ONLY if the selection offsets for the\nSetTextProperty() call match the selection offsets after it.",
            "creator": "kinmoz@netscape.net",
            "timestamp": "1999-07-29T17:35:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Moving some SpellChecker/TextServices feature requests and bugs, that can wait\ntill after beta 1, to milestone M14.",
            "creator": "kinmoz@netscape.net",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-09T17:02:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Moved to M15 to balance bug counts across milestones.",
            "creator": "kinmoz@netscape.net",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-20T22:26:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Moving all non-beta1 bugs to M16 since I am going on sabbatical.\n",
            "creator": "kinmoz@netscape.net",
            "timestamp": "2000-03-03T22:48:18Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "moving to m17",
            "creator": "rubydoo123@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-05-04T22:13:13Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Move to M19.",
            "creator": "kinmoz@netscape.net",
            "timestamp": "2000-07-17T20:29:29Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "setting to future, although this was a great tool for QA to use for debugging\n",
            "creator": "rubydoo123@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-07-19T17:14:39Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "adding help wanted keyword",
            "creator": "rubydoo123@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-07-27T21:16:57Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Bulk-downgrade of unassigned, untouched DOM/Storage bug's priority.\n\nIf you have reason to believe, this is wrong, please write a comment and ni :jstutte.",
            "creator": "jstutte@mozilla.com",
            "timestamp": "2020-12-14T15:19:36Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Pushed by ctuns@mozilla.com:\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/19c768547c7c\n[fenix] For https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/issues/10756 -  UI intermittent media playback failures (https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/pull/10775)",
            "creator": "pulsebot@bmo.tld",
