{
    "bug_id": 11557,
    "summary": "nsIFileSpec.idl should forward declare nsFileSpec",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "Currently, it explicitly includes \"nsFileSpec.h\" which brings in a lot of extra\n#includes for everybody, namely nsString.h, and friends. This causes lots of\nsource files to implicitly get nsString, nsCRT, etc.\n\nIn my tree, I've experimented with this and have had to touch the following list\nof files to get them to correctly, explicitly #include nsString.h and nsCRT.h:\n\nmozilla/mailnews/mime/emitters/src/nsEmitterUtils.cpp\nmozilla/mailnews/imap/src/nsImapStringBundle.cpp\nmozilla/mailnews/addrbook/src/nsCardDataSource.cpp\nmozilla/xpfe/components/history/src/nsGlobalHistory.cpp\nmozilla/layout/base/src/nsPresContext.cpp\nmozilla/xpcom/components/xcDll.cpp\nmozilla/netwerk/protocol/http/src/nsHTTPHandler.cpp\nmozilla/mailnews/mime/emitters/src/nsMimeXmlEmitter.cpp\nmozilla/mailnews/mime/emitters/src/nsMimeHtmlEmitter.cpp\nmozilla/mailnews/compose/src/nsMsgComposeStringBundle.cpp\nmozilla/netwerk/base/src/nsLoadGroup.cpp\nmozilla/modules/libimg/src/if.cpp\nmozilla/netwerk/protocol/about/src/nsAboutProtocolHandler.cpp",
            "creator": "beard@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-10T20:27:28Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Do you want to check these changes in?",
            "creator": "doug.turner@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-10T22:46:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I have been propagating them forward but keep getting conflicts, so I filed this\nbug to notify you of the problem. And there hasn't been a good time to check them\nin. They're easy to find, just make the change to nsIFileSpec.idl, and things\nwill start to break, usually because they need either nsString.h or nsCRT.h.",
            "creator": "beard@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-10T22:54:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "risky change before m9 tree closure.  Setting target milestone to m10.",
            "creator": "doug.turner@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-10T23:09:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "moving to m11.",
            "creator": "doug.turner@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-01T20:16:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "moving to m11.",
            "creator": "doug.turner@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-01T20:17:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "moving after beta.",
            "creator": "doug.turner@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-14T21:48:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "will be fixed by 22047",
            "creator": "doug.turner@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-17T19:14:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "users should not be using nsFileSpec any longer.",
            "creator": "doug.turner@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-01-25T18:08:44Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "nsfilespec is dead.  ",
            "creator": "doug.turner@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-07-27T02:00:14Z"
        }
    ]
}

{
    "bug_id": 12230,
    "summary": "In OPTGROUPs, fonts don't match when list dropped down",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "Build ID: 1999082008\nPlatform: Windows NT (can't test on Mac OS yet)\n\nTo reproduce:\n- Launch apprunner\n- Load the above URL (Netscape internal only) or attached test case\n- Click on the down arrow to drop down the list\n\nResult: Although 12 point Times New Roman is used for items on the list, 10\npoint Arial is used for the currently selected option drawn above the top of the\nlist.\n\nExpected result: The same font should be used if at all possible.",
            "creator": "cpratt@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-20T19:31:17Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Reassigning to Rod.",
            "creator": "karnaze@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-20T20:58:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Fixed.",
            "creator": "rods@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-31T14:23:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "apres moi, la deluge. (merci)",
            "creator": "phillip@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-16T00:05:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Reopening and clearing resolution. Currently, we have:\n\nArial 10 pt - used when optionlist menu is not displayed\nTimes 12 pt bold italic - used for group headings\nArial 10 pt - used for selectable items in list\n\nIs there a spec for this? I'm guessing that using Arial 10 pt for everything\n*but* group headings is correct, but what to use for the group headings? I think\nArial 11 pt bold italic is where it's at, but I'm not part of the UI/UE team.\nGerman? Shuang?",
            "creator": "cpratt@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-16T00:13:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 1686\nRTF file with a rough estimate of what this should look like",
            "creator": "cpratt@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-16T00:15:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Changing priority and severity (this is absolutely NOT something we need to look\nat for beta!)...",
            "creator": "cpratt@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-16T00:29:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Fix in my tree",
            "creator": "rods@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-30T18:13:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "They now have the same font - fixed",
            "creator": "rods@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-11T23:54:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Using the 1999101109 build under NT, the problem doesn't appear to be fixed. Is\nthis fixed in a later build or something? To verify the fix, download the\nattachment and rename it 'foo.rtf'; open in Word, and compare it with the\noptgroup generated by Mozilla. They don't currently match (you can see this as\nthe category headers have serifs, but the actual selectable items do not; try\ncomparing the 'a' in China with the 'a' in Yunnan).",
            "creator": "cpratt@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-12T00:00:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Perfect! 1999101908 build, NT.",
            "creator": "cpratt@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-19T21:43:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Pushed by ctuns@mozilla.com:\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/a5a851cd7088\n[components] Issue https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/android-components/issues/12230: Speculative fix for test failures in PromptFeatureTest",
            "creator": "pulsebot@bmo.tld",
            "timestamp": "2024-03-18T18:06:04Z"
        }
    ]
}

{
    "bug_id": 12699,
    "summary": "[meta] Good Netkeeping Seal of Approval (GNKSA newsreader standard)",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "This is a meta bug to track the places where mozilla needs to improve to meet\nthe Good Netkeeping Seal of Approval",
            "creator": "phil@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-27T22:47:04Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Added GNSKA url",
            "creator": "sfraser_bugs@smfr.org",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-27T23:37:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Phil found a way to weasel out of owning this bug.  Reassigning.\n",
            "creator": "selmer@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-02T06:51:23Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "One moment, fixing dependencies ... (Bugzilla won't let me do this in one step)\n",
            "creator": "mpt@postinbox.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-05T05:35:49Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "... there we go. Much better.\n",
            "creator": "mpt@postinbox.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-05T05:36:34Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "4.5 evaluation:\n<http://www.xs4all.nl/~js/gnksa/Evaluations/netscape-communicator-4.5.txt>",
            "creator": "ben.bucksch@beonex.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-08T10:55:31Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Is the score identical for both 4.5 and Seamonkey??\n\nIs anyone willing to help fix some of these dependent bugs?\n",
            "creator": "selmer@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-08T14:07:00Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Steve, I'm sure, it's not identical, but I guess, the evaluation will look\nsimilar - some problems fixed, but some new problems :-(.\n\nMaybe, it would be good to do a \"preview evaluation\" by ourseves (i.e. look over\nthe requirements to see, if we fail in new places), if we care. Maybe I'll do it\nsome time, when I'm in the right mood.\n\nI'm working on 35158 (fixed in my tree) and 9202 (mostly fixed in my tree) and\nindirectly on 6276.",
            "creator": "ben.bucksch@beonex.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-08T16:51:00Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "> Maybe, it would be good to do a \"preview evaluation\" by ourseves\n\nI just noticed, John did the 4.5 evaluation. He would propably the right guy to\ndo it, then.",
            "creator": "ben.bucksch@beonex.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-19T00:07:42Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I'll do a full evaluation latter, but for now...\n\n\n\nFollowup-To and Reply-To no longer shown by default.\n\nFollowup-To: poster -- is addressed to the \"newsgroup\" poster.\n\nWhen I changed that to the newsgroup I was using for testing,\n\nand posted the message, the content-type said plain/text but\n\nthe body was HTML (this despite my having to answer a dialog\n\nasking if I wanted HTML).  More latter\n\n",
            "creator": "John.planb@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-19T17:09:42Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Ok, finished enough for the moment.  I haven't submitted it, but\nI've put it up at: <http://www.newsreaders.com/john/m15.html> for\nthe moment.\n\nSome points -- there isn't a command for Reply Via Email, so I've\nfailed it on 8a and 8b.   I didn't test it for server load, it was so slow\nI doubt if I could have got it to even attempt a second action before it\ncompleted the last.",
            "creator": "John.planb@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-04-21T04:35:07Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Nomination for mozilla 1.0.",
            "creator": "ben.bucksch@beonex.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-10-12T02:52:58Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Did someone just change this to \"fixed\"?  If so why?\n",
            "creator": "John.planb@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2001-03-24T04:20:34Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "> Did someone just change this to \"fixed\"?  If so why?\n\nNo, a depending bug (#71121) was changed to 'fixed'. You can turn of e-mail \nnotification of related (depending/blocking) bugs onthe BugZilla e-mail \npreferences page.",
            "creator": "karl@huftis.org",
            "timestamp": "2001-03-24T11:44:56Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "John Moreno's evaluation is no longer available on newsreaders.com, AFAICT.",
            "creator": "gwalla@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2001-04-23T20:32:29Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I assume you mean my  unfinished evaluation of m15 at, \n<http://www.newsreaders.com/john/m15.html>, I changed the directory \nname and didn't provide any links.  Sorry about that, I've fixed it.\n\nBut it's way out of date, and according to the docs my computer is no \nlonger supported (not too surprising given the speed when I did the \nevaluation).  And at least some of the failures in that version have been \nfixed in later versions.",
            "creator": "John.planb@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2001-04-23T22:13:12Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Should bug #95623 take the place of #17796 in this bug's dependency list? 17796 \nis listed as blocking only because it could be used to fulfill the GNKSA \nsection 2 requirements. The subject of 17796 (dual menubuttons for replying, \nforwarding etc.) is not itself a GNKSA issue.",
            "creator": "gwalla@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2001-08-16T18:58:00Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This bug is not OS dependend. Please someone set OS=ALL\n\nAdding bug 37088 (Trailing whitespace when folding QP encoded headers) to\ndependency, this one is for GNKSA requirement 5 b) (Preserves entire original\nSubject), adding additional white space destroys the original Subject.\n\npi",
            "creator": "3.14@piology.org",
            "timestamp": "2002-01-29T12:34:27Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Scott, over to you for safe keeping :-)",
            "creator": "selmer@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2002-01-30T08:21:24Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Hows about adding the 'meta' keyword and setting target milestone to Mozilla 1.0 ?\nAlso, should this be nsDogFood or nsCatFood ?",
            "creator": "vhaarr+bmo@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2002-02-20T08:06:01Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "unfortunately, the chance that this will get in before 1.0 is next to 0. Today\nis feature deadline, I think.",
            "creator": "ben.bucksch@beonex.com",
            "timestamp": "2002-02-20T08:18:46Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Requirement 13a): Cancel -- Adding bug 150036.\n\npi",
            "creator": "3.14@piology.org",
            "timestamp": "2002-08-09T15:00:43Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Removing dupes:\nBug 4567 is a dupe of bug 73403 which is already in the list.\nBug 17124 is a dupe of bug 13767 which is fixed (so I don't add it).\nBug 34549 is a dupe of bug 6276 which is already in the list.\n\nShould we also remove other resolved bugs?\n\npi",
            "creator": "3.14@piology.org",
            "timestamp": "2002-09-19T08:21:53Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I discussed with Jonas that it would be better to have the dependencies for this\nbug an bug 76449 (Must-fix GNKSA bugs) non-overlapping. This will enhance the\noverview. Changing summary etc. to make this clear. Of course, bug 76449 blocks\nthis here.\n\nRemoving bugs listed in bug 76449:\nBug 3744, bug 3745, bug 3746, bug 17796, bug 35338, bug 66150, bug 95623, bug 169614\n\npi",
            "creator": "3.14@piology.org",
            "timestamp": "2002-09-19T09:13:54Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "reassigning to sspitzer",
            "creator": "scottputterman@gmail.com",
