        }
    ]
}

{
    "bug_id": 12752,
    "summary": "very large font sizes display as 1px text",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "The attached testcase shows that when font-size is specified to be ten million\npixels, Mozilla just displays garbage.\n\n(I think the text should be either displayed at the largest possible size, or\nnot at all. IE displays the text at an illegible 1 pixel height.)",
            "creator": "allen.sam@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-29T03:23:38Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 1445\ntestcase -- font-size:10000000px",
            "creator": "allen.sam@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-08-29T03:24:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This isn't my call. Most likely a style bug.",
            "creator": "beard@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-01T05:05:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Moving non-beta 1 items to M15",
            "creator": "peterl-retired@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-08T00:59:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Reassigning peterl's bugs to myself.",
            "creator": "pierre@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-21T08:06:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Accepting peterl's bugs that have a Target Milestone",
            "creator": "pierre@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-21T08:12:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 3578\nMega wide table width=32760",
            "creator": "extremely@hostile.org",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-17T18:03:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "When looking at this, The bug causes the background to render as junk. The\nwindow scrollbars properly size and when scrolling you can see the properly\nrendered gigantic font.  For a different font the minimum px number that\ncauses the bug is different. For the default font in windows I got it at 11345px\nand for Comic Sans MS it was between 9000 and 9500.\n\nIt would seem that the background is improperly \"prerendered\" when the WIDTH of\nthe window exceeds 32000 ish pixels.\n\nSee the attached table set to 32760 width attachment to get the same bug.\nThis isn't a style bug.",
            "creator": "extremely@hostile.org",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-17T18:05:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I tested on WinNT but I can't see the problems as described. The 10Mpx characters\nare drawn with a 1 pixel height (like IE - maybe it's an OS thing) and I can't\nsee any garbled background with the second testcase.\n\nI don't understand why you mentioned a \"gigantic font\" for the second testcase\nbecause it doesn't contain any font tag.\n\nClosing as WontFix anyhow: a 10Mpx font size is too unrealistic to spend some\ntime on it.",
            "creator": "pierre@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-18T05:20:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I can see garbled backgrounds on both the testcases mentioned in this bug, but\nonly on a resize of the viewport.\n\nI concede that this is not a high-priority task. It is, however, something that\nshould be fixed eventually. I would like to see it upgraded to 'later'.",
            "creator": "allen.sam@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-18T05:55:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Will do.\n\nChris, could you check that bug on different Windows flavors (95/98/NT)? We\nalready fixed problems due to the 32k pixels limit on some OSes (can't remember\nwhich).",
            "creator": "pierre@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-18T06:42:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Changed the resolution to Remind.",
            "creator": "pierre@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-12-18T06:43:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Netscape's standard compliance QA team reorganised itself once again, so taking \nremaining non-tables style bugs. Sorry about the spam. I tried to get this done \ndirectly at the database level, but apparently that is \"not easy because of the \nshadow db\", \"plus it screws up the audit trail\", so no can do...",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "2001-02-13T00:24:30Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "REMIND is deprecated. Reopening and moving to Future.",
            "creator": "ian@hixie.ch",
            "timestamp": "2001-06-14T03:27:48Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Both the problems seem fixed, probably thanks to ViewMgr 2.\n",
            "creator": "pierre@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2001-07-17T18:34:36Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "hey.... in win2k .... 2002-10-14-08trunk build .... the testcase attachment 1445\nstill shows the text displayed in an illegible 1 pixel height.  Is this a\npossible regression ?\n",
            "creator": "madhur@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2002-10-14T20:05:36Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Pushed by ctuns@mozilla.com:\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/707e2929b053\n[fenix] Fixes https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/issues/12752, https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/issues/12764 - Temp disable openHistoryInNewTabTest intermittent UI test failures (https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/pull/12754)\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/9bdc4edde8a5\n[fenix] Fix UI tests from https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/issues/12752 https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/issues/12637 https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/issues/12764 (https://github.com/mozilla-mobile/fenix/pull/12779)",
            "creator": "pulsebot@bmo.tld",
            "timestamp": "2024-03-18T18:29:37Z"
        }
    ]
}

{
    "bug_id": 13093,
    "summary": "Don't change cursor or do mouseovers during selection",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "During selection of some text if you move the mouse over a hyperlink the cursor\nchanges from the I-beam to the pointing-hand.   Instead, it should always stay\nas an I-beam.",
            "creator": "michael.j.lowe@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-03T17:32:49Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Confirmed that this is a cross-platform issue, and also present on Mac OS &\nLinux; adjusted platforms correspondingly. Thanks, Michael!",
            "creator": "elig@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-03T20:48:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I also noticed that the cursor currently changes to a normal pointer when it is\nnot over any text.   I think what should happen is that once the mouse is down\nthe cursor changes to an I-beam and stays that way no matter what it is over\nuntil the mouse is back up again.",
            "creator": "michael.j.lowe@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-03T21:15:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Agreed 100%; that's probably a side-effect of the fact that selection currently\ndoesn't work in dead spaces (without text).",
            "creator": "elig@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-03T21:41:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "another bounced to the manske man.",
            "creator": "mjudge@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-15T00:09:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** This bug has been marked as a duplicate of 10236 ***",
            "creator": "cmanske@jivamedia.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-15T17:34:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Is this really a duplicate?   bug 10236 deals only with the cursor over\nhyperlinks in the editor.  This bug deals with the cursor while selecting text\nin the browser or the editor, which seems a different problem.   Also read\ncomment from [09/03/99 14:15]",
            "creator": "michael.j.lowe@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-15T21:33:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "It doesn't matter if you are in the act of selecting or not. The cursor is\ncontrolled by CSS in both cases. So bug 10236, which is fixed, covers the\neditor case, which should never use the \"pointer\" hand cursor.\nSo if you don't want the pointer when selecting in the browser, that is a\ndifferent bug. I don't think CSS can respond differently during selecting,\ni.e., when the mouse is being dragged.\nPeter: Is that possible?",
            "creator": "cmanske@jivamedia.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-16T23:44:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "No, CSS has no notion of \"dragging\" state to select against. This seems like the\ncode looking for different cursors should just not do anything during a drag\nselect... (all in event state manager?)",
            "creator": "peterl-retired@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-17T00:52:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "So it seems the selection code will have to communicate with the style system\nto control this and the related problem in bug 12523, where the cursor is\nchanging to inappropriate types and cannot be defeated with CSS settings.\nSorry, Mike, but these problems will have to be solved in the selection/pres.\nshell code, not in our CSS files.",
            "creator": "cmanske@jivamedia.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-17T18:54:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "still happening in 9/17 build....Charley wanted me to verify if its working...",
            "creator": "sujay@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-17T21:54:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "One more related bug.   During selection, when the mouse is over a button or\nanything else where the hover style is set, the hover style should not be\npainted in this case.",
            "creator": "michael.j.lowe@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-24T17:20:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I added \"in browser\" to summary to remind us that this is not a problem in\nthe editor because we override the \"pointer\" cursor over links.",
            "creator": "cmanske@jivamedia.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-24T18:30:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Another related bug.   During selection, when the mouse is over something where\nJavaScript on-mouse-over or similar event handlers have been set, the JavaScript\nhandlers should not be called.",
            "creator": "michael.j.lowe@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-24T20:03:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Actually, this is a problem in both the editor and browser.   In the editor,\nthis has been fixed for links, but it is still a problem in whitespace\n(areas containing no text) where the cursor changes back to an arrow during\nselection.   Other parts of this bug such as diabling hover style and JavaScript\nevents also apply.",
            "creator": "michael.j.lowe@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-24T20:24:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This bug is closely related to bug 15030 and vice versa.",
            "creator": "michael.j.lowe@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-09-27T23:47:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "changing status to assigned, keeping this at m15, it can wiat till after beta\npush",
            "creator": "rubydoo123@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "1999-10-14T21:52:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 15030 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "brade@comcast.net",
            "timestamp": "2000-03-06T20:30:07Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "[Note to self: please verify 15030 when verifying this bug.]\n",
            "creator": "elig@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-03-06T21:01:04Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "moving to M17",
            "creator": "rubydoo123@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-05-08T22:41:14Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "per beppe moving to polish",
            "creator": "mjudge@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-07-26T00:26:15Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 27318 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "mjudge@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-07-26T01:26:46Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*** Bug 38796 has been marked as a duplicate of this bug. ***",
            "creator": "mjudge@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "2000-07-26T03:21:47Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "moving this to future and adding helpwanted keyword",
            "creator": "rubydoo123@aol.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-08T23:38:19Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "*SPAM*: Changing the QA contact of all open/resolved Selection bugs from \nelig@netscape.com to BlakeR1234@aol.com.  After the many great years of service \nEli has given to Mozilla, it's time for him to move on; he has accepted a \nposition at Eazel.  We'll be sad to see him go, and I'll do my best to fill his \nspot...",
            "creator": "bugzilla@blakeross.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-08-14T23:50:52Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "[Resummarizing]\n",
            "creator": "mpt@postinbox.com",
            "timestamp": "2000-11-26T11:05:17Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "changing selection qa to tpreston.",
            "creator": "bugzilla@blakeross.com",
            "timestamp": "2002-02-16T21:12:48Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "It seems to me that the cursor should become an arrow to indicate that the\nselection is draggable (you can drag/copy/paste).  However, if you do\n:-moz-selection { cursor: normal } selection becomes utterly impossible, so this\nrule is hard to enforce.",
            "creator": "john@johnkeiser.com",
            "timestamp": "2002-12-05T03:18:30Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "still happening in build:\nMozilla/5.0 (X11; U; Linux i586; en-US; rv:1.5) Gecko/20030925\n",
            "creator": "waazup@hotmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2003-11-10T06:35:37Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "the ::-moz-selection { cursor: something; }  bug is really the issue found in\nBug 231894, which has a patch (by me) pending review.",
            "creator": "bugspam.Callek@gmail.com",
            "timestamp": "2004-10-19T06:11:48Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Bulk-downgrade of unassigned, >=5 years untouched DOM/Storage bugs' priority and severity.\n\nIf you have reason to believe this is wrong, please write a comment and ni :jstutte.",
            "creator": "jstutte@mozilla.com",
            "timestamp": "2020-12-15T07:16:10Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "This seems can be fixed by adding some checks to `nsTextFrame::GetCursor` to \nsee `if (GetFrameSelection()->GetDragState() && GetContent()->AsElement()->IsLink() && (PreviousCursorIsText || PreviousCursorIsVerticalText) && NoUserProvidedStyleForLink) { return PreviousCursor; }`\n\nWDYT Emilio?",
            "creator": "sefeng@mozilla.com",
            "timestamp": "2023-04-07T00:45:02Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "`GetContent()->AsElement()->IsLink()` would trivially crash because the content of text frames is a text node, but something along those lines might make sense. Couple notes:\n\n * I don't think we want to look at the previous cursor, as it can be basically anything right? Plus even if you're not dragging the text cursor is an I-beam so...\n * Is `GetDragState` enough / the right thing, so that it doesn't change the cursor on link dragging?\n * We probably want to also do it if the cursor is `pointer` more generally, as it'd be weird that doing `:link { cursor: pointer }` would break this.\n\nChrome handles it [here](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/refs/heads/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/input/event_handler.cc;l=672;drc=3c99f1f962379a8a7ea0fd338cc0d60d0ab80441) fwiw.",
            "creator": "emilio@crisal.io",
            "timestamp": "2023-04-10T13:46:49Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Created attachment 9327807\nBug 13093 - Don't change cursor when mouseover links during selection r=emilio",
            "creator": "sefeng@mozilla.com",
            "timestamp": "2023-04-10T18:10:24Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Pushed by sefeng@mozilla.com:\nhttps://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/5c9aa60ea6f4\nDon't change cursor when mouseover links during selection r=emilio",
            "creator": "pulsebot@bmo.tld",
            "timestamp": "2023-04-13T11:48:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "https://hg.mozilla.org/mozilla-central/rev/5c9aa60ea6f4",
            "creator": "aryx.bugmail@gmx-topmail.de",
            "timestamp": "2023-04-14T09:52:49Z"
        }
    ]
}

{
    "bug_id": 13827,
    "summary": "vertical alignment and floaters don't mix well",
    "comments": [
        {
            "text": "Imagine a line that intersects a floater. Now imagine a tall image on that line\nthat causes most of the content to drop below the floater. The result in gecko\ntoday will be that the line will break too soon because the height of the image\nisn't known ahead of time and therefore the available space ins't quite right.",
