        {
            "text": "DESCRIPTION:  The page http://ww2010.atmos.uiuc.edu/(Gl)/wx/satellite.rxml has\nlinked pages that are complex JavaScript weather image viewers (allows browsing\narchives, animating, etc.).  Right now they're not working, and there are some\nother problems.\n\nI'm filing this bug and assigning it to myself to figure out what's wrong here,\nand I'll file (or find) specific bugs as needed and mark them as dependencies.\n\nDOES NOT WORK CORRECTLY ON:\n * Linux, apprunner, 1999-11-08-08-M11\n\nWORKS CORRECTLY ON:\n * Linux NN 4.61",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "1999-11-09T01:13:28Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "It turns out there's a Java applet in the page, so it shouldn't work\ncompletely.  However, there are three existing bugs I've already filed on the\npage (marked as dependencies).\n\nIf I get the external Java runtime working, then maybe I can test more.  (Should\nsuch things work yet?)  The page uses some JS/Java interaction.\n\nThere's also a potential layout compatibility issue on all the subpages.  There\nare scrollbars on the bottom frame that don't appear in other browsers.  It has\nto do with a 55px table in a 55px frame (height).  There's some occurrence of\nbug 5821 inside the table (because of whitespace, that should be eliminated by\nthe fix for bug 5821, I think), but that's not the real problem.  The real\nproblem either has to do with compatibility about body margins when the only\nchild is a table or about frame attributes such as scrolling=no.  I may\ninvestigate further...",
            "creator": "dbaron@dbaron.org",
            "timestamp": "1999-11-09T03:00:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "I believe the JS/Java interaction should work if you have the Java plugin\ncorrectly installed.",
            "creator": "vidur@formerly-netscape.com.tld",
            "timestamp": "1999-11-11T19:18:59Z"
        },
        {
            "text": "Are there still problems with this site?  All of the dependencies have been\nfixed, and it seems to be working for me.\n\nA newer version of the given URL is\nhttp://ww2010.atmos.uiuc.edu/(Gh)/wx/satellite.rxml though a lot of the same\ncode is being executed.",
